    "role": "user",
    "content": "{\"schema_version\":\"optomind.writing_evidence.payload.v1\",\"book_sha256\":\"3662038f6f241a48979bc8f9e30c8382776def734fcaa4cdddb82858d6cb6322\",\"language\":\"zh\",\"research_question\":\"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\",\"review_argument\":\"肠道微生物组通过分类学特征、代谢产物及免疫通路调节实体瘤患者对 ICI 的临床疗效，但证据强度因肿瘤类型、研究设计及干预策略而异。观察性关联证据在黑色素瘤中最强，NSCLC 和 RCC 次之，但关联不等于因果。机制证据主要来自动物模型，人类验证有限，特别是肿瘤微环境内代谢物浓度数据缺失（如肌苷仅有血浆数据）。干预策略在初治人群中显示希望（FMT-LUMINate ORR 75-80%），但在难治人群中效果有限（MITRIC ORR 0%），且安全性受 ICI 方案调节（Prevotella 相关心肌炎仅在双 ICI 背景下出现）。目前缺乏 Phase III RCT 证据支持微生物干预的常规临床应用，未来研究需解决标准化、因果推断及人群分层问题。\",\"user_request\":\"\",\"target_reader\":\"\",\"review_scope\":{\"statement\":\"本综述聚焦于实体瘤（黑色素瘤、非小细胞肺癌、肾细胞癌、结直肠癌等）患者接受免疫检查点抑制剂（PD-1/PD-L1、CTLA-4 抑制剂）治疗期间，肠道微生物组对治疗疗效（ORR、PFS、OS）及毒性（irAEs）的调节作用。涵盖观察性关联证据（区分回顾性与前瞻性队列）、因果机制解析（免疫细胞、分子通路、代谢物）、外部干扰因素（抗生素、PPI、饮食）及微生物干预策略（FMT、益生菌、工程菌）的临床试验数据。明确排除血液系统恶性肿瘤及非免疫治疗背景下的微生物组研究（除非用于机制对比）。严格区分肠道微生物组与肿瘤内微生物组的作用边界。证据等级标注明确：观察性关联不推断因果，干预试验区分 I/II 期与 III 期，代谢物数据区分血浆与肿瘤组织浓度。\"},\"missing_original_context_fields\":[\"user_request\",\"target_reader\"],\"editable_task_ids\":[\"Ch3::U3_1::U3_1_P01\",\"Ch3::U3_1::U3_1_P02\",\"Ch3::U3_1::U3_1_P03\",\"Ch3::U3_1::U3_1_P04\",\"Ch3::U3_2::U3_2_P01\",\"Ch3::U3_2::U3_2_P02\",\"Ch3::U3_2::U3_2_P03\",\"Ch3::U3_2::U3_2_P04\",\"Ch3::U3_3::U3_3_P01\",\"Ch3::U3_3::U3_3_P02\",\"Ch3::U3_3::U3_3_P03\",\"Ch3::U3_4::U3_4_P01\",\"Ch3::U3_4::U3_4_P02\",\"Ch3::U3_4::U3_4_P03\",\"Ch3::U3_5::U3_5_P01\",\"Ch3::U3_5::U3_5_P02\",\"Ch3::U3_5::U3_5_P03\"],\"tasks\":{\"Ch3::U3_1::U3_1_P01\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_1::U3_1_P01\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_1_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_1\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_1_P01\",\"point\":\"阐明 SCFAs（乙酸、丙酸、丁酸）通过 HDAC 抑制与 GPR41/43/GPR109A 受体调控免疫细胞代谢与分化的基础生化路径。\",\"development\":\"对比 SCFAs 在正常结肠上皮与肿瘤微环境中的代谢流向差异，建立表观遗传调控的理论框架。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"详述丁酸通过 HDAC 抑制上调 Pdcd1/Cd28 增强 CD8+ T 细胞记忆的分子基础\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"role\":\"背景\",\"use\":\"提供 CRC 背景下调节微生物群增强 ICI 疗效的机制分类框架\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_1_P01\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_1_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_1\",\"ordinal\":1,\"point\":\"阐明 SCFAs（乙酸、丙酸、丁酸）通过 HDAC 抑制与 GPR41/43/GPR109A 受体调控免疫细胞代谢与分化的基础生化路径。\",\"development\":\"对比 SCFAs 在正常结肠上皮与肿瘤微环境中的代谢流向差异，建立表观遗传调控的理论框架。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0515\",\"P0544\"]}]}},\"Ch3::U3_1::U3_1_P02\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_1::U3_1_P02\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_1_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_1\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_1_P02\",\"point\":\"呈现 SCFAs 在抗 PD-1 治疗中增强抗肿瘤免疫的临床与临床前证据。\",\"development\":\"结合 P0092 与 P0223 的队列数据，说明高粪便 SCFA 水平如何转化为更长的 PFS，并引用 P0515 解释其增强 CD8+ T 细胞杀伤的分子基础。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"提供粪便 SCFA 水平与抗 PD-1 疗效正相关的临床队列证据\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"补充实体瘤抗 PD-1 治疗中响应者 fSCFA 显著升高的表型数据\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"role\":\"背景\",\"use\":\"解释 SCFA 增强 CD8+ T 细胞杀伤的分子基础\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_1_P02\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_1_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_1\",\"ordinal\":2,\"point\":\"呈现 SCFAs 在抗 PD-1 治疗中增强抗肿瘤免疫的临床与临床前证据。\",\"development\":\"结合 P0092 与 P0223 的队列数据，说明高粪便 SCFA 水平如何转化为更长的 PFS，并引用 P0515 解释其增强 CD8+ T 细胞杀伤的分子基础。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0092\",\"P0223\",\"P0515\"]}]}},\"Ch3::U3_1::U3_1_P03\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_1::U3_1_P03\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_1_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_1\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_1_P03\",\"point\":\"揭示 SCFAs 在抗 CTLA-4 治疗中的负面或限制性作用。\",\"development\":\"基于 P0503 与 P0559 的数据，论证高血清丁酸/丙酸如何通过促进 Treg 极化或抑制 DC 表面共刺激分子表达，削弱抗 CTLA-4 介导的初始 T 细胞激活。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"揭示血清丁酸/丙酸与抗 CTLA-4 预后负相关，阐明靶点依赖性\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"role\":\"比较\",\"use\":\"绘制高阶机制图谱，区分丁酸盐对 PD-1 与 CTLA-4 抑制剂疗效的差异化影响\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_1_P03\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_1_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_1\",\"ordinal\":3,\"point\":\"揭示 SCFAs 在抗 CTLA-4 治疗中的负面或限制性作用。\",\"development\":\"基于 P0503 与 P0559 的数据，论证高血清丁酸/丙酸如何通过促进 Treg 极化或抑制 DC 表面共刺激分子表达，削弱抗 CTLA-4 介导的初始 T 细胞激活。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0503\",\"P0559\"]}]}},\"Ch3::U3_1::U3_1_P04\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_1::U3_1_P04\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_1_P04\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_1\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_1_P04\",\"point\":\"分析微环境缺氧状态与代谢物浓度阈值对 SCFAs 效应方向的决定性影响。\",\"development\":\"利用 P0377 与 P0544 的机制发现，指出在葡萄糖剥夺或严重缺氧条件下，SCFAs 可能被肿瘤细胞逆向摄取作为碳源，从而逆转其预期的抑癌效果。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"展示缺氧微环境中癌细胞逆向摄取丁酸供能的反常现象\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"role\":\"背景\",\"use\":\"提供 CRC 中调节微生物群增强 ICI 疗效的机制视角\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"role\":\"发展\",\"use\":\"梳理 SCFA 在不同浓度与癌种下的矛盾功能，为解释情境依赖性提供理论框架\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_1_P04\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_1_P04\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_1\",\"ordinal\":4,\"point\":\"分析微环境缺氧状态与代谢物浓度阈值对 SCFAs 效应方向的决定性影响。\",\"development\":\"利用 P0377 与 P0544 的机制发现，指出在葡萄糖剥夺或严重缺氧条件下，SCFAs 可能被肿瘤细胞逆向摄取作为碳源，从而逆转其预期的抑癌效果。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0377\",\"P0544\"]}]}},\"Ch3::U3_2::U3_2_P01\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_2::U3_2_P01\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_2_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_2\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_2_P01\",\"point\":\"详述肌苷靶向 UBA6 的生化结合验证、遗传学回补实验及对肿瘤细胞抗原呈递通路的分子重塑。\",\"development\":\"整合 P0582 的 LiP-SMap 筛选、体外硫酯酶活性测定及 CRISPR 敲除数据，构建“肌苷-UBA6-USE1-FAT10\\\"信号轴，阐明其如何解除肿瘤内在免疫抑制。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"核心文献，证实肌苷直接结合 UBA6 解除 MHC-I 抑制\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"role\":\"例证\",\"use\":\"发现别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌、增强肿瘤免疫原性的分子机制\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_2_P01\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_2_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_2\",\"ordinal\":1,\"point\":\"详述肌苷靶向 UBA6 的生化结合验证、遗传学回补实验及对肿瘤细胞抗原呈递通路的分子重塑。\",\"development\":\"整合 P0582 的 LiP-SMap 筛选、体外硫酯酶活性测定及 CRISPR 敲除数据，构建“肌苷-UBA6-USE1-FAT10\\\"信号轴，阐明其如何解除肿瘤内在免疫抑制。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0582\"]}]}},\"Ch3::U3_2::U3_2_P02\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_2::U3_2_P02\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_2_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_2\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_2_P02\",\"point\":\"汇报 CheckMate 025 队列中血浆肌苷水平与抗 PD-1 治疗总生存期的定量关联，并强调其作为系统性暴露代理的局限性。\",\"development\":\"基于 P0582 的临床队列数据，对比 nivolumab 与 everolimus 组的差异，确立高血浆肌苷作为 ICI 疗效预测因子的统计效力，同时指出缺乏 TME 实测数据的现状。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"提供 CheckMate 025 队列中血浆肌苷与 OS 关联的临床数据\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"role\":\"发展\",\"use\":\"提供肌苷联合 ICI 治疗晚期实体瘤的随机对照临床 II 期数据，证实 PFS 获益\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_2_P02\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_2_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_2\",\"ordinal\":2,\"point\":\"汇报 CheckMate 025 队列中血浆肌苷水平与抗 PD-1 治疗总生存期的定量关联，并强调其作为系统性暴露代理的局限性。\",\"development\":\"基于 P0582 的临床队列数据，对比 nivolumab 与 everolimus 组的差异，确立高血浆肌苷作为 ICI 疗效预测因子的统计效力，同时指出缺乏 TME 实测数据的现状。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0582\"]}]}},\"Ch3::U3_2::U3_2_P03\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_2::U3_2_P03\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_2_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_2\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_2_P03\",\"point\":\"区分肌苷的肿瘤内在作用（UBA6 抑制）与 T 细胞外在作用（A2AR 激活/碳源补充）。\",\"development\":\"结合 P0124 与 P0584，对比肌苷在肿瘤细胞内直接抑制 UBA6 与在 T 细胞内通过 A2AR/cAMP 通路或替代糖酵解途径发挥作用的平行机制，避免机制混淆。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"阐释双歧杆菌来源肌苷经 A2AR/cAMP 通路促进 Th1 分化及作为替代碳源维持效应 T 细胞存活\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"role\":\"比较\",\"use\":\"对比生态与还原论方法，明确双歧杆菌通过肌苷-A2AR 轴增强 T 细胞活性的分子路径\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0584\",\"role\":\"背景\",\"use\":\"提供腺苷脱氨酶将免疫抑制性腺苷转化为肌苷的药代动力学数据\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_2_P03\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_2_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_2\",\"ordinal\":3,\"point\":\"区分肌苷的肿瘤内在作用（UBA6 抑制）与 T 细胞外在作用（A2AR 激活/碳源补充）。\",\"development\":\"结合 P0124 与 P0584，对比肌苷在肿瘤细胞内直接抑制 UBA6 与在 T 细胞内通过 A2AR/cAMP 通路或替代糖酵解途径发挥作用的平行机制，避免机制混淆。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0124\",\"P0251\",\"P0584\"]}]}},\"Ch3::U3_2::U3_2_P04\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_2::U3_2_P04\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_2_P04\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_2\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_2_P04\",\"point\":\"明确标注人体 TME 内肌苷绝对浓度数据的缺失现状及药代动力学挑战。\",\"development\":\"综合 P0582 与 P0584 的讨论，指出腺苷快速降解（~10 秒）与肌苷较长半衰期（~15 小时）导致的测量窗口限制，以及缺乏原位微透析或空间代谢组学数据的现状，强调这是限制机制确证的关键缺口。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"role\":\"局限\",\"use\":\"明确指出因样本完整性问题未能在人体肿瘤队列中直接检测肌苷浓度\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0584\",\"role\":\"局限\",\"use\":\"指出体外有效浓度属人工设定而非内源性实测值，体内浓度受血流灌注与降解酶多重制约\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_2_P04\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_2_P04\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_2\",\"ordinal\":4,\"point\":\"明确标注人体 TME 内肌苷绝对浓度数据的缺失现状及药代动力学挑战。\",\"development\":\"综合 P0582 与 P0584 的讨论，指出腺苷快速降解（~10 秒）与肌苷较长半衰期（~15 小时）导致的测量窗口限制，以及缺乏原位微透析或空间代谢组学数据的现状，强调这是限制机制确证的关键缺口。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0582\",\"P0584\"]}]}},\"Ch3::U3_3::U3_3_P01\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_3::U3_3_P01\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_3_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_3\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_3_P01\",\"point\":\"阐述次级胆汁酸（TDCA, UDCA 等）通过 TGR5/FXR 受体增强 CD8+ T 细胞杀伤与巨噬细胞 M1 极化的机制。\",\"development\":\"整合 P0481 与 P0424 的证据，说明胆汁酸如何克服抗生素介导的菌群耗竭，并在 HCC 患者中转化为可测量的预后标志物。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"证实牛磺脱氧胆酸经 TGR5 受体直接增强 CD8+ T 细胞毒性，并在菌群失调模型中恢复 ICI 疗效\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"提供不可切除肝细胞癌队列中次级胆汁酸丰度与更长 PFS 的正向关联\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"role\":\"背景\",\"use\":\"基于毛螺菌科比较基因组学预测胆汁酸转化基因簇，为核受体配体生成提供菌株特异性功能线索\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_3_P01\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_3_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_3\",\"ordinal\":1,\"point\":\"阐述次级胆汁酸（TDCA, UDCA 等）通过 TGR5/FXR 受体增强 CD8+ T 细胞杀伤与巨噬细胞 M1 极化的机制。\",\"development\":\"整合 P0481 与 P0424 的证据，说明胆汁酸如何克服抗生素介导的菌群耗竭，并在 HCC 患者中转化为可测量的预后标志物。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0481\",\"P0424\"]}]}},\"Ch3::U3_3::U3_3_P02\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_3::U3_3_P02\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_3_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_3\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_3_P02\",\"point\":\"解析色氨酸代谢物（IPA, Kynurenine）通过 AhR 与 RORγt 受体调控 T 细胞亚群分化与骨髓细胞极化的路径。\",\"development\":\"基于 P0180 与 P0209，对比保护性吲哚衍生物（激活 AhR 维持 T 细胞干性）与致病性犬尿氨酸（抑制 T 细胞/促进 Treg）的双向调节作用。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"揭示次级胆汁酸结合非经典核受体 RORγt 与 NR4A1，精细调控 Th17/Treg 平衡的分子细节\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"阐明色氨酸代谢物 IPA 通过 AhR 维持 CD8+ T 细胞干性（Tcf7 超增强子），并与抗 PD-1 产生协同效应\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_3_P02\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_3_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_3\",\"ordinal\":2,\"point\":\"解析色氨酸代谢物（IPA, Kynurenine）通过 AhR 与 RORγt 受体调控 T 细胞亚群分化与骨髓细胞极化的路径。\",\"development\":\"基于 P0180 与 P0209，对比保护性吲哚衍生物（激活 AhR 维持 T 细胞干性）与致病性犬尿氨酸（抑制 T 细胞/促进 Treg）的双向调节作用。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0180\",\"P0209\"]}]}},\"Ch3::U3_3::U3_3_P03\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_3::U3_3_P03\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_3_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_3\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_3_P03\",\"point\":\"讨论核受体信号在跨组织免疫监视中的系统性与局部性差异。\",\"development\":\"结合 P0180 与 P0481 的动物模型数据，辨析核受体配体在肠道局部稳态维持与远端肿瘤微环境重塑中的剂量与分布差异。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"role\":\"背景\",\"use\":\"提供核受体配体在肠道局部稳态维持与远端肿瘤微环境重塑中的剂量与分布差异的理论支撑\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"role\":\"例证\",\"use\":\"展示胆汁酸在克服抗生素介导的菌群耗竭中的远端肿瘤微环境重塑作用\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_3_P03\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_3_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_3\",\"ordinal\":3,\"point\":\"讨论核受体信号在跨组织免疫监视中的系统性与局部性差异。\",\"development\":\"结合 P0180 与 P0481 的动物模型数据，辨析核受体配体在肠道局部稳态维持与远端肿瘤微环境重塑中的剂量与分布差异。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0180\",\"P0481\"]}]}},\"Ch3::U3_4::U3_4_P01\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_4::U3_4_P01\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_4_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_4\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_4_P01\",\"point\":\"论证宏基因组功能通路（如 MEP、核黄素合成）与特定 T 细胞亚群（Vδ2, MAIT）活化的直接关联。\",\"development\":\"基于 P0444 的 PDTO 共培养与纵向队列数据，说明为何关注代谢通路丰度比单一菌属更能准确预测 ICI 反应。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"提供宏基因组功能通路（MEP、核黄素合成）与特定 T 细胞亚群（Vδ2、MAIT）活化直接关联的纵向队列证据\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_4_P01\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_4_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_4\",\"ordinal\":1,\"point\":\"论证宏基因组功能通路（如 MEP、核黄素合成）与特定 T 细胞亚群（Vδ2, MAIT）活化的直接关联。\",\"development\":\"基于 P0444 的 PDTO 共培养与纵向队列数据，说明为何关注代谢通路丰度比单一菌属更能准确预测 ICI 反应。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0444\"]}]}},\"Ch3::U3_4::U3_4_P02\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_4::U3_4_P02\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_4_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_4\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_4_P02\",\"point\":\"阐述代谢物驱动的表观遗传重编程（HDAC 抑制、染色质开放）如何决定免疫细胞的功能状态。\",\"development\":\"整合 P0220 与 P0587 的机制发现，解释代谢物如何作为表观遗传酶的变构调节剂或底物，锁定 T 细胞或巨噬细胞的效应/耗竭表型。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"阐述代谢物作为表观遗传修饰底物或直接抑制 HDAC，改变染色质开放性以重编程巨噬细胞与 T 细胞转录程序\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"role\":\"发展\",\"use\":\"整合多组学数据揭示微生物代谢物系统性调节宿主免疫细胞氧化磷酸化与糖酵解平衡，决定效应与耗竭 T 细胞命运\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_4_P02\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_4_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_4\",\"ordinal\":2,\"point\":\"阐述代谢物驱动的表观遗传重编程（HDAC 抑制、染色质开放）如何决定免疫细胞的功能状态。\",\"development\":\"整合 P0220 与 P0587 的机制发现，解释代谢物如何作为表观遗传酶的变构调节剂或底物，锁定 T 细胞或巨噬细胞的效应/耗竭表型。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0220\",\"P0587\"]}]}},\"Ch3::U3_4::U3_4_P03\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_4::U3_4_P03\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_4_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_4\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_4_P03\",\"point\":\"提出以“功能性菌群失调评分”替代传统α/β多样性作为 ICI 疗效预测指标的必要性。\",\"development\":\"结合 P0444 与 P0363 的观点，批判单一分类学分析的局限，主张采用多组学整合与机器学习模型捕捉代谢功能的动态变化。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"提供功能性通路优于物种分类的实证\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"role\":\"发展\",\"use\":\"批判单一分类学分析的局限，主张采用多组学整合与机器学习模型捕捉代谢功能的动态变化以替代传统多样性指标\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_4_P03\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_4_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_4\",\"ordinal\":3,\"point\":\"提出以“功能性菌群失调评分”替代传统α/β多样性作为 ICI 疗效预测指标的必要性。\",\"development\":\"结合 P0444 与 P0363 的观点，批判单一分类学分析的局限，主张采用多组学整合与机器学习模型捕捉代谢功能的动态变化。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0444\",\"P0363\"]}]}},\"Ch3::U3_5::U3_5_P01\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_5::U3_5_P01\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_5_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_5\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_5_P01\",\"point\":\"客观评估当前血浆/粪便代谢组学作为 ICI 疗效预测工具的效能与固有偏差。\",\"development\":\"基于 P0582 与 P0363，承认宏观代谢物检测在临床可行性上的优势，同时指出其无法区分游离态与结合态、无法反映组织滞留时间的缺陷。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"指出因样本完整性问题未能在人体肿瘤队列中直接检测肌苷浓度，仅能以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性代理\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"role\":\"背景\",\"use\":\"强调多数机制证据来自小鼠模型，血浆/粪便浓度不能完全代表 TME 暴露水平，警示跨物种外推风险\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_5_P01\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_5_P01\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_5\",\"ordinal\":1,\"point\":\"客观评估当前血浆/粪便代谢组学作为 ICI 疗效预测工具的效能与固有偏差。\",\"development\":\"基于 P0582 与 P0363，承认宏观代谢物检测在临床可行性上的优势，同时指出其无法区分游离态与结合态、无法反映组织滞留时间的缺陷。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0582\",\"P0363\"]}]}},\"Ch3::U3_5::U3_5_P02\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_5::U3_5_P02\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_5_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_5\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_5_P02\",\"point\":\"深入剖析人体 TME 内代谢物绝对浓度数据缺失对机制研究与临床转化的具体阻碍，特别强调肌苷案例。\",\"development\":\"结合 P0584 与 P0413 的药代动力学与递送障碍分析，说明缺乏 TME 浓度阈值如何导致体外有效浓度无法在体内复现，以及为何单纯提高血浆浓度未必改善疗效。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0584\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"指出体外有效浓度（如 100 μM 肌苷）属人工设定而非内源性实测值，体内浓度受血流灌注与降解酶多重制约\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"role\":\"主论据\",\"use\":\"从药理学角度分析代谢物在 TME 中的递送效率受血管通透性及转运体限制，导致全身循环与局部有效浓度脱节\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_5_P02\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_5_P02\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_5\",\"ordinal\":2,\"point\":\"深入剖析人体 TME 内代谢物绝对浓度数据缺失对机制研究与临床转化的具体阻碍，特别强调肌苷案例。\",\"development\":\"结合 P0584 与 P0413 的药代动力学与递送障碍分析，说明缺乏 TME 浓度阈值如何导致体外有效浓度无法在体内复现，以及为何单纯提高血浆浓度未必改善疗效。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0584\",\"P0413\"]}]}},\"Ch3::U3_5::U3_5_P03\":{\"chapter_id\":\"Ch3\",\"local_task_id\":\"U3_5::U3_5_P03\",\"original_task_id\":\"U3_5_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_5\",\"kind\":\"paragraph\",\"task\":{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_5_P03\",\"point\":\"规划填补 TME 浓度缺口的未来技术路线与研究范式。\",\"development\":\"提出引入原位微透析（microdialysis）、基质辅助激光解吸电离质谱成像（MALDI-MSI）及配对组织 - 血液纵向采样，以建立“局部浓度 - 受体占有率 - 临床结局”的直接定量映射。\",\"source_uses\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"role\":\"发展\",\"use\":\"呼吁未来研究需解决 TME 内代谢物浓度测量问题\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"role\":\"发展\",\"use\":\"主张采用多组学整合与机器学习模型捕捉代谢功能的动态变化\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"role\":\"发展\",\"use\":\"提出需解决代谢物在 TME 中的递送效率问题\"}],\"carried_over\":true,\"point_changed_from_brief\":false,\"source_briefs\":[\"U3_5_P03\"],\"source_brief_details\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"U3_5_P03\",\"unit_id\":\"U3_5\",\"ordinal\":3,\"point\":\"规划填补 TME 浓度缺口的未来技术路线与研究范式。\",\"development\":\"提出引入原位微透析（microdialysis）、基质辅助激光解吸电离质谱成像（MALDI-MSI）及配对组织 - 血液纵向采样，以建立“局部浓度 - 受体占有率 - 临床结局”的直接定量映射。\",\"source_handles\":[\"P0582\",\"P0363\",\"P0413\"]}]}}},\"chapter_frames\":{\"Ch3\":{\"chapter_title\":\"微生物代谢物的中介作用与分子机制\",\"chapter_purpose\":\"读者将掌握四大类核心微生物代谢物调节 ICI 疗效的具体分子靶点与下游通路，理解代谢物效应的强情境依赖性（如 SCFAs 在 PD-1 与 CTLA-4 背景下的双向作用），并明确当前文献中人体 TME 代谢物浓度数据的缺失现状（特别是肌苷仅有血浆关联数据而无组织实测值）及其对因果推断的限制。\",\"chapter_scope\":\"肠道微生物组通过特定代谢物（如 SCFAs、肌苷、胆汁酸及色氨酸衍生物）介导的表观遗传修饰、受体信号传导及肿瘤细胞内在重编程，系统性调节实体瘤对 ICI 的疗效；然而，现有临床证据高度依赖血浆或粪便浓度作为系统性暴露代理，人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内代谢物的绝对生理浓度及其与疗效的直接定量关联仍属关键证据缺口，尤其是肌苷在 TME 内的实测数据缺失限制了因果推断与剂量优化。\",\"chapter_thesis\":\"肠道微生物组通过特定代谢物（如 SCFAs、肌苷、胆汁酸及色氨酸衍生物）介导的表观遗传修饰、受体信号传导及肿瘤细胞内在重编程，系统性调节实体瘤对 ICI 的疗效；然而，现有临床证据高度依赖血浆或粪便浓度作为系统性暴露代理，人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内代谢物的绝对生理浓度及其与疗效的直接定量关联仍属关键证据缺口，尤其是肌苷在 TME 内的实测数据缺失限制了因果推断与剂量优化。\",\"chapter_argument\":\"肠道微生物组通过特定代谢物（如 SCFAs、肌苷、胆汁酸及色氨酸衍生物）介导的表观遗传修饰、受体信号传导及肿瘤细胞内在重编程，系统性调节实体瘤对 ICI 的疗效；然而，现有临床证据高度依赖血浆或粪便浓度作为系统性暴露代理，人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内代谢物的绝对生理浓度及其与疗效的直接定量关联仍属关键证据缺口，尤其是肌苷在 TME 内的实测数据缺失限制了因果推断与剂量优化。\",\"reader_objective\":\"读者将掌握四大类核心微生物代谢物调节 ICI 疗效的具体分子靶点与下游通路，理解代谢物效应的强情境依赖性（如 SCFAs 在 PD-1 与 CTLA-4 背景下的双向作用），并明确当前文献中人体 TME 代谢物浓度数据的缺失现状（特别是肌苷仅有血浆关联数据而无组织实测值）及其对因果推断的限制。\",\"research_question\":\"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\",\"review_argument\":\"肠道微生物组通过分类学特征、代谢产物及免疫通路调节实体瘤患者对 ICI 的临床疗效，但证据强度因肿瘤类型、研究设计及干预策略而异。观察性关联证据在黑色素瘤中最强，NSCLC 和 RCC 次之，但关联不等于因果。机制证据主要来自动物模型，人类验证有限，特别是肿瘤微环境内代谢物浓度数据缺失（如肌苷仅有血浆数据）。干预策略在初治人群中显示希望（FMT-LUMINate ORR 75-80%），但在难治人群中效果有限（MITRIC ORR 0%），且安全性受 ICI 方案调节（Prevotella 相关心肌炎仅在双 ICI 背景下出现）。目前缺乏 Phase III RCT 证据支持微生物干预的常规临床应用，未来研究需解决标准化、因果推断及人群分层问题。\",\"shared_scope\":{\"statement\":\"本综述聚焦于实体瘤（黑色素瘤、非小细胞肺癌、肾细胞癌、结直肠癌等）患者接受免疫检查点抑制剂（PD-1/PD-L1、CTLA-4 抑制剂）治疗期间，肠道微生物组对治疗疗效（ORR、PFS、OS）及毒性（irAEs）的调节作用。涵盖观察性关联证据（区分回顾性与前瞻性队列）、因果机制解析（免疫细胞、分子通路、代谢物）、外部干扰因素（抗生素、PPI、饮食）及微生物干预策略（FMT、益生菌、工程菌）的临床试验数据。明确排除血液系统恶性肿瘤及非免疫治疗背景下的微生物组研究（除非用于机制对比）。严格区分肠道微生物组与肿瘤内微生物组的作用边界。证据等级标注明确：观察性关联不推断因果，干预试验区分 I/II 期与 III 期，代谢物数据区分血浆与肿瘤组织浓度。\"},\"review_argument_status\":\"calibrated\",\"review_argument_source\":\"whole_plan_improvement\"}},\"unit_contexts\":{\"Ch3\":{\"U3_1\":{\"unit_id\":\"U3_1\",\"focus\":\"短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）通过 HDAC 抑制与 GPCR 信号通路发挥双重免疫调节作用，其效应方向严格取决于 ICI 靶点类型、局部微环境状态及浓度阈值。\",\"owner_unit_context\":{\"evidence_conditions\":\"\",\"synthesis\":\"上述案例共同表明，SCFAs 并非单向的“免疫增敏剂”。其在 PD-1 背景下主要通过表观遗传重编程增强效应 T 细胞功能（P0092, P0515），而在 CTLA-4 背景下可能因过度促进 Treg 或干扰 DC 共刺激信号而限制疗效（P0503）。此外，微环境的缺氧状态与局部浓度阈值决定了 SCFAs 是作为抑癌代谢物还是促癌底物（P0377），这要求后续机制讨论必须剥离单一维度的线性描述。\",\"transition\":\"与 SCFAs 主要作用于宿主免疫细胞不同，部分微生物代谢物能够直接穿透细胞膜靶向肿瘤细胞内在蛋白，从而重塑肿瘤的抗原呈递属性。\",\"supporting_studies\":[{\"contribution\":\"提供粪便SCFA水平与抗PD-1疗效正相关的临床队列证据，确立其作为疗效预测标志物的实证基础。\",\"paper_id\":\"2365676f101b69b7a4aa2e5ba20e1e3bbe1c0cb6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\"},{\"contribution\":\"揭示血清丁酸/丙酸与抗CTLA-4预后负相关，阐明SCFA效应的靶点依赖性与情境反转。\",\"paper_id\":\"e2d5688c3346ac3349ad3e82b9abf9f5b92382ee\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\"},{\"contribution\":\"详述丁酸通过HDAC抑制上调Pdcd1/Cd28增强CD8+ T细胞记忆，同时提示Treg分化的双向潜力。\",\"paper_id\":\"e79cf5704aa32b05d4bd83b923592452b3074529\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\"},{\"contribution\":\"展示缺氧微环境中癌细胞逆向摄取丁酸供能的反常现象，凸显代谢物效应的微环境阈值依赖性。\",\"paper_id\":\"a2db7c8539dee7153c704805a86c4fbcbdb2c8c9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\"},{\"contribution\":\"补充实体瘤抗PD-1治疗中响应者fSCFA显著升高的表型数据，强化代谢物介导免疫激活的临床关联。\",\"paper_id\":\"5dafc84d8aa8c1cc679fad0bfc3f4fa134a26c65\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\"},{\"contribution\":\"梳理SCFA在不同浓度与癌种下的矛盾功能，为解释肠道菌群对ICI疗效的情境依赖性提供理论框架。\",\"paper_id\":\"5d4d1432a51cc91edfadc9f8ca60f84f5bd9c2f4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\"},{\"contribution\":\"绘制微生物代谢物调节抗肿瘤免疫的高阶机制图谱，详细区分不同代谢物对PD-1与CTLA-4抑制剂疗效的差异化影响（如丁酸盐的双刃剑效应）。\",\"paper_id\":\"f740fe4e28eed64b9c255e57d2e93b64c6cbdd27\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\"}]},\"unit_notes\":\"\"},\"U3_2\":{\"unit_id\":\"U3_2\",\"focus\":\"肌苷直接靶向肿瘤细胞泛素激活酶 UBA6，解除其对炎症信号与 MHC-I 表达的抑制，从而增强肿瘤内在免疫原性与 T 细胞杀伤敏感性；然而，人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据缺失，现有临床关联仅基于血浆水平。\",\"owner_unit_context\":{\"evidence_conditions\":\"\",\"synthesis\":\"肌苷的作用具有明确的靶点特异性：它并非单纯作用于免疫细胞，而是通过直接抑制肿瘤细胞 UBA6 来解除对 MHC-I 与炎症通路的转录后抑制（P0582），同时作为 T 细胞的代谢燃料与 A2AR 配体协同增效（P0124, P0584）。CheckMate 025 队列提供了循环肌苷预测 OS 的强临床关联（P0582），但所有研究均受限于无法在人体活检组织中直接定量肌苷浓度，目前仅能依赖血浆水平或 UBA6 表达作为间接代理指标。这一缺口阻碍了确定 TME 内有效抑制 UBA6 所需的肌苷浓度阈值。\",\"transition\":\"除了直接靶向肿瘤细胞或作为 T 细胞燃料外，更多微生物代谢物通过激活宿主核受体网络，远程调控髓系与淋巴系细胞的极化平衡。\",\"supporting_studies\":[{\"contribution\":\"核心文献，证实肌苷直接结合UBA6解除MHC-I抑制，并指出人体肿瘤内实测浓度缺失的关键转化缺口。\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\"},{\"contribution\":\"阐释双歧杆菌来源肌苷经A2AR/cAMP通路促进Th1分化及作为替代碳源维持效应T细胞存活的平行机制。\",\"paper_id\":\"364d5abc343a02132e4f3f24c0b441cb277190f2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\"},{\"contribution\":\"提供腺苷脱氨酶将免疫抑制性腺苷转化为肌苷的药代动力学数据，说明肌苷半衰期延长对微环境暴露的意义。\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:290154100\",\"source_handle\":\"P0584\"},{\"contribution\":\"对比生态与还原论方法，明确双歧杆菌通过肌苷-A2AR轴增强T细胞活性的分子路径，支撑机制解析。\",\"paper_id\":\"68b67449fc944c707f68e31b629b3909e59b29ea\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\"},{\"contribution\":\"提供肌苷联合ICI治疗晚期实体瘤的首个随机对照临床II期数据，证实了肌苷在延长PFS方面的统计学显著性，并为“肠道代谢物调节免疫治疗”假说提供了初步临床支持。\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:272644866\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\"},{\"contribution\":\"建立基于单细胞分辨率的药物诱导TME重塑量化框架，发现别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌、增强肿瘤免疫原性和T细胞功能的分子机制。\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286644045\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\"}]},\"unit_notes\":\"\"},\"U3_3\":{\"unit_id\":\"U3_3\",\"focus\":\"次级胆汁酸与色氨酸代谢物主要通过激活宿主核受体（FXR, TGR5, AhR, RORγt）重塑髓系与淋巴系细胞的极化状态，进而决定抗肿瘤免疫基调。\",\"owner_unit_context\":{\"evidence_conditions\":\"\",\"synthesis\":\"胆汁酸与色氨酸代谢物构成了微生物 - 宿主跨器官通讯的核心化学语言。TDCA 通过 TGR5 直接赋能 CD8+ T 细胞（P0481），而多种次级胆汁酸与 IPA 则通过 FXR/TGR5/AhR/RORγt 等核受体网络精细调控 Th17/Treg 比例与巨噬细胞表型（P0180, P0209）。HCC 队列数据进一步证实，这些受体介导的代谢信号不仅存在于动物模型，也在人类实体瘤患者的基线代谢谱中与长期临床获益挂钩（P0424）。\",\"transition\":\"上述代谢物不仅作为独立的信号分子，还深度嵌入宿主免疫细胞的能量代谢与表观遗传网络中，形成多维度的功能整合。\",\"supporting_studies\":[{\"contribution\":\"证实牛磺脱氧胆酸经TGR5受体直接增强CD8+ T细胞毒性，并在菌群失调模型中恢复ICI疗效。\",\"paper_id\":\"d684f0baadf8b8893a164468cb9ee38f1eb49901\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\"},{\"contribution\":\"揭示次级胆汁酸结合非经典核受体RORγt与NR4A1，精细调控Th17/Treg平衡的分子细节。\",\"paper_id\":\"4ed2637cc267e69d764e877652226e827eb752a9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\"},{\"contribution\":\"阐明色氨酸代谢物IPA通过AhR维持CD8+ T细胞干性（Tcf7超增强子），并与抗PD-1产生协同效应。\",\"paper_id\":\"5a81f2ebb2189b30d6f36f3aa8ed1ae9503fa614\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\"},{\"contribution\":\"提供不可切除肝细胞癌队列中次级胆汁酸丰度与更长PFS的正向关联，连接特定菌群与临床预后。\",\"paper_id\":\"ba17ba65137d50666a0e60a34c2cfe287f8bc9a4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\"},{\"contribution\":\"基于毛螺菌科比较基因组学预测胆汁酸转化基因簇，为核受体配体生成提供菌株特异性功能线索。\",\"paper_id\":\"52fc41afc10d1874915df79a5f918e521e7ca077\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\"}]},\"unit_notes\":\"\"},\"U3_4\":{\"unit_id\":\"U3_4\",\"focus\":\"微生物代谢物通过重塑免疫细胞的能量代谢通路与表观遗传景观，实现抗肿瘤免疫功能的系统性整合，其中功能性通路特征比单一物种分类更具预测价值。\",\"owner_unit_context\":{\"evidence_conditions\":\"\",\"synthesis\":\"代谢物的作用超越了单纯的受体配体角色，它们直接参与宿主细胞的能量代谢与表观遗传架构。P0444 揭示了特定细菌代谢通路（MEP vs 核黄素合成）如何精准匹配 Vδ2 与 MAIT 这两类非典型 T 细胞的活化需求，提供了“功能通路优于物种分类”的实证。P0220 与 P0587 进一步表明，代谢物通过提供乙酰-CoA 或抑制 HDAC，直接改写免疫细胞的染色质景观，这种代谢 - 表观遗传耦合是解释为何相同菌群在不同宿主状态下产生不同疗效的关键。\",\"transition\":\"尽管上述机制在临床前模型与部分人类队列中得到有力支持，但整个领域面临一个根本性的方法学瓶颈：人体肿瘤局部的代谢物浓度数据极度匮乏。\",\"supporting_studies\":[{\"contribution\":\"提供宏基因组功能通路（MEP、核黄素合成）与特定T细胞亚群（Vδ2、MAIT）活化直接关联的纵向队列证据。\",\"paper_id\":\"c426f22c38d341a24524f67fd75537f6ef60aaf0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\"},{\"contribution\":\"阐述代谢物作为表观遗传修饰底物或直接抑制HDAC，改变染色质开放性以重编程巨噬细胞与T细胞转录程序。\",\"paper_id\":\"5d4d1432a51cc91edfadc9f8ca60f84f5bd9c2f4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\"},{\"contribution\":\"整合多组学数据揭示微生物代谢物系统性调节宿主免疫细胞氧化磷酸化与糖酵解平衡，决定效应与耗竭T细胞命运。\",\"paper_id\":\"OpenAlex:W7116840248\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\"},{\"contribution\":\"批判单一分类学分析的局限，主张采用多组学整合与机器学习模型捕捉代谢功能的动态变化以替代传统多样性指标。\",\"paper_id\":\"9db1c1ced73dca207c6289b20b4a2914a09ca2b1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\"}]},\"unit_notes\":\"\"},\"U3_5\":{\"unit_id\":\"U3_5\",\"focus\":\"现有证据高度依赖血浆或粪便代谢物浓度作为系统性暴露代理，人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内代谢物的绝对生理浓度及其与 ICI 疗效的直接定量关联构成关键转化缺口，特别是肌苷在 TME 内的实测数据缺失。\",\"owner_unit_context\":{\"evidence_conditions\":\"\",\"synthesis\":\"本章节的所有机制假设均建立在“系统性暴露代理”之上。P0582 的坦诚声明代表了当前领域的普遍困境：我们已知高血浆肌苷预示更长 OS，但不知肿瘤实质内究竟需要多少μM 的肌苷才能饱和抑制 UBA6。P0363 与 P0413 进一步指出，血浆/粪便浓度受饮食、肾脏清除率及肠道菌群周转率的强烈干扰，无法精确反映 TME 局部的真实化学梯度。这一缺口不仅阻碍了代谢物补充剂的精准给药，也使得许多基于动物模型的高浓度干预策略难以直接翻译至临床。\",\"transition\":\"综上所述，微生物代谢物通过精密的分子网络深刻重塑了实体瘤的免疫景观，但跨越从系统性关联到局部因果确证的鸿沟，仍需下一代空间与动态监测技术的介入。\",\"supporting_studies\":[{\"contribution\":\"明确指出因样本完整性问题未能在人体肿瘤队列中直接检测肌苷浓度，仅能以UBA6表达作为通路活性代理。\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\"},{\"contribution\":\"强调多数机制证据来自小鼠模型，血浆/粪便浓度不能完全代表TME暴露水平，警示跨物种外推风险。\",\"paper_id\":\"9db1c1ced73dca207c6289b20b4a2914a09ca2b1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\"},{\"contribution\":\"指出体外有效浓度（如100 μM肌苷）属人工设定而非内源性实测值，体内浓度受血流灌注与降解酶多重制约。\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:290154100\",\"source_handle\":\"P0584\"},{\"contribution\":\"从药理学角度分析代谢物在TME中的递送效率受血管通透性及转运体限制，导致全身循环与局部有效浓度脱节。\",\"paper_id\":\"b4de79d677aec2f2b495ddebba1aaf8a77cffc38\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\"}]},\"unit_notes\":\"\"}}},\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8f9d2277a529e4937cdaca92\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fe7e2c2b4f9c14cf1516a980\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0190aee6e65653c45ab9f85a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用叙述性综述方法，系统梳理现有文献中关于肠道微生物代谢物与宿主免疫系统相互作用的研究。文章按逻辑模块组织：1) 基础免疫调节机制（先天性与适应性免疫）；2) 主要代谢物类别及其分子机制（受体结合、表观遗传修饰等）；3) 在癌症免疫治疗中的具体作用（增强ICI反应、重塑TME、克服耐药）；4) 临床应用前景与挑战。未进行系统性检索流程描述或定量荟萃分析。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a9e0be44201b834afc0e41d0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物代谢物（SCFAs、胆汁酸、色氨酸代谢物）调节先天性和适应性免疫的详细机制框架，特别是它们在重塑肿瘤微环境和增强ICI疗效中的具体分子路径。\",\"limits\":\"作为叙述性综述，未提供新的实验数据；因果关系的验证仍依赖于未来的研究（如无菌动物模型和人类代谢组学验证）；未能量化不同代谢物在不同癌症类型中的具体效应大小。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::dd9bb6e8ffb215ae50417294\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"总结了当前基于微生物群的临床干预策略（FMT、益生菌、代谢物补充）的现状和挑战，为未来个性化治疗提供了方向。\",\"limits\":\"指出个体异质性、长期安全性及代谢物生物利用度等问题仍是主要障碍，目前缺乏大规模随机对照试验的确证证据。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9f5239607957a19db0afd224\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"基于现有文献的综合分析\",\"finding\":\"SCFAs（如丁酸盐、丙酸盐）通过抑制组蛋白去乙酰化酶（HDACs）和激活GPCRs，促进调节性T细胞（Tregs）分化以维持耐受，同时增强CD8+ T细胞的细胞毒性；丁酸盐还能通过表观遗传机制（FOXP3乙酰化）促进Treg分化。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3ebb778a131e2f098cc397f1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"基于现有文献的综合分析\",\"finding\":\"次级胆汁酸通过FXR和GPBAR1受体调节树突状细胞成熟和促炎细胞因子分泌，其代谢失调与ICI反应降低相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c2d3a800d8235cb666344991\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"基于现有文献的综合分析\",\"finding\":\"色氨酸代谢物（吲哚类）通过芳香烃受体（AhR）途径强化黏膜屏障，维持Treg稳态并限制Th17驱动的炎症。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b4643d6cf49328804701dfd1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"基于现有文献的综合分析\",\"finding\":\"FMT从ICI响应者转移至非响应者可在难治性癌症中恢复治疗敏感性，表明代谢物介导的免疫重塑具有临床转化潜力。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::14638f27ef074f516c01ef1b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::120c6ef4af77e0ac5dec14ed\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）取得了显著进展，但仅部分患者有效且存在耐药性。肠道微生物群被认为是影响疗效的关键因素，但其具体功能产物——微生物代谢物——如何精确调控免疫通路以影响癌症免疫治疗结局的机制尚不完全清楚。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3ecea46a17c2d52ab1552c24\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"肠道微生物群衍生的代谢物（如短链脂肪酸、胆汁酸衍生物、色氨酸代谢物）在癌症免疫治疗中的作用机制及临床潜力，聚焦于宿主-微生物互作对免疫系统的影响。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::67568df7eed98bde33489f51\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述，旨在综合近期关于肠道微生物代谢物如何调节抗肿瘤免疫和免疫治疗疗效的研究发现。文章首先阐述了肠道菌群通过代谢产物作为生化介质，协调先天性和适应性免疫过程，重塑肿瘤微环境（TME），从而影响免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）疗效的机制。随后，详细分类介绍了SCFAs、次级胆汁酸和色氨酸代谢物的具体免疫调节功能。最后，讨论了粪菌移植（FMT）、益生菌/益生元补充及代谢物直接补充等临床干预策略的潜力与挑战，强调需进一步验证因果关系并解决个体异质性问题。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::aa4e2b799008bfbdb03a47b7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物如何通过代谢产物调节免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效提供了全面的机制背景。它详细拆解了SCFAs、胆汁酸和色氨酸代谢物三大类关键分子的作用路径，并评估了FMT和代谢物补充等临床干预手段的潜力。对于综述而言，此文是解释“微生物-免疫-治疗”轴心机制的核心素材，特别适用于阐述代谢物如何作为连接微生物组成与宿主免疫反应的桥梁，以及这些机制如何转化为临床获益或面临挑战。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0beefc7af267d256286d6908\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制描述基于文献综述，具体效应可能因癌症类型、药物种类和患者个体差异而异；未提供针对特定实体瘤亚型的定量比较数据。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物代谢物（SCFAs, 胆汁酸, 色氨酸代谢物）影响ICI疗效的具体生物学机制，包括对T细胞、巨噬细胞和树突状细胞的调节。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f94847366c8bcd9dd7211d42\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制多为相关性或体外/动物模型证据，文中明确指出因果关系尚未完全确立；不同代谢物之间的协同或拮抗作用细节有限。\",\"contribution\":\"详细阐述了代谢物介导免疫调节的信号通路（如HDAC抑制、GPCR激活、AhR途径、FXR/TGR5受体），以及这些通路如何重塑肿瘤微环境（TME）和克服耐药性。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5c3357e54a093d51c9d6b2e4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述提出了“微生物代谢物作为宿主-微生物通信的生化介质”这一核心概念，并构建了从微生物组成到免疫调节再到临床疗效的逻辑框架。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ed83ff5b3c75d80d594093a1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"讨论了FMT、益生菌/益生元补充和直接代谢物补充三种主要临床干预途径，指出了各自的潜力（如FMT在非响应者中的效果）和挑战（如标准化、安全性、生物利用度）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0080ff02742ee7644494b4a8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"强调了因果关系验证的必要性（需无菌动物模型和人类代谢组学）、个体异质性（多组学指导个性化）以及代谢物药代动力学知识的不足。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6ef9c7d596b464090047fdaf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"本文是综述文章，其结论基于对已有研究的综合，而非原始实验数据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::caac1d9288cbd3c83470d630\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的机制（如SCFAs促进Treg分化）多为基于特定模型或文献的报道，实际临床效果受多种因素影响，需谨慎外推。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2cd669f9b3de59085c83f213\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"作者明确指出因果关系尚未完全验证，因此在引用其机制解释时，应标注为“潜在机制”或“文献报道的机制”，而非既定事实。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ea50e0d9024c7e55474aa042\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"不同代谢物的作用可能存在情境依赖性（如SCFAs在某些情况下促进M2型巨噬细胞，这可能有利于组织修复但也可能抑制抗肿瘤免疫），需结合具体上下文理解。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5853515f396a502689e442b3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0515\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s016\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0be2b85ecad3848b4b6bd3bb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d75f9e2f8d75e5d4121db45c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a61414ebf37d6e26fb25c8ab\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用系统性文献回顾与综合的方法。作者梳理了关于肠道微生物群组成、功能及其与宿主免疫互作的现有研究，重点归纳了从分子机制（信号通路、代谢途径）到临床前模型证据，再到早期临床试验数据的多层次信息。文章按机制分类（特定菌株、代谢物、生物活性成分、昼夜节律）和组织治疗策略（饮食、FMT、LBPs等）进行逻辑编排，未提供新的原始实验数据，而是对已有证据进行分类、解释和综合评议。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7989217ee9a26ec028a34cad\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"系统整合了肠道微生物群调节ICI疗效的多维机制，包括菌株特异性效应、代谢物介导的信号通路及昼夜节律维度；提供了从基础机制到临床转化策略的全面图谱。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代具体的文献检索策略、纳入排除标准及质量评估方法；主要依赖已发表文献的综合，缺乏对异质性的大规模定量Meta分析；部分结论基于动物模型，临床验证尚处于早期阶段。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bf373bb67b77ec20f45b7a31\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"基于小鼠模型及部分人类队列观察\",\"finding\":\"特定益生菌株（如LGG、B. breve JCM92、C. butyricum）可通过激活DCs、促进CD8+ T细胞浸润或减少Tregs来增强ICI疗效；而某些病原体（如F. nucleatum的不同存在形式）可能通过代谢物介导免疫抑制或局部激活适应性抵抗。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a6217b254e21a2974b6c3c63\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"体外及动物实验机制研究\",\"finding\":\"微生物代谢物（丁酸盐、ICA、肌苷、UB）通过表观遗传修饰、受体激活（AHR, A2aR）等途径直接调节T细胞功能和分化；但某些代谢物（琥珀酸、4-HPA、脱氧胆酸）可诱导MDSCs浸润或Treg积累，导致ICI耐药。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::41de4893349e5dda8838775b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"跨学科理论推导与初步临床观察\",\"finding\":\"肠道微生物群和免疫细胞均具有昼夜节律，干扰节律可能导致代谢紊乱和免疫抑制；同步ICI给药时间与免疫/微生物节律高峰可能提高疗效（时间免疫治疗概念）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::40c304f2af6e24d9727997ce\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2dc8864454dd12af0d85f50c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"解决结直肠癌中大多数MSS患者对ICI治疗原发性耐药的临床困境，探索通过调节肠道微生物群来增强ICI疗效的潜在机制和治疗策略。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::94e811e66263ba6df8d78a76\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"结直肠癌（CRC），特别是微卫星稳定型（MSS）患者对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）的耐药问题；聚焦肠道微生物群及其代谢产物、生物活性成分在调节ICI疗效中的双重作用，以及昼夜节律的影响。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::afe7ad26d480688d4c9f3392\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述，旨在阐明肠道微生物群如何通过特定菌株、代谢物和生物活性成分调节宿主免疫系统，进而影响结直肠癌中ICIs的疗效。文章首先分析了有益菌和致病菌通过抗原呈递、T细胞浸润及免疫抑制细胞调控等机制对ICI反应的双向影响；其次探讨了微生物代谢物（如短链脂肪酸、色氨酸代谢物、肌苷等）作为免疫调节信使的作用；接着引入了肠道微生物群与宿主免疫细胞的昼夜节律交互概念，提出时间免疫治疗的潜力；最后综合了饮食干预、粪便微生物移植（FMT）、益生菌/益生元补充及靶向抗生素等临床转化策略，并评估了其成熟度与挑战。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::45e4d9250c21caec00f4a3d1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为“肠道微生物群如何调节实体瘤ICI疗效”这一核心问题提供了详尽的机制分类框架和临床策略评估。其价值在于将分散的菌株、代谢物和节律研究整合为一个连贯的解释体系，特别适用于构建关于微生物-免疫互作机制的综述章节，并为评估不同干预手段（FMT vs LBPs vs 饮食）的临床证据等级提供参考。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::adea10aba1e36bb84bfa3998\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"多数机制证据来自小鼠模型，人类临床相关性多为相关性研究或早期试验，因果链条在人体内的确证程度不一。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物群影响ICI疗效的具体生物学路径：包括通过DCs成熟、CD8+ T细胞招募/活化、Treg/M2 TAM抑制来增强抗肿瘤免疫，以及通过代谢物诱导MDSCs/Treg来抑制免疫。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b404ca97dff2ff1c948e1bcf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制描述多基于体外或动物实验，部分通路在人体肿瘤微环境中的确切角色尚需更多临床数据支持；不同菌株/代谢物的效应具有高度情境依赖性。\",\"contribution\":\"详细描述了介导效应的具体分子机制：如cGAS/STING通路、HDAC抑制、AHR/A2aR受体信号、TLR4/NF-kB通路等；并区分了不同代谢物（如丁酸盐vs琥珀酸）的相反作用。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::42f9bb5ec25209a85ca2ee7e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"该领域研究处于起步阶段，人体内的具体节律同步策略尚未标准化，证据多为理论推导或小规模观察。\",\"contribution\":\"提出了昼夜节律作为调节微生物-免疫互作的新维度，指出节律紊乱可能导致代谢异常和免疫抑制，而时间给药可能优化疗效。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7122c492de11ff5cd5a81b4e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述中Table 1总结了饮食、FMT、益生菌/益生元、靶向抗生素四种策略的原理、代表物质、临床成熟度（Level 0-2）及挑战。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::002d0d635179c80da9c8da0d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文中提到商业益生菌在黑色素瘤患者中可能与较差的ICI反应相关，强调菌株特异性和定植失败风险。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::073ee8d1f69f6dce1f884a1b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"讨论了厌氧菌的储存、胃酸耐受、制剂技术（包埋、冻干、孢子）等转化障碍。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::731261fac8e7206de02c3682\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述主要聚焦结直肠癌（CRC），虽然提及黑色素瘤等其他实体瘤作为类比，但其核心机制和临床数据主要源于CRC研究，外推至其他实体瘤时需考虑肿瘤微环境的差异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::07a304c9811c3d5e2bf7ad29\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的许多机制（如特定菌株的作用）主要基于小鼠模型，人类体内的复杂生态系统和个体差异可能导致结果不同，需谨慎解读因果性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e29c6b7635fa985315443e61\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"昼夜节律部分多为理论探索和初步证据，尚未形成标准化的临床治疗方案，不应视为既定事实。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::365380f2d431637a3205386a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"对于“超级供体”等概念，综述指出其存在性尚未完全证实，应避免将其作为确定的科学结论引用。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7c5d3e0d3bfbb9f3b3c2811f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0544\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-4dcc7c19ae5301df5638\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-d48cd64bd12b302ad2ba\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-1c552864f10e55d2639d\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-76a4a344a1a9861e53c5\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-57c86dec56d8ae37b5be\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"kind\":\"assets\",\"reason\":\"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\"status\":\"missing\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s003\",\"s139\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::65e45eaeea5f900b2790ecde\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a9fe100ac75a8144b05036a6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d21084f927684cbb0ce741ee\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用前瞻性观察性队列设计。纳入52名计划接受PD-1i治疗的实体瘤患者。在治疗前收集粪便和血液样本，使用UPLC-MS/MS定量分析9种SCFAs及其他代谢物。根据RECIST 1.1标准分类治疗反应（应答者vs非应答者）。使用Mann-Whitney检验比较组间差异，递归分区分析筛选变量，单变量和多变量Cox比例风险模型评估PFS的影响因素（HR及95% CI）。同时，通过逻辑回归分析饮食频率与粪便SCFA浓度的关联。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b2d7a100951317e480d13ca2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"首次报道了粪便SCFAs（特别是丙酸、丁酸等）浓度与实体瘤患者PD-1i疗效及PFS的正向关联，提示SCFAs可能是连接肠道菌群与免疫治疗疗效的桥梁。\",\"limits\":\"样本量较小（N=52），缺乏外部验证队列；未进行肠道微生物组的物种鉴定和多样性分析，因此无法直接证实菌群种类与SCFAs的具体对应关系；饮食数据回顾期为确诊前1年，而非治疗期间，可能存在回忆偏倚或时效性问题；观察性研究设计不能确立因果关系。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f7180273af7c9191b5b89238\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"在52例实体瘤患者队列中，治疗前粪便样本\",\"finding\":\"高浓度的乙酸（HR=0.29）、丙酸（HR=0.08）、丁酸（HR=0.31）和戊酸（HR=0.53）与更长的无进展生存期显著相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cbeaa6220986efc91a30ef25\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"在31例有血浆样本的患者中\",\"finding\":\"高浓度的血浆异戊酸（HR=0.38）与更长的无进展生存期显著相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bed6397bdb547f9d272b8d55\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"多变量Cox回归分析后\",\"finding\":\"仅粪便丙酸浓度被确认为与PFS独立相关的保护因子（HR=0.07）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ead73e1926e3f5b1becac608\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"饮食与代谢物关联分析\",\"finding\":\"高频摄入蘑菇与高粪便丁酸浓度相关；高频摄入绿叶蔬菜和卷心菜与高粪便戊酸浓度相关。高频蘑菇摄入也与较长PFS相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::73469d576c9eb239bfa24a97\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b84796f736c93b0c7fd9d524\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）在多种癌症中有效，但实体瘤患者的响应率相对较低，且肠道微生物组可能影响其疗效，但具体机制尚不明确。本研究试图确定粪便和血浆中的短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）是否与PD-1抑制剂的临床结果相关，从而探索潜在的生物标志物。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3c8903704d3dea1de97915c2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"日本京都大学医院收治的52例接受PD-1抑制剂（纳武利尤单抗或帕博利珠单抗）治疗的实体瘤患者；研究聚焦于治疗前粪便和血浆中短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）浓度与临床疗效及生存期的关联。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::92f11850ff08622857b9bd59\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"该研究是一项前瞻性队列生物标志物研究，旨在评估肠道微生物代谢产物短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）与实体瘤患者PD-1抑制剂疗效之间的关联。研究通过超高效液相色谱-串联质谱法测定了患者治疗前的粪便和血浆样本中的多种SCFA浓度，并结合RECIST 1.1标准将患者分为应答者和非应答者，分析其与无进展生存期（PFS）的关系。同时，研究还探讨了饮食摄入频率与粪便SCFA浓度的关联。结果显示，高浓度的特定粪便SCFAs（乙酸、丙酸、丁酸、戊酸）和血浆异戊酸与较长的PFS显著相关，其中粪便丙酸在多元分析中是独立的保护性因素。此外，蘑菇、绿叶蔬菜和卷心菜的频繁摄入与较高的粪便丁酸和戊酸浓度相关。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::eac369cd2360fda547d02606\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文提供了肠道微生物代谢产物（具体为短链脂肪酸）作为预测实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂疗效的生物标志物的实证证据。它填补了从“菌群存在”到“功能代谢物效应”的研究空白，并初步揭示了饮食-菌群-代谢物-宿主免疫轴的潜在联系。对于综述而言，它是解释“为什么某些菌群特征能改善ICI疗效”的重要功能性机制证据，同时也提供了关于饮食干预潜力的线索。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c3b82e4eb4b3a1a483ad3f86\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅限实体瘤人群；基于单一中心小样本；相关性而非因果性；未涵盖所有SCFA类型。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了粪便SCFAs（乙酸、丙酸、丁酸、戊酸）水平与PD-1i疗效正相关的临床队列证据。高浓度SCFAs对应更长的PFS。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1584fd8515c96dbece42f2f4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制部分主要引用既往文献和本研究的间接证据（如HDAC抑制作用），本研究本身未直接检测免疫细胞亚群或分子通路变化；需结合其他研究确认具体菌种来源。\",\"contribution\":\"提出了SCFAs可能的免疫调节机制：包括诱导Treg分化、增强CD8+ T细胞IFNγ表达、以及通过抑制组蛋白去乙酰化酶（HDACs）上调PD-1配体并增强抗肿瘤免疫。同时指出粪便丙酸是独立的预后因子。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4e5ea4fe8715836b612866b7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"论文指出SCFAs是肠道微生物厌氧发酵膳食纤维的主要终产物，具有广泛的宿主生理影响，并连接了肠道菌群与全身免疫。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ec865036e5d63d9e946b8058\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"发现蘑菇、绿叶蔬菜摄入与特定SCFAs升高相关，且蘑菇摄入与PFS延长相关。但饮食数据滞后于治疗。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ee5bf46901c54558e94fa88e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"使用了UPLC-MS/MS技术定量粪便和血浆中的多种SCFAs，并采用了递归分区分析和多变量Cox模型。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cba0f1c3cc2a2a30d67aecec\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该研究结果为观察性关联，不能推断SCFAs直接导致疗效改善，可能存在混杂因素。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2bded970f646f3fbb86a7f1f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"样本量小且无验证集，结果可能在其他人群中不具普适性，需谨慎外推。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a880fec11ed7e446c934564e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"未分析微生物群落结构，因此无法确定产生这些SCFAs的具体细菌物种，不能替代对菌群组成的研究。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1c27ce2d750eff2ff581a075\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"饮食数据收集时间为确诊前一年，可能无法准确反映治疗期间的实际饮食对当前代谢物水平的影响。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bb0b7562b21a8b09ca03e824\",\"source_handle\":\"P0092\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s155\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a19df6e16abd8a757d7c6611\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"abstract\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e79e30de825ee8d1fd20ddf5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::59b58b6958198ba2be6d0236\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"这是一项单中心、前瞻性观察性研究。纳入标准为接受特定抗PD-1药物（纳武利尤单抗或帕博利珠单抗）治疗的实体瘤患者。主要干预措施为常规药物治疗，研究重点在于基线数据的采集与分析。方法学上，在PD-1抑制剂给药前收集患者粪便样本，使用超高效液相色谱-串联质谱系统定量分析fSCFA。结局指标依据RECIST 1.1标准判定客观缓解情况，将患者分为响应组（R）和非响应组（NR），比较两组间fSCFA水平的差异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8118b11f9d52015ed250b811\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了在实体瘤抗PD-1治疗人群中，基线粪便短链脂肪酸水平与治疗响应之间存在正相关关系的初步证据。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代具体的统计学检验细节（如P值确切数值、置信区间）、fSCFA的具体种类（乙酸、丙酸等）及其各自的变化趋势。样本量较小（n=40），且为单中心研究，可能存在选择偏倚。未提供关于肠道微生物群落结构或其他代谢物的数据，仅聚焦于SCFA这一单一维度。无法确定因果关系，仅能说明关联性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fc101e78cc2732fcbc075244\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"40例实体瘤患者（黑色素瘤19例，头颈部癌7例，胃肠道癌7例，泌尿生殖系统癌4例，其他3例），总响应率为22.5%。响应者9例，非响应者31例。\",\"finding\":\"响应者（R）组的粪便短链脂肪酸（fSCFA）水平显著高于非响应者（NR）组（p值在摘要中未完整显示，但明确指出显著更高）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4120b76283240cea50a8aeb9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::74e70f82c82081f03088a3f8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）在多种癌症中有效，但其疗效存在个体差异。肠道微生物群被认为是影响ICI疗效的因素之一，但肠道微生物群与肿瘤微环境免疫状态之间的关系尚不清楚。本研究具体关注肠道微生物的主要代谢产物——短链脂肪酸（SCFAs），探讨其在抗PD-1治疗中的临床意义。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::856964dc8d1a86bacb24ad8f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"2016年7月至2018年4月在京都大学医院接受抗PD-1抑制剂（纳武利尤单抗或帕博利珠单抗）治疗的实体瘤患者。研究对象包括黑色素瘤、头颈部癌、胃肠道癌、泌尿生殖系统癌及其他类型肿瘤，共40例。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::040dc30caacd5090b419382f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"该研究旨在评估肠道微生物代谢产物短链脂肪酸（SCFA）与实体瘤患者抗PD-1免疫治疗疗效之间的关联。研究采用前瞻性设计，收集患者在给药前的粪便样本，利用超高效液相色谱-串联质谱法分析粪便短链脂肪酸（fSCFA）水平，并根据RECIST 1.1标准将患者分为响应者（R）和非响应者（NR）。结果显示，响应者的fSCFA水平显著高于非响应者，提示fSCFA可能作为预测抗PD-1治疗疗效的生物标志物。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ffa14478b80c6999d1e3ff80\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文为综述提供了关于肠道微生物代谢产物（特别是短链脂肪酸）与免疫检查点抑制剂疗效关联的直接实证数据。它支持“肠道微生物通过代谢产物调节ICI疗效”的假设，并提出了fSCFA作为潜在预测生物标志物的可能性。对于综述而言，它是连接微生物组成/功能与治疗临床结局的重要桥梁证据。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::df6638fa60cf581d1f6279f3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅涉及SCFA，未涵盖其他微生物代谢物或菌群组成细节。样本量有限，且为单中心研究，外推至所有实体瘤或所有ICI药物需谨慎。不能单独证明机制，仅展示表型关联。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物代谢物（SCFA）水平与实体瘤患者抗PD-1治疗响应率相关的直接临床数据。发现响应者的fSCFA水平显著高于非响应者。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::928fcccf0dd4cc0fc2e22e74\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"摘要未提供SCFA影响免疫细胞的具体路径（如HDAC抑制、GPR受体激活等），因此不能用于详细解释分子机制，仅能作为机制研究的起点或背景支持。\",\"contribution\":\"虽然未深入阐述分子机制，但确立了SCFA作为中介变量的可能性，暗示微生物代谢活动可能是连接微生物群与宿主免疫反应的关键环节。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::96650ae6ada537818cc1e6b1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"研究确认了SCFA是肠道微生物的主要代谢产物，并具有广泛的宿主生理影响。这有助于综述中界定“微生物-宿主互作”的具体化学介质。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::832bdc8efdbdbb08b7860380\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提出fSCFA可作为预测抗PD-1治疗疗效的生物标志物。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0ba4ebb6bfaec36ff5d0ef95\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该研究为观察性关联，非因果推断。高fSCFA水平可能与更好的预后相关，但不一定意味着提高fSCFA就能改善疗效。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f4d53629a3b6dc362139a5f2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"样本量小（n=40），且包含多种癌症类型，不同癌种对免疫治疗的反应基础可能不同，合并分析可能掩盖亚组特异性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9df19ff1e9539007ef8f06fc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"摘要中P值不完整，需警惕统计显著性的实际强度。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1dd42a0522b36c0a9380b239\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"仅针对抗PD-1抑制剂，结论不直接适用于CTLA-4等其他类型的免疫检查点抑制剂。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::080344dbde3c280fed799419\",\"source_handle\":\"P0223\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"no complete research body was indexed\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"local source was absent or unreadable\",\"status\":\"partial\"}],\"material_scope\":\"abstract_only\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s116\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2cd5e26b675c9e32ea224a3f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5dc71a485f3ab28808300a3c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3bb10c2c7435ffb9a34b098e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用叙事性综述方法，综合近期临床观察研究、回顾性队列分析以及临床前动物模型数据。按代谢物类别（SCFAs, BCFAs, Tryptophan metabolites, BAs等）和治疗模式（ICI, allo-SCT, CAR-T）两个维度组织材料。重点提取各代谢物的分子机制（如受体结合、表观遗传修饰、信号通路激活）及其在特定临床试验或模型中的表现。对于存在矛盾结果的情况（如SCFAs在不同ICI类型中的不同效应），进行对比分析和情境化解释。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::34a21dd7a8bf45bc9025d7bf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了关于微生物代谢物在三种主要癌症免疫治疗模式（ICI, allo-SCT, CAR-T）中作用的全面机制综述，强调了代谢物作为功能性生物标志物相对于分类学标记的优势。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代具体的文献检索策略、纳入排除标准及偏倚风险评估方法。综述内容混合了临床观察数据和临床前模型，因果关系的确定性受限于观察性研究的性质。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1d2fbe96d54a02fcef32a6d9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"指出了当前临床转化的关键障碍，包括抗生素导致的菌群耗竭、代谢物检测的非标准化、以及个体间微生物组成的异质性。\",\"limits\":\"部分结论基于小样本临床研究或单一动物模型，外推至广泛人群需谨慎。许多潜在的治疗组合（如代谢物联合CAR-T）尚未进入临床试验阶段。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c36d0f92a2f75af5bb33bb48\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"ICI治疗（抗PD-1/PD-L1 vs 抗CTLA-4）\",\"finding\":\"SCFAs（如丁酸、丙酸）对ICI疗效的影响具有双向性和情境依赖性。在抗PD-1治疗中，较高的粪便SCFA水平通常与更好的无进展生存期（PFS）相关；但在抗CTLA-4治疗中，血清SCFA水平升高可能与较差的预后相关，提示不同检查点靶点对代谢物的响应机制不同。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::abae9cd68dfbb32af320a0ad\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"allo-SCT后的移植物抗宿主病（GVHD）\",\"finding\":\"严重GVHD患者表现出粪便和血浆中SCFAs（特别是丁酸）和某些胆汁酸（如3-oxoLCA）的显著降低。低水平的这些代谢物与GVHD发生率和死亡率增加相关。补充UDCA或TUDCA可减轻GVHD严重程度。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::71143331a642e94f3a483408\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"CAR-T细胞疗法\",\"finding\":\"抗生素暴露（特别是针对厌氧菌的广谱抗生素）与CAR-T疗法疗效不佳和不良事件增加有关。血清中特定的代谢物（如戊酸、TMAO、靛基硫酸盐）在CAR-T输注前的高水平与更好的总生存期（OS）和无进展生存期（PFS）相关。戊酸可通过抑制组蛋白去乙酰化酶（HDAC）增强CAR-T细胞的持久性和细胞毒性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3fbf9446f83927446084894d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"色氨酸代谢物（吲哚类）\",\"finding\":\"吲哚-3-甲醛（ICA）等代谢物通过激活芳香烃受体（AHR）和I型干扰素（IFN-I）信号通路，增强CD8+ T细胞功能并改善ICI疗效，同时在小鼠模型中显示能缓解ICI相关的结肠炎。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::845abe9472e11a51d817589f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::05922aee7354f86b7239d986\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"鉴于个体间微生物组差异巨大且抗生素使用普遍，如何理解微生物代谢物在癌症免疫治疗中的具体作用机制？如何利用这些代谢物作为预测性生物标志物或治疗辅助手段，以提高疗效并减少毒性？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3cf9923a6ec65b9cd53067bb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"人类肠道微生物群及其衍生的免疫调节代谢物（IMMs），重点涵盖短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）、支链脂肪酸（BCFAs）、色氨酸代谢物/吲哚、胆汁酸（BAs）、尿石素A（UA）、氧化三甲胺（TMAO）及肌苷等。研究情境包括癌症免疫治疗的主要模式：免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）、异基因造血干细胞移植（allo-SCT）和嵌合抗原受体T细胞（CAR-T）疗法，以及相关的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2a00cee64ac60d24cc389223\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述，系统梳理了肠道微生物群通过其代谢产物调控局部和全身免疫反应，进而影响癌症免疫治疗疗效的机制。文章详细阐述了各类关键代谢物的生物合成途径、作用位点（局部肠道或系统性循环）及其对免疫细胞（如T细胞、巨噬细胞、树突状细胞）和肿瘤微环境（TME）的具体调节机制。同时，综述评估了这些代谢物在不同免疫治疗模式（ICI、allo-SCT、CAR-T）中的临床关联与干预潜力，讨论了从活体生物制品（LBPs）、益生元到后生元（postbiotics）等转化策略的现状与挑战，并提出了未来建立标准化代谢物生物标志物和个性化干预方案的方向。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0e78bdd2f0cc5e069908e3e8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为“肠道微生物群如何调节实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂疗效及其机制”这一主题提供了核心的机制解释素材和临床关联证据。它详细区分了不同代谢物类别的作用路径，并特别指出了代谢物效应的上下文依赖性（如SCFAs在不同ICI靶点下的相反效果），这对于解释临床研究中结果的异质性至关重要。此外，文中提到的Immunomodulatory Metabolite Risk Index (IMM-RI) 和多组学整合思路为生物标志物的开发提供了参考框架。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::873d0fba4e425fd1d58d1f16\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"需注意不同癌症类型（NSCLC/CRC vs 黑色素瘤）和不同ICI靶点（PD-1 vs CTLA-4）之间的效应方向可能相反，不能简单概括为“有益”或“有害”。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了微生物代谢物影响ICI疗效的临床关联证据。例如，在NSCLC和CRC患者中，粪便SCFAs（乙酸、丙酸、丁酸）水平与抗PD-1治疗的响应正相关；而在黑色素瘤抗CTLA-4治疗中，血清丁酸和丙酸与预后负相关。还提到了色氨酸代谢物（如ICA）在黑色素瘤患者中与抗PD-1响应的正相关性。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4b0cb2fc8e9467b3beb920ed\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"多数机制细节来自小鼠模型或体外实验，需明确区分哪些是已验证的人体机制，哪些是推测机制。例如，SCFAs对CTLA-4的负面影响机制主要在动物模型中阐明。\",\"contribution\":\"详细阐述了代谢物介导ICI疗效的具体分子机制。包括：1) SCFAs通过GPR41/43受体信号和HDAC抑制调节Treg和CD8+ T细胞分化；2) 吲哚类代谢物通过AHR和IFN-I信号通路增强抗肿瘤免疫；3) 胆汁酸通过FXR/TGR5受体调节免疫细胞浸润和IFN表达；4) TMAO通过NLRP3炎症小体和IFN-I通路促进M1型巨噬细胞极化。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::04c554ef8e3d4200741aab2e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"主要基于观察性研究和动物模型，人体内的因果关系需结合其他研究进一步确认。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了关于抗生素使用对ICI疗效负面影响的代谢物中介证据。指出广谱抗生素会耗竭产生有益代谢物（如SCFAs、DAT）的厌氧菌，导致代谢物水平下降，从而削弱ICI疗效。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::87df1b467b715a1a15d02967\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述提出了从“分类学导向”向“功能/代谢物导向”转变的观点，认为代谢物比物种丰度更能反映微生物的功能输出，且更稳定、可量化。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cbb3078b73e91f8065511c19\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"讨论了活体生物制品（LBPs）临床试验的失败案例（如SER-401因万古霉素预处理导致丁酸合成受损而失效），以及益生元（如抗性淀粉）和后生元（如UDCA、肌苷）的试验进展。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6a555a910e0f65bc9cd6734c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"对比了代谢物在ICI、allo-SCT和CAR-T疗法中的不同作用重点。ICI侧重TME重塑和T细胞浸润；allo-SCT侧重肠道屏障保护和GVHD预防；CAR-T侧重细胞内在代谢状态和持久性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::750f4003f9e2f3e566d3cc2d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述涵盖多种癌症类型（包括血液肿瘤如淋巴瘤），但用户关注实体瘤。提取证据时需严格筛选仅适用于实体瘤（如NSCLC, CRC, Melanoma, HCC, PDAC）的数据，排除仅涉及血液肿瘤的结论。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8a2bdf55757e485be43fde5e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中强调代谢物效应的“上下文依赖性”，特别是SCFAs在不同ICI类型（PD-1 vs CTLA-4）和不同肿瘤微环境中的双向作用。解读时必须保留这种复杂性，避免单一方向的简化结论。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6859b34486e2b2256197ea59\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"许多机制描述基于临床前模型（小鼠、类器官），在应用于人类临床解释时，需注明其来源限制，区分观察性关联与因果证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3735241add152cdb335b4252\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"抗生素对代谢物的影响是间接的（通过改变菌群），在归因时需明确是“抗生素-菌群-代谢物-疗效”链条，而非抗生素直接作用于代谢物。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6efe5fd5bbc2b90c5944cd7a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0503\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-8c71e871c7aa5482d545\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-f85da31c482f020fe5f7\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-a7a6e9bd3a48b1fef12e\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-12c6cac6a4bef2539d08\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-4e6e3fd8f37ea344363f\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s014\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3c34d43bb2fbb8276518303c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::76108cfa8f06397f625e8bcb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::221c2187ede4977dfa1dadb7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"The authors employ a narrative synthesis approach, organizing the content by metabolite class (SCFAs, Tryptophan metabolites, etc.) and then by therapeutic context (anti-tumor immunity, immunotherapy, chemotherapy). They aggregate findings from cited primary studies (mostly preclinical mouse models and some clinical correlations) to construct mechanistic pathways (e.g., HDAC inhibition, GPCR activation, AHR signaling). The review does not report new experimental data but curates and interprets existing evidence to build a conceptual map of metabolite-mediated immune modulation.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e75a3abec20585306499ff41\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Provides a structured classification of microbial metabolites and their distinct, often opposing, roles in cancer therapy outcomes. It consolidates mechanistic insights (e.g., specific receptors like TLR5, AHR, GPCRs; epigenetic modifications) linking specific metabolites to immune cell phenotypes.\",\"limits\":\"As a narrative review, it aggregates heterogeneous data from various study designs (mouse models, human cohorts, in vitro). It does not perform a systematic meta-analysis. Many mechanistic claims are derived from animal models, and direct translation to human physiology is noted as a challenge. The review acknowledges methodological inconsistencies in microbiome research but does not resolve them.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fc89388ebe329b72b674f50a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"General anti-tumor immunity and immunotherapy contexts\",\"finding\":\"Microbial metabolites act as critical mediators; some enhance anti-tumor immunity (e.g., Butyrate enhancing CD8+ T cell activity via TLR5 or ID2/IL-12 pathways; ILA promoting DC maturation via epigenetic regulation), while others suppress it (e.g., Formate inducing AhR signaling and stemness; Succinic acid inhibiting cGAS-interferon pathway).\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a37833089861a4988eac7fe2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Response to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors (ICIs)\",\"finding\":\"Metabolite levels correlate with ICI efficacy. Butyrate can enhance anti-PD-1 efficacy (via histone acetylation of Pdcd1/Cd28) but may reduce anti-CTLA-4 efficacy (by increasing Tregs). TMAO enhances response to ICIs in pancreatic cancer via Type I IFN pathway. DAT facilitates ICI treatment by boosting IFN-I signaling.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::91b489e62aed13f36a47b130\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Chemotherapy response\",\"finding\":\"3-IAA improves chemotherapy efficacy in pancreatic cancer by increasing ROS accumulation via myeloperoxidase. Lactate produced by intratumoral bacteria can induce chemoradiation resistance. Statins may improve CRC prevention by altering microbiota to increase ILA production.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::53a0e5c59d242df9530832d5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c38c95af14abb4799933f6ba\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"To systematically summarize and analyze the diverse roles of microbial-derived metabolites in shaping anti-tumor immunity and modulating the efficacy of major cancer therapies (immunotherapy and chemotherapy), thereby identifying potential therapeutic targets and biomarkers.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d62a6e78ffa6bd5524f54b6e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"The review focuses on microbial-derived metabolites (specifically SCFAs, tryptophan metabolites, TMAO, urolithins, formate, DAT, and succinic acid) and their regulatory roles in anti-tumor immunity, cancer immunotherapy (particularly immune checkpoint inhibitors), and chemotherapy outcomes across various cancer types.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fb8823d1bac67f48579eecd8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"This is a comprehensive narrative review that synthesizes current literature on how gut microbiota-derived metabolites influence cancer biology and treatment responses. It categorizes key metabolites, detailing their origins, mechanisms of action within the tumor microenvironment (TME), and their specific impacts on immune cell function (e.g., CD8+ T cells, Tregs, macrophages). The review highlights both beneficial effects (enhancing immunotherapy efficacy, sensitizing tumors to chemotherapy) and detrimental effects (inducing resistance, promoting immunosuppression), providing a mechanistic framework for understanding microbiome-immune-tumor interactions.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a91efcf335aaa13a883e57b3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"This review serves as a high-level mechanistic map for the user's综述, specifically addressing how gut microbiome metabolites modulate immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) efficacy in solid tumors. It provides concrete examples of metabolites that either sensitize tumors to ICIs (e.g., Butyrate/PD-1, TMAO/PD-1, DAT/CTLA-4) or confer resistance (e.g., Butyrate/CTLA-4, Succinic acid/PD-1). It offers detailed molecular mechanisms (receptors, signaling pathways, epigenetic changes) that can be used to answer the 'how' and 'what mechanisms' facets of the user's query.\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::06e260e6ced336c2a4cf02b7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Most evidence comes from mouse models (e.g., Kang et al., Wang et al., Joachim et al.). Human clinical data is often correlational (e.g., Zhu et al. on serum butyrate and PD-1 expression). Causality in humans is not fully established.\",\"contribution\":\"Identifies specific metabolites associated with improved or reduced ICI efficacy. For example, it links Butyrate to enhanced anti-PD-1 response (via H3K27ac) but reduced anti-CTLA-4 response (via Treg induction). It also links TMAO and DAT to enhanced ICI responses, while Succinic acid and Formate are linked to resistance.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1b75395d66392d4c131fbb5a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Mechanisms are often described in isolated cell types or mouse models. The complexity of the TME means these single-pathway descriptions may not capture all interactions. Some mechanisms (e.g., Butyrate's dual role) depend on context (ICI type, dose, timing).\",\"contribution\":\"Details the molecular mechanisms: Butyrate acts via HDAC inhibition, GPCR activation (HCA2), TLR5 binding, and epigenetic regulation of Cd28/Pdcd1. TMAO activates PERK kinase and Type I IFN pathway. DAT activates IFN-I signaling. Succinic acid inhibits cGAS-interferon-beta pathway. ILA regulates epigenetic marks (H3K27ac) on IL12a enhancers.\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::190d11ca380f707b36b51f06\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Overview of SCFA, Tryptophan, and other metabolite classes; general discussion of gut microbiota health and disease.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e551fc0cca5ffe01ac4c1234\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Succinic acid inhibiting cGAS pathway; Formate inducing AhR/stemness; Lactate inducing chemoradiation resistance.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::18ac47da3c3906dc22d3f12a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Discussion on standardization of sampling, sequencing technologies, and inter-individual variability.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5241863596df9f36cf313abc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The review covers multiple cancer types (CRC, TNBC, PDAC, NSCLC, Melanoma). Effects of metabolites may be cancer-type specific (e.g., TMAO benefit in TNBC/PDAC vs. general cardiovascular risks). Do not generalize findings across all solid tumors without noting context.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e31645d6a0093fce292194f4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Many mechanistic claims are based on murine models. Direct extrapolation to human clinical efficacy requires caution.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b000af9ca97720e495011227\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Butyrate has contradictory effects depending on the ICI target (beneficial for PD-1, potentially detrimental for CTLA-4). This nuance is critical for accurate interpretation.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b7bcd2437af8ba6ed5e822e5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0559\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-ff810900b7e604c42248\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-0bb63c7811be02b5f16f\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"kind\":\"assets\",\"reason\":\"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\"status\":\"missing\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s175\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2c356367c59dffb2c0b331e8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"abstract\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::94b51d5c268bf7c6648403d1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::af7229e313c22cc9f45f4fc4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"文献综述与综合评议。作者通过梳理现有研究，归纳SCFAs的分子作用机制（HDAC抑制、GPCR激活等）、生物学效应（抗肿瘤、免疫调节）以及临床干预手段（益生菌、FMT等）的证据，并对特定代谢物（如丁酸盐）的功能复杂性进行辨析。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5282d638f57d10663cf8fb0a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了SCFAs在肺癌中从分子机制到临床效应的综合框架，特别是明确了其作为免疫检查点抑制剂增效剂和放化疗减毒剂的潜力。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代具体的文献检索策略、纳入排除标准及证据等级评估方法；对于“双重性”的具体实验数据或临床案例未提供细节；未明确区分不同SCFA种类（如乙酸、丙酸、丁酸）的具体差异贡献。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::dca3f3ee3415a7493c6fdfe2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"一般机制层面\",\"finding\":\"SCFAs通过抑制组蛋白去乙酰化酶、激活G蛋白偶联受体和代谢重编程发挥作用；直接抑制肿瘤生长、诱导凋亡、抑制血管生成并调节上皮-间质转化。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::de8de63fd7881b2d15e7a917\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"联合治疗情境\",\"finding\":\"SCFAs能增强免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）的治疗效果，并通过维持黏膜屏障和恢复全身免疫稳态，降低放疗和化疗的毒性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0b8c8a72e713a31e54433651\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"特定条件/代谢物（丁酸盐）\",\"finding\":\"丁酸盐具有高度双重性功能：通常起保护作用，但在某些治疗条件下可能赋予多重耐药性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::614a0e82106eef28a63438d7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3dbd8d7f9f04dae46cc98795\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"阐明短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）作为肠道微生物群与宿主之间的关键介质，在肺癌发生发展及治疗响应中的具体作用机制、临床效应及潜在的双向矛盾，以解决基于微生物群的疗法在转化医学中的难题。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::322b0ca67418365c815fd350\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"肺肿瘤（lung cancer）患者肠道微生物群产生的短链脂肪酸（SCFAs），重点探讨其在肿瘤生长控制、药物反应及免疫调节中的作用。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::da43f420ae95b42b0ee3b374\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述文章聚焦于由肠道菌群发酵膳食纤维产生的短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）在肺癌治疗中的新兴重要性。文章系统梳理了SCFAs的作用机制，包括抑制组蛋白去乙酰化酶、激活G蛋白偶联受体以及代谢重编程。内容涵盖了SCFAs对肿瘤的直接影响（如抑制生长、诱导凋亡、抑制血管生成和调节上皮-间质转化），以及其通过维持黏膜屏障和恢复全身免疫稳态来增强免疫检查点抑制剂疗效并降低放化疗毒性的间接作用。此外，文章特别指出了丁酸盐功能的双重性及其带来的临床转化挑战，并评估了益生菌、粪菌移植等靶向SCFAs的治疗策略。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::042b9e5164c0be2d02dce89e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文为综述“肠道微生物群如何调节实体瘤中免疫检查点抑制剂疗效”及其机制提供了重要的代谢中介视角。它具体指出了短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）作为连接肠道菌群与宿主免疫/肿瘤微环境的关键分子，不仅直接作用于肿瘤细胞，还通过系统性免疫调节增强ICI疗效并改善治疗安全性。同时，其关于丁酸盐双重性的讨论为理解治疗反应的异质性提供了重要背景。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fbfea1c18fda8d9c8fcd5119\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"主要局限于肺癌模型或论述，且侧重于代谢物介导的免疫调节，未涵盖所有菌群-免疫互作机制（如抗原模拟等）。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了SCFAs增强免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的具体路径：通过维持黏膜屏障和恢复全身免疫稳态。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c4ad974ae4c0c7f44cf3d967\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制描述较为概括，未提供针对特定实体瘤类型的特异性机制对比；未区分不同SCFA分子的机制差异。\",\"contribution\":\"详细列出了SCFAs介导效应的分子机制：抑制组蛋白去乙酰化酶、激活GPCRs、代谢重编程；以及细胞层面的效应：抑制生长、诱导凋亡、抑制血管生成、调节EMT。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f75b19ebecd7bf5b7a6a0fc7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"摘要未说明导致耐药的具体“治疗条件”是什么，也未提供确证的因果链条，仅为一种需要解决的挑战或观察到的现象。\",\"contribution\":\"提出了丁酸盐功能的“双重性”概念：通常保护但可能在特定条件下导致多重耐药。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3be4c4c384dcac14c77b0e68\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提及益生菌、粪菌移植（FMT）和设计微生物群落作为靶向SCFAs的治疗手段。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9bf1152b9fff56433234d681\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"SCFAs通过维持黏膜屏障和恢复免疫稳态降低放化疗毒性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6ab329e0436bead3b5718546\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该材料为综述性质，其结论依赖于所引用的原始研究，需警惕将综述作者的概括视为未经证实的共识。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c2ba939063b3874e7f6f9939\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"关于丁酸盐“双重性”的描述需谨慎使用，摘要未提供导致耐药的具体条件或证据强度，不能据此断定丁酸盐必然导致耐药。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f3171c51e802e7ffae66fb82\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"研究对象明确为“肺肿瘤”，在应用于其他实体瘤时需注意外推风险，尽管机制可能有共性，但临床效应可能因肿瘤类型而异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d601cedc32b314c83ebf7fe2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"摘要未交代具体的文献筛选过程和证据质量评估，因此其声称的“proven role”应理解为作者对现有文献的综合判断，而非绝对的确证。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::521794f70967c2b23bfeee44\",\"source_handle\":\"P0377\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"no complete research body was indexed\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"html\",\"reason\":\"html_empty\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\"status\":\"partial\"}],\"material_scope\":\"abstract_only\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s137\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::58bcf0fbc5e7b379f8595177\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::83ff6813e1f78d197362acb6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8f2d21d8fee37488d3078ceb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用系统性文献综述方法。1. **分类梳理**：将代谢物按功能分为促进肿瘤进展和抑制肿瘤进展两类，并按信号通路（MAPK, PI3K/Akt/mTOR, NFκB, Wnt/β-catenin）和免疫调节机制进行归类。2. **对比分析**：重点对比同一代谢物在不同癌症类型、不同浓度或不同免疫微环境下的相反作用（矛盾功能）。3. **临床转化关联**：将基础机制研究与临床治疗手段（放疗、化疗、免疫治疗）相结合，分析代谢物对现有疗法疗效和副作用的影响。4. **策略总结**：归纳基于代谢物调控的新型治疗干预措施及其优缺点。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::49ffd73edb65a3456c498074\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物代谢物在癌症进展和治疗中作用的全面分类框架，详细列出了涉及的关键信号通路（MAPK, PI3K/Akt, NFκB, Wnt）和免疫细胞亚群。\",\"limits\":\"作为综述，其结论依赖于所引用的原始研究，未提供新的实验数据验证所有机制。对于某些代谢物的矛盾功能，原文指出需进一步探究因果机制，目前多为观察性关联。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1dcffce52796ea372a267e47\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"明确了特定代谢物（如SCFAs, LCA, Inosine, TMAO）在不同癌症类型和微环境条件下的双向调节作用，强调了情境依赖性。\",\"limits\":\"部分机制描述较为概括，例如TMAO的具体抗癌机制被标记为“尚未完全阐明”，且不同研究间可能存在异质性，综述未深入探讨这些差异的来源。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fc52ea176053f9bf9c00ccf7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"总结了基于代谢物调控的新型治疗策略（饮食、噬菌体、FMT、合成生物学等），并评估了其优势和挑战。\",\"limits\":\"许多新型策略（如合成生物学工程菌、噬菌体联合疗法）仍处于早期研究阶段，临床应用的可行性和安全性尚待大规模临床试验证实。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f56da8af01dd158236d62743\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"生理浓度下；结肠癌\",\"finding\":\"短链脂肪酸（SCFAs，如丁酸盐）通过抑制组蛋白去乙酰化酶（HDAC）和激活GPCRs，抑制结肠癌进展，促进Treg分化，抑制Th17。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2c694f52856386f670af88cb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"非酒精性脂肪肝相关肝细胞癌（NAFLD-HCC）；高浓度\",\"finding\":\"SCFAs水平显著升高时，可能超过宿主耐受阈值，通过增加Tregs比例和损害CD8+ T细胞功能，促进肿瘤进展。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e3b83737f287b84dd75ba66d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"存在外源性IFN-γ和共刺激信号\",\"finding\":\"肌苷（Inosine）结合T细胞表面的A2AR，促进Th1分化，增强抗肿瘤免疫。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2f283cdde31560b336c23f86\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"缺乏外源性IFN-γ\",\"finding\":\"肌苷（Inosine）通过A2AR抑制Th1和Th2细胞的分化，削弱抗肿瘤免疫。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9c50dcbedc9f76ceeed7af5e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"结直肠癌\",\"finding\":\"石胆酸（LCA）激活ERK1/2并诱导miR21，抑制PTEN，促进IL-8分泌，加速肿瘤进展。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::77c3dc6ef72d4150427da369\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"肾母细胞瘤和乳腺癌MCF-7细胞\",\"finding\":\"LCA结合GPBAR1受体，诱导细胞凋亡，发挥抑癌作用。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4067817483e6c7f81773da5f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"接受抗PD-1/PD-L1治疗的黑色素瘤患者\",\"finding\":\"responders体内粪便和血浆中SCFAs浓度显著高于non-responders，提示SCFAs可能影响免疫检查点阻断疗法的疗效。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::67346ea6e9c87818703107a5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"伊立替康治疗\",\"finding\":\"肠道微生物β-葡萄糖醛酸酶将无活性的SN-38G转化为有毒性的SN-38，导致严重腹泻，限制化疗疗效。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c9c91ffe4097177005ed7266\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::42a8d7d145acafeefeb67e2a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"旨在解决肠道微生物代谢物在癌症发生发展及治疗响应中扮演的复杂角色尚不明确的问题，特别是其双重/矛盾功能及具体分子机制。目的是为未来科学研究提供新思路，并探索利用代谢物改善癌症治疗的潜在策略。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7aa315b711ede69909f5c8d2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"肠道微生物群衍生的代谢物（Gut microbiota-derived metabolites）在肿瘤进展（Tumor Progression）和癌症治疗（Cancer Therapy）中的作用。涵盖多种癌症类型（如结肠癌、肝癌、乳腺癌等），重点讨论代谢物对肿瘤微环境（TME）、信号通路及免疫细胞的影响，以及其在放化疗和免疫治疗中的调节作用。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8050b9f4e149b36a2ef8c37c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述系统总结了肠道微生物代谢物与癌症之间的关联。首先阐述了代谢物如何通过重塑肿瘤微环境和调节关键信号通路（如MAPK, PI3K/Akt, NFκB, Wnt）来影响肿瘤进展，既包括促癌作用也包括抑癌作用。其次，分析了代谢物如何调节化疗药物（如伊立替康、吉西他滨）的疗效和毒性，以及如何增强或削弱免疫检查点阻断疗法（ICB）的效果。文章特别指出了部分代谢物（如短链脂肪酸SCFAs、石胆酸LCA、肌苷Inosine）具有情境依赖性的矛盾功能（Paradoxical Functions）。最后，综述了基于代谢物的新型治疗策略，包括饮食干预、噬菌体疗法、粪菌移植（FMT）、合成生物学改造及益生菌/益生元应用。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0d513eb6cff96cd4c9bec6bf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物如何通过代谢物调节免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在实体瘤中的疗效提供了丰富的机制素材和背景信息。它详细列举了促进ICI疗效（如SCFAs、肌苷、MDP）和阻碍ICI疗效（如SCFAs在某些情况下、吲哚类代谢物）的具体代谢物及其作用路径，并讨论了克服耐药性的策略（如FMT）。此外，它还涵盖了代谢物对化疗药物代谢的影响，可作为对比或补充材料。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6798a44a963a8960414fb94a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"主要基于已发表的观察性研究和部分机制研究，部分关联（如SCFAs与ICI响应的统计相关性）的详细机制仍需进一步阐明。不同癌症类型中代谢物的作用可能不同，需注意适用范围。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了微生物代谢物调节ICI疗效的具体实例和方向。例如，指出接受抗PD-1治疗的响应者体内SCFAs水平较高；肌苷在特定条件下增强抗CTLA-4和抗PD-1抗体疗效；Enterococcus肽聚糖产物MDP通过NOD2激活NFκB增强抗肿瘤能力；TMAO增强胰腺癌对ICB的反应。同时也提到了SCFAs可能在转移性黑色素瘤中限制抗CTLA-4抗体功能的反面证据。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::723d64302b82cfc9ce8e48f3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制描述多基于体外细胞实验或动物模型（如小鼠），直接外推到人体需谨慎。部分机制（如TMAO的具体通路）仍被作者标记为“未完全阐明”。\",\"contribution\":\"详细描述了代谢物介导ICI疗效的分子机制。包括：1. SCFAs通过抑制HDAC、调节mTOR活性增强T细胞功能；2. 肌苷通过A2AR-cAMP-PKA通路促进Th1分化，并抑制UBA6稳定MHC I和PD-L1；3. MDP通过NOD2-NFκB通路激活巨噬细胞和T细胞；4. 吲哚类代谢物通过AhR抑制TAMs功能从而抑制CD8+ T细胞；5. FMT通过改变血清次级胆汁酸水平克服耐药。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a8bf25585c4571d85531e094\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这部分内容主要针对化疗，与ICI的直接关联较弱，除非综述主题包含广义的癌症治疗反应。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了关于微生物代谢物影响化疗药物疗效和毒性的背景信息，特别是伊立替康和吉西他滨的代谢机制。指出微生物酶（如β-葡萄糖醛酸酶、胞苷脱氨酶）可激活或失活化疗药物，导致耐药性或严重副作用。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5ec9285b20b9ff6fc226fa12\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"SCFAs、LCA、Inosine、TMAO等在特定条件下促癌或在另一条件下抑癌的实例。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::545b61b8421560b0362c5c95\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Table 3中总结的策略及其优缺点。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::68eb3b98e486895c162812f2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"代谢物对Treg, Th17, CD8+ T, NK cells, TAMs等免疫细胞分化和功能的影响。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ed1356ff45fc83f17beb7289\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述涵盖多种癌症类型，但用户关注的实体瘤（Solid Tumours）中，结肠癌、肝癌、乳腺癌、胰腺癌等有较多提及，而血液肿瘤较少。需注意区分不同癌种的特异性结果。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::81ec6b60fbc4d93dc3f3cf61\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的许多机制来自动物模型（如小鼠）或细胞系，直接应用于人类临床需谨慎，特别是剂量和微环境差异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f4d16feb32d78c286609459c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"对于“矛盾功能”的描述，应理解为情境依赖而非绝对的对立，避免断章取义。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4edf2afc7351603dca62b6ab\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"综述中提到的某些代谢物（如TMAO）的作用机制尚不完全清楚，引用时应保留不确定性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e871fb136070113d30129be3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"不要将综述中提到的“建议后续研究”当作已证实的结论。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e8265a2c39a6736bc4a202cf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0220\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s226\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9d739547675bf1f029cb7f80\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4934f29df0db2e522a57309c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::396dfedaa89b32ffd21f5639\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"1. 代谢组学筛选：对接受抗PD-1/抗CTLA-4联合治疗的B16-F0荷瘤小鼠血浆进行非靶向代谢组学分析；重分析人肾细胞癌（RCC）患者CheckMate 025临床试验的血浆代谢数据。 2. 体内药效学评估：在B16-F0（敏感）、B16-GMCSF（抵抗）和4T1（抵抗）小鼠模型中，评估单独使用肌苷、ICB或两者联合治疗的肿瘤生长和生存率。 3. 单细胞转录组与流式细胞术：对4T1肿瘤浸润免疫细胞进行scRNA-seq和流式分析，评估免疫微环境（TIME）的变化（如CD8+ T细胞、巨噬细胞极化）。 4. 体外共培养与机制验证：建立T细胞介导的肿瘤细胞杀伤实验，区分肌苷对T细胞和肿瘤细胞的直接作用；使用LiP-SMap化学蛋白质组学筛选肌苷结合蛋白；通过CRISPR筛选和基因敲除验证UBA6的功能。 5. 生化与分子机制：体外纯化UBA6和USE1蛋白，检测肌苷对UBA6-USE1相互作用及FAT10硫酯键形成的影响；通过RNA-seq和Western Blot分析UBA6缺失对炎症信号和抗原呈递的影响。 6. 临床相关性分析：利用TIDE数据库和自建的人体组织队列（食管癌、肺癌等），分析UBA6表达水平与ICB疗效、患者生存期及CD8+ T细胞浸润的关系。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f8623759d31182c3e5688409\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"识别出肌苷作为连接肠道微生物/代谢与ICB疗效的关键代谢物，并揭示其通过直接抑制肿瘤细胞UBA6来增强肿瘤内在免疫原性的新机制。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代肌苷在人体内的药代动力学细节及最佳给药剂量；所给摘要未交代肌苷对非嘌呤代谢途径或其他潜在脱靶效应的全面评估；临床验证队列规模较小（n=22用于IHC，部分公共数据），且缺乏对患者内源性肌苷水平的直接测量（因腺苷快速降解为肌苷，测量存在技术挑战）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c55e555eb32db1921348363a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"B16-F0小鼠模型及人RCC患者队列\",\"finding\":\"ICB治疗后血浆中嘌呤代谢物（包括肌苷）水平升高；在人RCC患者中，基线高水平肌苷与尼莫单抗（anti-PD1）治疗后的更长总生存期（mOS 33 vs 22个月）相关，但与mTOR抑制剂无关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b88c7cca77869597d719c9d5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"B16-GMCSF和4T1小鼠模型（ICB抵抗模型）\",\"finding\":\"肌苷补充剂与ICB联合治疗克服了内在耐药性，显著延长生存期并诱导完全缓解；肌苷不引起系统性炎症或肝毒性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::65aff76b39d92549f8641eec\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"4T1肿瘤微环境\",\"finding\":\"肌苷+ICB组合治疗将免疫抑制性TIME转化为炎症性TIME，增加M1型巨噬细胞、效应CD8+ T细胞比例，减少M2型巨噬细胞和Treg。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9a27e1609bb7eff8810d2f34\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"体外T细胞-肿瘤细胞共培养\",\"finding\":\"肌苷预处理肿瘤细胞而非T细胞，显著增强肿瘤细胞对T细胞介导的细胞毒性的敏感性；肌苷上调肿瘤细胞表面MHC-I表达及抗原加工/呈递相关基因。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::738f3bcda3e274730a37d403\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"LiP-SMap筛选与CRISPR筛选\",\"finding\":\"肌苷直接结合并抑制UBA6活性；UBA6缺失使肿瘤细胞对T细胞和NK细胞介导的杀伤更敏感。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ef496a9b4a88daae4f841123\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"UBA6功能缺失模型\",\"finding\":\"UBA6缺失模拟肌苷效应，上调TNF-α、IFN响应基因及MHC-I表达；UBA6缺失消除了肌苷对基因表达的进一步诱导作用，表明肌苷通过抑制UBA6发挥作用。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::69e97b9a59ffba6e35ecb95f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"不同肿瘤细胞系（MC38 vs 4T1/B16）\",\"finding\":\"肌苷仅在高表达UBA6的肿瘤细胞（4T1, B16）中增强免疫原性；在低表达UBA6的MC38细胞中无效，但在过表达UBA6的MC38细胞中恢复效应。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ae4d00fb49f9bc51ac7600ee\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"人类肿瘤队列（黑色素瘤、NSCLC等）\",\"finding\":\"肿瘤细胞中高UBA6表达与ICB治疗后的较差无进展生存期（PFS）和总生存期（OS）相关；低UBA6表达与较高的客观缓解率（ORR）和CD8+ T细胞浸润正相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f03c7ae90d3d5790e2cd05c1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b4fff44f5f224025776a35f4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管免疫检查点阻断（ICB）疗法在某些癌症中取得显著成效，但大多数患者无响应或产生耐药性。肿瘤内在因素（如低突变负荷、局部免疫抑制）和宿主因素导致响应异质性。具体而言，肿瘤代谢环境的改变如何调节抗肿瘤免疫反应并影响ICB疗效？特别是肠道微生物群产生的代谢物是否通过特定分子机制直接作用于肿瘤细胞以克服内在耐药性？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::af5d41b91f81e7f88d8672b8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"小鼠黑色素瘤（B16-F0, B16-GMCSF）和三阴性乳腺癌（4T1）模型，以及人类肾细胞癌（CheckMate 025队列）、黑色素瘤和实体瘤篮式试验患者队列。研究聚焦于免疫检查点阻断（ICB）治疗下的肿瘤代谢微环境与内在免疫原性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a67cc1373019bb00b465e85c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本研究旨在阐明肿瘤代谢状态如何影响免疫检查点阻断（ICB）的疗效。通过小鼠模型的代谢组学筛选和临床队列分析，发现嘌呤代谢物肌苷（inosine）水平与ICB敏感性正相关。机制研究表明，肌苷直接抑制肿瘤细胞内的泛素激活酶UBA6，从而增强肿瘤细胞的抗原呈递能力和对T细胞介导的细胞毒性的敏感性，进而改善抗肿瘤免疫反应。该通路在多种ICB抵抗的小鼠模型中验证了肌苷联合ICB的治疗潜力，并在人类肿瘤样本中证实了UBA6高表达与不良预后及低CD8+ T细胞浸润的相关性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cc0e5e2d630e43e2fb9bdbae\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文提供了关于肠道微生物群衍生代谢物（肌苷）如何通过直接靶向肿瘤细胞内在机制（UBA6抑制）来增强免疫检查点抑制剂（ICB）疗效的具体证据。它填补了“微生物代谢物-肿瘤细胞内在属性-免疫响应”这一链条中的关键分子机制空白，特别强调了肿瘤细胞并非被动受体，而是通过代谢感应主动调节其免疫原性。这对于解释为何某些微生物组成有利于ICB响应，以及如何通过代谢干预克服肿瘤内在耐药性具有重要参考价值。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::553895acd68d4c0b06a1ddba\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"主要基于小鼠模型和有限的临床队列；肌苷的来源不仅限于肠道微生物（也可由癌细胞分泌），需结合其他文献明确其在不同情境下的主要来源。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肌苷（一种由肠道微生物群产生或受其影响的代谢物）与ICB疗效正相关的临床和体内证据。展示了肌苷水平可作为预测ICB响应的生物标志物。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0f83e7bc4d3b58656458d42e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制主要在黑色素瘤和乳腺癌模型中验证；UBA6在其他类型实体瘤中的作用可能不同（如MC38结肠癌模型中UBA6低表达导致肌苷无效）。\",\"contribution\":\"揭示了肌苷增强ICB疗效的具体分子机制：直接结合并抑制肿瘤细胞内的UBA6（泛素激活酶），从而解除其对炎症信号和抗原呈递通路的抑制，增强肿瘤细胞对T细胞介导杀伤的敏感性。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d6f2c080372a18438124a4d3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"UBA6作为靶点的普适性需在不同肿瘤类型中进一步验证；目前证据显示其效果依赖于肿瘤细胞的基础UBA6表达水平。\",\"contribution\":\"证明了UBA6是肿瘤内在的免疫检查点，其高表达导致免疫抑制性微环境和ICB耐药，而UBA6缺失或抑制可逆转这一过程。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a405723c3547b12ae18c0c63\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"论文指出肿瘤代谢环境改变（如营养短缺、腺苷积累）导致免疫抑制性TME，而肌苷作为腺苷代谢物，其水平受肠道微生物群失调影响。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c26e2b1b9b5510743ab26c53\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"肌苷在B16和4T1模型中有效，但在低UBA6表达的MC38模型中无效；肌苷不直接作用于T细胞，而是作用于肿瘤细胞。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::87c42055f780c5f40261519f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"肌苷作为膳食补充剂已长期使用，安全性良好；UBA6表达可作为预测ICB疗效的生物标志物。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bc6b57f494bd389836ec9257\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"肌苷的来源具有多源性（肠道微生物、饮食、癌细胞自身），本论文侧重于其作为循环代谢物对肿瘤细胞的直接作用，解读时需区分其与肠道微生物群的间接联系与直接靶向关系。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8c03a2c7f2fcb1164d5f8077\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"UBA6的作用具有肿瘤类型特异性，不能将其在所有实体瘤中的功能外推至所有情况，需注意不同肿瘤细胞系中UBA6基础表达水平的差异对治疗效果的决定性影响。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c72d9b498e6ac469eba1251b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"临床数据的局限性：人类队列中未直接测量肌苷水平（因技术困难），主要依赖UBA6表达作为下游效应指标，解读临床相关性时需保留这一推断性质。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1d38ce2464cb72745cdabef7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"deep_read_material\",\"current_question_material\"],\"value\":{\"examples\":[{\"attribution\":\"本研究\",\"conditions\":\"使用4T1细胞裂解液进行LiP-SMap筛选；使用HEK293细胞和纯化蛋白进行体外相互作用及硫酯活性测定；使用CRISPR敲除UBA6的4T1和B16-GMCSF肿瘤细胞系进行功能验证。\",\"finding\":\"通过LiP-SMap化学蛋白质组学筛选，在4T1细胞裂解物中鉴定出23个与肌苷结合的候选蛋白，其中仅UBA6的缺失能显著增强T细胞介导的肿瘤杀伤。体外生化实验证实，肌苷直接减少UBA6与其特异性E2酶USE1之间的相互作用，并降低UBA6介导的FAT10硫酯键形成活性。此外，删除UBA6的泛素折叠结构域（UFD）可消除肌苷对UBA6-USE1相互作用的抑制作用，且UBA6缺失消除了肌苷对T细胞介导肿瘤杀伤的增敏效应，表明肌苷通过直接抑制UBA6活性来增强肿瘤免疫原性。\",\"reference_ids\":[],\"use_in_review\":\"提供肌苷抑制UBA6的具体分子机制证据，包括结合筛选、生化验证及功能回补实验，证明肌苷通过直接靶向肿瘤细胞内的UBA6发挥作用。\"},{\"attribution\":\"本研究\",\"conditions\":\"分析CheckMate 025临床试验中394名接受纳武利尤单抗治疗和349名接受依维莫司治疗的RCC患者的血浆代谢谱；以代谢物中位数分组比较OS。\",\"finding\":\"在CheckMate 025肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列中，接受纳武利尤单抗（抗PD-1）治疗的患者的血浆肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）呈正相关：高肌苷组中位OS为33个月，低肌苷组为22个月；而在接受依维莫司（mTOR抑制剂）治疗的患者中无此关联。这表明高水平肌苷能为接受ICB治疗的患者带来持久的生存获益。\",\"reference_ids\":[\"R15\"],\"use_in_review\":\"提供血浆肌苷水平与接受ICB治疗患者生存期关联的临床队列数据，确立肌苷作为ICB疗效生物标志物的临床相关性。\"},{\"attribution\":\"本研究\",\"conditions\":\"基于文献综述和讨论部分的逻辑推断，结合研究中提到的腺苷半衰期短、肌苷半衰期长的药代动力学特征，以及未能直接在患者肿瘤组织中测量肌苷的事实。\",\"finding\":\"讨论部分指出，尽管肌苷是腺苷的代谢产物且循环水平受饮食、基因和药物影响，但腺苷在体内可迅速降解为肌苷（约10秒）并在血浆中快速清除（约30秒），而肌苷的生物半衰期较长（约15小时）。由于样本缺失，研究未能在其临床队列中验证肌苷测量或转录组分析。这提示在评估TME中肌苷的实际有效浓度时，需考虑其前体腺苷的不稳定性以及局部摄取机制（如ENT转运体）的作用，目前TME内肌苷的具体浓度缺口及其对UBA6抑制效率的影响尚待进一步解析。\",\"reference_ids\":[\"R55\",\"R56\"],\"use_in_review\":\"补充说明肌苷在肿瘤微环境（TME）中的浓度缺口或来源限制，指出虽然肌苷由肠道菌群产生并可进入循环，但其在TME局部的具体浓度动态及测量受限于腺苷的快速降解，暗示TME内有效肌苷浓度的维持可能存在挑战。\"}],\"explanation\":\"本研究提出并验证了一个由肌苷调控的UBA6依赖性通路，该通路控制肿瘤的内在免疫原性，进而影响免疫检查点阻断（ICB）的敏感性。核心机制在于：肌苷作为一种嘌呤代谢物，能够直接进入肿瘤细胞（通过ENT转运体而非腺苷受体），并直接结合和抑制泛素激活酶UBA6的活性。UBA6不仅激活泛素，还激活泛素样蛋白FAT10。肌苷通过干扰UBA6与E2酶USE1的结合，抑制了UBA6介导的FAT10硫酯键形成。UBA6活性的降低导致肿瘤细胞内炎症信号通路（如TNF-α、IFN-γ响应基因）和抗原加工/呈递相关基因的上调，从而增加MHC-I表达和肿瘤免疫原性。这种增强的免疫原性使肿瘤细胞对CD8+ T细胞介导的细胞毒性更加敏感，从而克服肿瘤内在的ICB耐药性。临床数据显示，患者血浆中高水平的肌苷以及肿瘤组织中低水平的UBA6表达均与接受ICB治疗后的良好预后（更长的OS/PFS和更高的客观缓解率）相关。\",\"question_id\":\"Q01\",\"remaining_points\":[\"TME中肌苷的具体局部浓度及其动态变化尚未量化，特别是考虑到腺苷到肌苷的快速转化及清除过程。\",\"肌苷抑制UBA6后，下游具体的泛素化/FAT10化底物蛋白及其如何具体调控MHC-I上调的详细分子路径仍需进一步阐明。\",\"不同癌症类型中UBA6表达基线差异对肌苷疗效预测价值的普适性需更大规模队列验证。\"]},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::77a7c6680577591119371633\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"deep_read_material\",\"paper_title\"],\"value\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e59d863567105425ca3bb22b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"deep_read_material\",\"plain_text\"],\"value\":\"\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f22829882f9d6376fc3f8adc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"deep_read_material\",\"prior_question_material\"],\"value\":{\"examples\":[{\"attribution\":\"Li et al. (2019) / CheckMate 025 队列分析\",\"conditions\":\"人群：接受Nivolumab或Everolimus治疗的晚期肾细胞癌患者；分组依据：基线血浆肌苷水平的中位数分为高/低两组；指标：总生存期（OS）。\",\"finding\":\"在肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列（CheckMate 025试验，Nivolumab治疗组 n=394, Everolimus对照组 n=349）中，通过非靶向代谢组学分析发现，只有肌苷水平与免疫检查点阻断（ICB）的总生存期（OS）显著相关。具体而言，基线血浆肌苷水平较高的Nivolumab治疗患者中位OS为33个月，而低肌苷水平患者的中位OS为22个月。这种关联仅在Nivolumab（抗PD-1）治疗组中存在，而在Everolimus（mTOR抑制剂）治疗组中未观察到显著差异。\",\"reference_ids\":[\"R15\"],\"use_in_review\":\"提供人类实体瘤患者血浆中肌苷浓度与ICI疗效的相关性数据，特别是生存期差异。\"},{\"attribution\":\"本研究 (Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine...)\",\"conditions\":\"动物模型：B16-F0黑色素瘤小鼠，ICI治疗前后对比；临床队列：22名接受Sintilimab（抗PD-1）治疗的实体瘤患者，基于肿瘤组织UBA6蛋白表达（IHC评分）分组；指标：肿瘤体积、生存率、总体响应率（ORR）、UBA6蛋白表达水平。\",\"finding\":\"在小鼠模型中，携带B16-F0肿瘤的野生型小鼠血浆肌苷水平高于无肿瘤小鼠，但在接受ICI（抗PD-1 + 抗CTLA-4）治疗后，血浆肌苷水平下降。在人类临床验证部分，研究纳入了22名接受抗PD-1治疗的不同实体瘤（食管癌、肺癌、胃癌、结肠癌等）患者，发现部分缓解（PR）或疾病稳定（SD）患者的肿瘤组织中UBA6蛋白表达水平显著低于疾病进展（PD）患者。低UBA6表达组的总体响应率（ORR）为50%，高UBA6表达组为17%。虽然本研究未直接报告这22例患者血浆肌苷的具体浓度范围，但证实了UBA6低表达（模拟肌苷抑制效果）与良好ICI疗效正相关。\",\"reference_ids\":[],\"use_in_review\":\"补充说明肌苷在动物模型中的变化趋势及临床样本中UBA6表达与疗效的关系，作为肌苷-UBA6轴的临床相关性佐证。\"}],\"explanation\":\"该研究通过代谢组学筛选和临床队列分析，确立了血浆肌苷水平与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效的正相关性。机制上，肌苷并非仅作为能量来源或作用于免疫细胞，而是直接进入肿瘤细胞，抑制泛素激活酶UBA6的活性。UBA6的抑制导致肿瘤细胞内FAT10依赖的抗原加工和炎症信号通路改变，上调MHC-I类分子表达和干扰素反应基因，从而增强肿瘤内在免疫原性，使其对T细胞介导的细胞毒性更敏感。在临床上，肿瘤细胞中UBA6的高表达预测了较差的ICI疗效，而低UBA6表达则与更好的生存期和响应率相关，提示肌苷或其类似物可能通过靶向UBA6来克服ICI耐药。\",\"question_id\":\"Q01\",\"remaining_points\":[\"原文指出由于腺苷在体内半衰期极短（约10秒），而肌苷较长（约15小时），且样本缺失，本研究未在临床队列中直接测量血浆肌苷浓度，因此缺乏人类实体瘤患者血浆肌苷的具体浓度数值范围数据。\",\"临床验证队列样本量较小（n=22），限制了统计效力。\"]},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::dd0499a53f9ada6cb39cd2f0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"deep_read_material\",\"question_material\"],\"value\":{\"examples\":[{\"attribution\":\"Li et al. (2019) / CheckMate 025 队列分析\",\"conditions\":\"人群：接受Nivolumab或Everolimus治疗的晚期肾细胞癌患者；分组依据：基线血浆肌苷水平的中位数分为高/低两组；指标：总生存期（OS）。\",\"finding\":\"在肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列（CheckMate 025试验，Nivolumab治疗组 n=394, Everolimus对照组 n=349）中，通过非靶向代谢组学分析发现，只有肌苷水平与免疫检查点阻断（ICB）的总生存期（OS）显著相关。具体而言，基线血浆肌苷水平较高的Nivolumab治疗患者中位OS为33个月，而低肌苷水平患者的中位OS为22个月。这种关联仅在Nivolumab（抗PD-1）治疗组中存在，而在Everolimus（mTOR抑制剂）治疗组中未观察到显著差异。\",\"reference_ids\":[\"R15\"],\"use_in_review\":\"提供人类实体瘤患者血浆中肌苷浓度与ICI疗效的相关性数据，特别是生存期差异。\"},{\"attribution\":\"本研究 (Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine...)\",\"conditions\":\"动物模型：B16-F0黑色素瘤小鼠，ICI治疗前后对比；临床队列：22名接受Sintilimab（抗PD-1）治疗的实体瘤患者，基于肿瘤组织UBA6蛋白表达（IHC评分）分组；指标：肿瘤体积、生存率、总体响应率（ORR）、UBA6蛋白表达水平。\",\"finding\":\"在小鼠模型中，携带B16-F0肿瘤的野生型小鼠血浆肌苷水平高于无肿瘤小鼠，但在接受ICI（抗PD-1 + 抗CTLA-4）治疗后，血浆肌苷水平下降。在人类临床验证部分，研究纳入了22名接受抗PD-1治疗的不同实体瘤（食管癌、肺癌、胃癌、结肠癌等）患者，发现部分缓解（PR）或疾病稳定（SD）患者的肿瘤组织中UBA6蛋白表达水平显著低于疾病进展（PD）患者。低UBA6表达组的总体响应率（ORR）为50%，高UBA6表达组为17%。虽然本研究未直接报告这22例患者血浆肌苷的具体浓度范围，但证实了UBA6低表达（模拟肌苷抑制效果）与良好ICI疗效正相关。\",\"reference_ids\":[],\"use_in_review\":\"补充说明肌苷在动物模型中的变化趋势及临床样本中UBA6表达与疗效的关系，作为肌苷-UBA6轴的临床相关性佐证。\"}],\"explanation\":\"该研究通过代谢组学筛选和临床队列分析，确立了血浆肌苷水平与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效的正相关性。机制上，肌苷并非仅作为能量来源或作用于免疫细胞，而是直接进入肿瘤细胞，抑制泛素激活酶UBA6的活性。UBA6的抑制导致肿瘤细胞内FAT10依赖的抗原加工和炎症信号通路改变，上调MHC-I类分子表达和干扰素反应基因，从而增强肿瘤内在免疫原性，使其对T细胞介导的细胞毒性更敏感。在临床上，肿瘤细胞中UBA6的高表达预测了较差的ICI疗效，而低UBA6表达则与更好的生存期和响应率相关，提示肌苷或其类似物可能通过靶向UBA6来克服ICI耐药。\",\"question_id\":\"Q01\",\"remaining_points\":[\"原文指出由于腺苷在体内半衰期极短（约10秒），而肌苷较长（约15小时），且样本缺失，本研究未在临床队列中直接测量血浆肌苷浓度，因此缺乏人类实体瘤患者血浆肌苷的具体浓度数值范围数据。\",\"临床验证队列样本量较小（n=22），限制了统计效力。\"]},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5666c4049aeb8034fbad0296\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"deep_read_material\",\"question_material\"],\"value\":{\"examples\":[{\"attribution\":\"本研究\",\"conditions\":\"使用4T1细胞裂解液进行LiP-SMap筛选；使用HEK293细胞和纯化蛋白进行体外相互作用及硫酯活性测定；使用CRISPR敲除UBA6的4T1和B16-GMCSF肿瘤细胞系进行功能验证。\",\"finding\":\"通过LiP-SMap化学蛋白质组学筛选，在4T1细胞裂解物中鉴定出23个与肌苷结合的候选蛋白，其中仅UBA6的缺失能显著增强T细胞介导的肿瘤杀伤。体外生化实验证实，肌苷直接减少UBA6与其特异性E2酶USE1之间的相互作用，并降低UBA6介导的FAT10硫酯键形成活性。此外，删除UBA6的泛素折叠结构域（UFD）可消除肌苷对UBA6-USE1相互作用的抑制作用，且UBA6缺失消除了肌苷对T细胞介导肿瘤杀伤的增敏效应，表明肌苷通过直接抑制UBA6活性来增强肿瘤免疫原性。\",\"reference_ids\":[],\"use_in_review\":\"提供肌苷抑制UBA6的具体分子机制证据，包括结合筛选、生化验证及功能回补实验，证明肌苷通过直接靶向肿瘤细胞内的UBA6发挥作用。\"},{\"attribution\":\"本研究\",\"conditions\":\"分析CheckMate 025临床试验中394名接受纳武利尤单抗治疗和349名接受依维莫司治疗的RCC患者的血浆代谢谱；以代谢物中位数分组比较OS。\",\"finding\":\"在CheckMate 025肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列中，接受纳武利尤单抗（抗PD-1）治疗的患者的血浆肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）呈正相关：高肌苷组中位OS为33个月，低肌苷组为22个月；而在接受依维莫司（mTOR抑制剂）治疗的患者中无此关联。这表明高水平肌苷能为接受ICB治疗的患者带来持久的生存获益。\",\"reference_ids\":[\"R15\"],\"use_in_review\":\"提供血浆肌苷水平与接受ICB治疗患者生存期关联的临床队列数据，确立肌苷作为ICB疗效生物标志物的临床相关性。\"},{\"attribution\":\"本研究\",\"conditions\":\"基于文献综述和讨论部分的逻辑推断，结合研究中提到的腺苷半衰期短、肌苷半衰期长的药代动力学特征，以及未能直接在患者肿瘤组织中测量肌苷的事实。\",\"finding\":\"讨论部分指出，尽管肌苷是腺苷的代谢产物且循环水平受饮食、基因和药物影响，但腺苷在体内可迅速降解为肌苷（约10秒）并在血浆中快速清除（约30秒），而肌苷的生物半衰期较长（约15小时）。由于样本缺失，研究未能在其临床队列中验证肌苷测量或转录组分析。这提示在评估TME中肌苷的实际有效浓度时，需考虑其前体腺苷的不稳定性以及局部摄取机制（如ENT转运体）的作用，目前TME内肌苷的具体浓度缺口及其对UBA6抑制效率的影响尚待进一步解析。\",\"reference_ids\":[\"R55\",\"R56\"],\"use_in_review\":\"补充说明肌苷在肿瘤微环境（TME）中的浓度缺口或来源限制，指出虽然肌苷由肠道菌群产生并可进入循环，但其在TME局部的具体浓度动态及测量受限于腺苷的快速降解，暗示TME内有效肌苷浓度的维持可能存在挑战。\"}],\"explanation\":\"本研究提出并验证了一个由肌苷调控的UBA6依赖性通路，该通路控制肿瘤的内在免疫原性，进而影响免疫检查点阻断（ICB）的敏感性。核心机制在于：肌苷作为一种嘌呤代谢物，能够直接进入肿瘤细胞（通过ENT转运体而非腺苷受体），并直接结合和抑制泛素激活酶UBA6的活性。UBA6不仅激活泛素，还激活泛素样蛋白FAT10。肌苷通过干扰UBA6与E2酶USE1的结合，抑制了UBA6介导的FAT10硫酯键形成。UBA6活性的降低导致肿瘤细胞内炎症信号通路（如TNF-α、IFN-γ响应基因）和抗原加工/呈递相关基因的上调，从而增加MHC-I表达和肿瘤免疫原性。这种增强的免疫原性使肿瘤细胞对CD8+ T细胞介导的细胞毒性更加敏感，从而克服肿瘤内在的ICB耐药性。临床数据显示，患者血浆中高水平的肌苷以及肿瘤组织中低水平的UBA6表达均与接受ICB治疗后的良好预后（更长的OS/PFS和更高的客观缓解率）相关。\",\"question_id\":\"Q01\",\"remaining_points\":[\"TME中肌苷的具体局部浓度及其动态变化尚未量化，特别是考虑到腺苷到肌苷的快速转化及清除过程。\",\"肌苷抑制UBA6后，下游具体的泛素化/FAT10化底物蛋白及其如何具体调控MHC-I上调的详细分子路径仍需进一步阐明。\",\"不同癌症类型中UBA6表达基线差异对肌苷疗效预测价值的普适性需更大规模队列验证。\"]},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8dad3f40352a117c2429e9ca\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"deep_read_material\",\"questions\"],\"value\":{\"gap_key\":\"肌苷抑制 UBA6 机制及血浆肌苷与生存期关联数据是 Ch3 核心证据，需明确标注 TME 浓度缺口。\",\"purpose\":\"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\"question\":\"肌苷抑制 UBA6 机制及血浆肌苷与生存期关联数据是 Ch3 核心证据，需明确标注 TME 浓度缺口。\",\"question_id\":\"Q01\",\"required_output_ids\":[\"O01\"]},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::91e19c0aacd69430ad08f0fd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"supplement_material\"],\"value\":{\"auxiliary_material\":[\"Mechanistic findings: Inosine directly inhibits UBA6 in tumour cells, enhancing tumour immunogenicity and sensitivity to T-cell-mediated killing.\",\"Preclinical evidence: Inosine supplementation sensitizes intrinsically ICB-resistant mouse melanoma and breast cancer models to ICB by inflaming the tumour microenvironment.\",\"Limitations stated by authors: The study did not validate or perform inosine measurement in their own clinical cohort of 22 patients due to intact sample issues; they relied on UBA6 expression as a proxy for the pathway's activity.\",\"Technical context: Adenosine degrades rapidly into inosine (~10 s) and clears quickly, whereas inosine has a longer half-life (~15 h), which impacts measurement strategies in human plasma.\"],\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_73af8e5de3\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"Search for studies that directly quantify inosine concentrations in human tumour biopsies or microdialysates. If only plasma data is available, clarify whether the gap requires intra-tumoral specificity or if systemic correlates are acceptable per the success criteria definition of 'tumour-adjacent material'. Note that this study provides strong associative evidence via plasma levels but lacks the direct intra-tumoral measurement required to fully satisfy the 'inside the human tumour microenvironment' criterion.\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"The specific measured concentration value of inosine inside the human tumour microenvironment (TME) is not provided. The study measures inosine in plasma (serum) of human RCC patients and in mouse plasma/tumours, but does not report direct quantification of inosine within the solid human tumour tissue itself. Furthermore, while the association between plasma inosine levels and survival is established, no absolute concentration values (e.g., ng/mL or μM) for human plasma or TME are explicitly stated in the text.\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"unmet\",\"useful_material\":[\"The study identifies inosine as a purine metabolite associated with immune checkpoint blockade (ICB) sensitivity in both mouse models and human renal cell carcinoma (RCC) patients treated with nivolumab.\",\"In human RCC patients from the CheckMate 025 trial, higher baseline plasma levels of inosine were significantly associated with longer overall survival (median OS 33 months vs. 22 months for low levels) specifically in the nivolumab-treated cohort.\",\"The authors note that circulating inosine levels are influenced by gut microbiota dysbiosis induced by ICB treatment, as well as diet and genetics.\",\"The study reports that plasma levels of inosine were reduced in both tumour-bearing mice and cancer patients after ICB treatment, suggesting dynamic changes during therapy.\"]},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::056b3f508ed27bbf36d498db\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"supplement_materials\"],\"value\":[{\"auxiliary_material\":[\"Mechanistic findings: Inosine directly inhibits UBA6 in tumour cells, enhancing tumour immunogenicity and sensitivity to T-cell-mediated killing.\",\"Preclinical evidence: Inosine supplementation sensitizes intrinsically ICB-resistant mouse melanoma and breast cancer models to ICB by inflaming the tumour microenvironment.\",\"Limitations stated by authors: The study did not validate or perform inosine measurement in their own clinical cohort of 22 patients due to intact sample issues; they relied on UBA6 expression as a proxy for the pathway's activity.\",\"Technical context: Adenosine degrades rapidly into inosine (~10 s) and clears quickly, whereas inosine has a longer half-life (~15 h), which impacts measurement strategies in human plasma.\"],\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_73af8e5de3\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"Search for studies that directly quantify inosine concentrations in human tumour biopsies or microdialysates. If only plasma data is available, clarify whether the gap requires intra-tumoral specificity or if systemic correlates are acceptable per the success criteria definition of 'tumour-adjacent material'. Note that this study provides strong associative evidence via plasma levels but lacks the direct intra-tumoral measurement required to fully satisfy the 'inside the human tumour microenvironment' criterion.\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"The specific measured concentration value of inosine inside the human tumour microenvironment (TME) is not provided. The study measures inosine in plasma (serum) of human RCC patients and in mouse plasma/tumours, but does not report direct quantification of inosine within the solid human tumour tissue itself. Furthermore, while the association between plasma inosine levels and survival is established, no absolute concentration values (e.g., ng/mL or μM) for human plasma or TME are explicitly stated in the text.\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"unmet\",\"useful_material\":[\"The study identifies inosine as a purine metabolite associated with immune checkpoint blockade (ICB) sensitivity in both mouse models and human renal cell carcinoma (RCC) patients treated with nivolumab.\",\"In human RCC patients from the CheckMate 025 trial, higher baseline plasma levels of inosine were significantly associated with longer overall survival (median OS 33 months vs. 22 months for low levels) specifically in the nivolumab-treated cohort.\",\"The authors note that circulating inosine levels are influenced by gut microbiota dysbiosis induced by ICB treatment, as well as diet and genetics.\",\"The study reports that plasma levels of inosine were reduced in both tumour-bearing mice and cancer patients after ICB treatment, suggesting dynamic changes during therapy.\"]},{\"auxiliary_material\":\"研究在小鼠模型（B16-F0, 4T1 等）中证实了外源性肌苷补充可增强 ICI 疗效，并揭示了分子机制：肌苷直接进入肿瘤细胞，抑制泛素激活酶 UBA6，从而解除 UBA6 对炎症信号和抗原呈递通路的抑制，提高肿瘤免疫原性。研究还指出肌苷在血浆中的半衰期较长（约 15 小时），而腺苷极短，这影响了体内测量的稳定性。此外，研究提到肌苷来源具有多源性（肠道微生物、饮食、癌细胞分泌），且在不同肿瘤类型中效果可能依赖基础 UBA6 表达水平（如在低 UBA6 的 MC38 模型中无效）。\",\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level1\\\\external\\\\N76e5cbf6bca57e729afb-df9b777a93e759ce\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-cbtjrz3v\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_216ff7fc1c\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"1. 检索专门针对人体肿瘤组织活检样本进行代谢组学分析（如质谱成像、组织提取 LC-MS）的研究，重点关注是否报告了肌苷的绝对定量数据。2. 查找是否有微透析（microdialysis）技术应用于肿瘤患者监测代谢物的临床研究。3. 关注本研究的后续工作或引用该研究的文献，看是否补充了人体肿瘤组织肌苷浓度的验证数据。4. 在综述中可利用本研究血浆数据作为系统性暴露的代理，利用 UBA6 数据作为 TME 内肌苷活性的代理，但需明确标注这是间接证据而非直接的浓度测量。\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"成功标准要求的‘人体肿瘤组织或微透析液中肌苷绝对浓度（如 μM 或 ng/mL）’数据在此研究中缺失。作者明确说明在人体肿瘤组织队列中因样本问题未进行肌苷测量，仅检测了下游蛋白 UBA6。此外，CheckMate 025 的数据基于血浆（plasma）而非肿瘤微环境（TME）组织液，且文中未报告肌苷的具体绝对浓度数值，仅按中位数分组报告了生存关联。因此，关于 TME 内肌苷生理浓度及其与 ICI 响应的直接定量统计关联仍未解决。\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"unmet\",\"useful_material\":\"这项研究在人体数据方面提供了两方面的关键证据：首先，通过分析 CheckMate 025 临床试验中肾细胞癌（RCC）患者的血浆代谢组数据（n=394 接受 nivolumab 治疗），发现血浆肌苷水平高低与总生存期（OS）显著相关（高肌苷组中位 OS 33 个月 vs 低肌苷组 22 个月），证实了循环肌苷水平与 ICI 疗效的临床关联。其次，在一个包含 22 名接受抗 PD-1 治疗的多癌种患者的小型队列中，作者检测了肿瘤组织内的 UBA6 蛋白表达（作为肌苷作用的下游靶点），发现低 UBA6 表达与更高的客观缓解率（ORR 50% vs 17%）及 CD8+ T 细胞浸润相关。然而，作者明确指出由于样本缺失，未能在该人体肿瘤队列中直接检测肌苷浓度。\"},{\"auxiliary_material\":\"研究通过小鼠模型（B16-F0, 4T1 等）证实了外源性肌苷补充可增强 ICI 疗效，并揭示了分子机制：肌苷直接进入肿瘤细胞，抑制泛素激活酶 UBA6，从而解除 UBA6 对炎症信号和抗原呈递通路的抑制，提高肿瘤免疫原性。研究引用外部文献提及坏死或缺氧微环境中肌苷可能积累至数百微摩尔（hundreds of micromolar），但这并非本研究中对人类患者的实测数据。研究还提到肌苷来源具有多源性（肠道微生物、饮食、癌细胞分泌），且在不同肿瘤类型中效果可能依赖基础 UBA6 表达水平（如在低 UBA6 的 MC38 模型中无效）。\",\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-b532f13f7ac0c36c\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-trstv1th\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_8dbfff8864\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"在综述中引用该研究作为肌苷 -UBA6 轴影响 ICI 疗效的关键机制证据及血浆生物标志物潜力的支持材料，但需明确标注人体 TME 肌苷浓度数据目前缺失。建议后续检索专门针对肿瘤组织间质液（interstitial fluid）或配对组织 - 血浆代谢组学的研究，以寻找可能存在的 TME 肌苷实测数据；或关注该研究团队后续是否发布了补充测量数据。同时可利用该研究提供的 UBA6 表达作为替代指标来讨论肌苷通路的临床相关性。\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"该研究明确指出由于样本完整性问题（intact samples missing），未能在其人类肿瘤临床队列中直接验证或测量肿瘤微环境（TME）内的肌苷浓度，而是以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性的代理指标。因此，关于“人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷的绝对生理浓度”及其与 ICI 疗效在组织层面的直接定量关联（即 TME 肌苷浓度值与 ORR/PFS/OS 的统计挂钩），当前材料显示为未满足的研究空白。现有的血浆数据不能直接等同于 TME 浓度，且引用的微摩尔范围数值为外部文献的理论背景而非本研究对 ICI 响应患者的实测数据。\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"unmet\",\"useful_material\":\"该研究在人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列（CheckMate 025 试验，n=394 接受 nivolumab 治疗）中检测了基线血浆代谢组，发现高血浆肌苷水平与更长的总生存期（OS）显著相关（高肌苷组中位 OS 33 个月 vs 低肌苷组 22 个月），提供了循环肌苷水平与 ICI 疗效的临床关联证据。在机制验证部分，研究在一个包含 22 名接受抗 PD-1 治疗的多癌种患者的小型队列中检测了肿瘤组织内的 UBA6 蛋白表达（作为肌苷作用的下游靶点），发现低 UBA6 表达与更高的客观缓解率（ORR 50% vs 17%）及 CD8+ T 细胞浸润相关。研究还指出肌苷在血浆中的半衰期较长（约 15 小时），而腺苷极短，这影响了体内测量的稳定性。\"},{\"auxiliary_material\":\"研究在小鼠模型（B16-F0, 4T1 等）中证实了外源性肌苷补充（400 mg/kg）可增强 ICI 疗效，并揭示了分子机制：肌苷直接进入肿瘤细胞，抑制泛素激活酶 UBA6，从而解除 UBA6 对炎症信号和抗原呈递通路的抑制。研究引用外部文献指出肌苷在血浆中为低微摩尔范围，而在坏死/缺氧微环境中可积累至数百微摩尔，但强调这些是理论背景而非本研究中对人类患者的实测数据。此外，研究提到肌苷在血浆中的半衰期较长（约 15 小时），而腺苷极短，这影响了体内测量的稳定性。\",\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-acf4314fb7d520c6\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-8uip1jwb\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_8dbfff8864\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"direct\",\"outline_action\":\"在综述中引用该研究作为人体循环肌苷与 ICI 疗效关联的关键证据，同时明确标注其局限性：缺乏人体 TME 内肌苷的直接定量数据。利用该研究提出的 UBA6 表达作为肌苷通路活性的代理指标，讨论其在临床生物标志物开发中的替代价值。指出未来研究需解决人体肿瘤组织内肌苷稳定测量及与临床结局配对分析的技术挑战，以填补 TME 浓度阈值数据的空白。\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"当前材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据（如肿瘤组织或间质液中的具体μM 值），也未报告 TME 内肌苷浓度与 ICI 疗效（如 ORR、PFS 或 OS）的直接定量关联。虽然提供了血浆肌苷与 OS 的相关性以及肿瘤 UBA6 表达与 ORR 的相关性，但研究者明确承认由于样本缺失，未在人体肿瘤样本中验证或测量肌苷浓度。引用的 TME 浓度范围（数百微摩尔）来自外部文献的一般性陈述，并非针对接受 ICI 治疗的人类患者的实测数据。\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"partial\",\"useful_material\":\"该研究在人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列（CheckMate 025 试验，n=394 接受 nivolumab 治疗）中检测了基线血浆肌苷水平，发现高肌苷组中位总生存期（OS）为 33 个月，显著高于低肌苷组的 22 个月，确立了循环肌苷水平与 ICI 疗效的临床统计关联。在另一个包含 22 名接受抗 PD-1 治疗的多癌种患者的小型队列中，作者检测了肿瘤组织内的 UBA6 蛋白表达（作为肌苷作用的下游靶点），发现低 UBA6 表达与更高的客观缓解率（ORR 50% vs 17%）及 CD8+ T 细胞浸润相关。研究明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未能在该人体肿瘤队列中直接检测肿瘤微环境（TME）内的肌苷浓度，而是以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性的代理指标。\"},{\"auxiliary_material\":[\"该研究引用外部文献指出肌苷在坏死/缺氧微环境中可积累至数百微摩尔（hundreds of micromolar），但这属于理论背景陈述，并非本研究对人类患者的实测数据。\",\"该研究在小鼠模型（B16-F0, 4T1 等）中证实了外源性肌苷补充（400 mg/kg 口服）可增强 ICI 疗效，并揭示了 UBA6 缺失可替代肌苷效果的体内证据。\",\"该研究提到肌苷来源具有多源性（肠道微生物、饮食、癌细胞分泌），且在不同肿瘤类型中效果可能依赖基础 UBA6 表达水平（如在低 UBA6 的 MC38 模型中无效）。\"],\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-acf4314fb7d520c6\\\\round_2\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-h4sdftel\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_8dbfff8864\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"在综述中引用该研究提供的血浆肌苷与 OS 相关性数据（CheckMate 025 队列）作为循环代谢物与 ICI 疗效关联的证据；使用 UBA6 表达与 ORR 的相关性数据作为肌苷通路在肿瘤组织内活性的间接证据；明确说明该研究作者承认未能在人体肿瘤样本中直接测量肌苷浓度，将此作为当前领域缺乏 TME 内代谢物绝对浓度实测数据的例证；引用其提及的外部文献关于 TME 肌苷浓度范围（数百微摩尔）时需标注为理论推测或非实测数据。\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据（如具体的μM 或 ng/mL 数值）仍然缺失；人体 TME 内肌苷浓度与 ICI 疗效（ORR/PFS/OS）的直接定量统计关联尚未建立，现有证据仅限于血浆肌苷水平与 OS 的关联，以及肿瘤组织 UBA6 表达（作为代理指标）与疗效的关联。\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"partial\",\"useful_material\":[\"该研究在 CheckMate 025 临床试验的肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列（n=394 接受 nivolumab 治疗）中，通过血浆代谢组分析发现基线血浆肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）显著相关：高肌苷组中位 OS 为 33 个月，低肌苷组为 22 个月。\",\"该研究在一个包含 22 名接受抗 PD-1 治疗的多癌种患者的小型队列中，检测了肿瘤组织内的 UBA6 蛋白表达（作为肌苷作用通路的下游代理指标），发现低 UBA6 表达与更高的客观缓解率（ORR 50% vs 17%）及 CD8+ T 细胞浸润相关。\",\"该研究明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未能在其人体肿瘤队列中直接验证或测量肿瘤微环境（TME）内的肌苷浓度，而是以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性的替代指标。\",\"该研究提供了肌苷增强 ICB 疗效的分子机制证据：肌苷直接进入肿瘤细胞，抑制泛素激活酶 UBA6，从而解除 UBA6 对炎症信号和抗原呈递通路的抑制，提高肿瘤免疫原性。\",\"该研究指出肌苷在血浆中的半衰期较长（约 15 小时），而腺苷极短，这影响了体内测量的稳定性，并提及未来研究需进一步解析两者关系。\"]},{\"auxiliary_material\":[\"研究在小鼠模型（B16-F0, 4T1 等）中证实了外源性肌苷补充（口服 400 mg/kg）可增强 ICI 疗效，并揭示了肌苷在血浆中的半衰期较长（约 15 小时），而腺苷极短，这影响了体内测量的稳定性。\",\"体外实验中使用了 100 μM 的肌苷浓度处理肿瘤细胞以观察 UBA6 抑制效果，但这并非人体内源性浓度的实测数据。\",\"研究指出肌苷来源具有多源性（肠道微生物、饮食、癌细胞分泌），且在不同肿瘤类型中效果可能依赖基础 UBA6 表达水平（如在低 UBA6 的 MC38 模型中无效）。\"],\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-acf4314fb7d520c6\\\\round_3\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-gam_e3ai\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_8dbfff8864\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"在综述中引用该研究作为肌苷与 ICI 疗效存在临床关联的关键证据（血浆层面及 UBA6 代理指标），同时明确标注其局限性（未实测人源 TME 肌苷浓度），以此说明当前文献中缺乏人体 TME 内肌苷绝对浓度数据的研究空白，并建议未来研究需结合配对的组织间质液代谢组学与临床结局数据以填补此缺口。\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"该研究未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据（如 μM 或 ng/mL），也未报告 TME 内肌苷浓度与 ICI 疗效（如 ORR、PFS 或 OS）的直接定量统计关联。虽然提供了血浆肌苷水平与生存期的相关性以及肿瘤组织 UBA6 表达与缓解率的相关性，但作者明确承认由于样本缺失，未在人类肿瘤组织中直接测量肌苷浓度，因此核心的'TME 内肌苷具体浓度阈值’及‘组织层面浓度 - 疗效直接挂钩’的证据在此材料中缺失。\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"partial\",\"useful_material\":[\"这项研究在 CheckMate 025 临床试验的肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列（n=394 接受 nivolumab 治疗）中分析了血浆代谢组数据，发现基线血浆肌苷水平较高与总生存期（OS）延长显著相关（高肌苷组中位 OS 33 个月 vs 低肌苷组 22 个月），证实了循环肌苷水平与 ICI 疗效的临床关联。\",\"研究在一个包含 22 名接受抗 PD-1 治疗的多癌种患者的小型队列中检测了肿瘤组织内的 UBA6 蛋白表达（作为肌苷作用的下游靶点），发现低 UBA6 表达与更高的客观缓解率（ORR 50% vs 17%）及 CD8+ T 细胞浸润相关。\",\"作者明确指出由于样本完整性问题（intact samples missing），未能在该人体肿瘤队列中直接检测或验证肌苷浓度，而是以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性的代理指标。\",\"研究揭示了肌苷增强 ICB 疗效的分子机制：肌苷直接进入肿瘤细胞，抑制泛素激活酶 UBA6，从而解除 UBA6 对炎症信号和抗原呈递通路的抑制，提高肿瘤免疫原性。\"]}],\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0b09743b266c65650f7a5ee5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"tool_supplement_materials\"],\"value\":[{\"allowed_use\":[],\"conditions\":[],\"decision\":\"stop\",\"intended_use\":\"\",\"limits\":[],\"need_id\":\"N2bdec0b1582a-465c62ed8bfc6cf2\",\"question\":\"肌苷通过抑制 UBA6 增强 ICI 疗效的具体分子机制是什么？人体血浆肌苷水平与生存期的关联数据如何？\",\"sources\":[{\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"title\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"year\":\"2022\"}],\"still_missing\":\"肌苷通过抑制 UBA6 增强 ICI 疗效的具体分子机制是什么？人体血浆肌苷水平与生存期的关联数据如何？\",\"usable_content\":\"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"直接回答肌苷通过抑制UBA6增强ICI疗效的分子机制，提供从代谢物结合到酶活性抑制、再到肿瘤细胞免疫原性改变的完整因果链条证据。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"肌苷在肿瘤细胞内直接结合并抑制泛素激活酶UBA6的活性。具体表现为：1) 化学蛋白质组学（LiP-SMap）筛选及CRISPR遗传筛选鉴定UBA6为肌苷的功能靶点；2) 体外生化实验证实肌苷预处理直接减少UBA6与E2连接酶USE1的相互作用，并降低UBA6介导的FAT10硫酯键形成活性；3) UBA6缺失或抑制导致肿瘤细胞内炎症因子（TNF-α, IFN-γ）响应基因上调，MHC-I表面表达增加，抗原加工/呈递相关基因表达增强；4) 经肌苷处理的肿瘤细胞对T细胞介导的细胞毒性更敏感，且这种增敏效应依赖于UBA6的存在（UBA6敲除后肌苷不再产生额外效果）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"使用4T1和B16-GMCSF小鼠肿瘤细胞系；采用LiP-SMap化学蛋白质组学、体外纯化蛋白硫酯酶活性测定、CRISPR介导的Uba6基因敲除、以及T细胞-肿瘤细胞共培养杀伤实验。对比对象包括野生型与Uba6-null肿瘤细胞、肌苷处理与未处理组、以及不同效靶比下的T细胞杀伤效率。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供人体血浆肌苷水平与生存期关联的临床队列数据，验证肌苷作为ICI疗效生物标志物的价值。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列（CheckMate 025试验）中，接受纳武利尤单抗（抗PD-1）治疗的患者基线血浆肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）正相关。高肌苷组的中位OS为33个月，低肌苷组为22个月。该关联仅在ICI治疗组中存在，而在接受mTOR抑制剂依维莫司治疗的对照组中不存在（两组OS无显著差异），表明高肌苷水平特异性地预测ICI疗效。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"数据来源为CheckMate 025临床试验的肾细胞癌患者队列（n=743，其中394人接受纳武利尤单抗，349人接受依维莫司）。分析基于基线血浆代谢组学数据，按各代谢物中位数将患者分为高低两组，使用Cox比例风险模型和Kaplan-Meier曲线评估OS。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R15\\\", \\\"R26\\\"]}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"本文阐述的核心机制是：肌苷作为一种嘌呤代谢物，能够克服肿瘤内在的免疫治疗抵抗。其作用路径并非主要作用于免疫细胞，而是直接靶向肿瘤细胞内的UBA6蛋白。UBA6是一种泛素激活酶，负责激活泛素和泛素样蛋白FAT10。肌苷通过直接结合UBA6，抑制其与E2酶USE1的相互作用及后续的催化活性。UBA6活性的降低解除了对肿瘤细胞内在免疫反应的抑制，导致肿瘤细胞呈现更高的免疫原性，具体表现为MHC-I类分子上调、抗原加工与呈递通路基因表达增加，以及对由CD8+ T细胞分泌的细胞毒性因子（如TNF-α和IFN-γ）更加敏感。这种“热”肿瘤微环境的建立增强了T细胞介导的杀伤作用，从而协同免疫检查点阻断疗法（ICB）提高疗效。临床数据支持这一机制，显示高血浆肌苷水平与接受PD-1抑制剂治疗患者的更长生存期相关。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"肌苷进入肿瘤细胞的具体转运蛋白机制虽提示依赖ENT转运体而非腺苷受体，但具体的分子细节未在正文详细展开。\\\", \\\"虽然建立了肌苷-UBA6-免疫原性的机制，但UBA6下游具体哪些底物的去泛素化或稳定化导致了免疫原性改变，文中指出仍需进一步定义。\\\", \\\"临床验证队列样本量较小（n=22用于UBA6蛋白表达验证），且由于样本缺失，未能同时测量这些患者体内的肌苷水平以进行直接的相关性分析。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"},{\"allowed_use\":[],\"conditions\":[],\"decision\":\"stop\",\"intended_use\":\"\",\"limits\":[],\"need_id\":\"Nd237f43b4811-465c62ed8bfc6cf2\",\"question\":\"肌苷抑制 UBA6 机制及血浆肌苷与生存期关联数据是 Ch3 核心证据，需明确标注 TME 浓度缺口。\",\"sources\":[{\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"title\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"year\":\"2022\"}],\"still_missing\":\"肌苷抑制 UBA6 机制及血浆肌苷与生存期关联数据是 Ch3 核心证据，需明确标注 TME 浓度缺口。\",\"usable_content\":\"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供肌苷抑制UBA6的具体分子机制证据，包括结合筛选、生化验证及功能回补实验，证明肌苷通过直接靶向肿瘤细胞内的UBA6发挥作用。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"通过LiP-SMap化学蛋白质组学筛选，在4T1细胞裂解物中鉴定出23个与肌苷结合的候选蛋白，其中仅UBA6的缺失能显著增强T细胞介导的肿瘤杀伤。体外生化实验证实，肌苷直接减少UBA6与其特异性E2酶USE1之间的相互作用，并降低UBA6介导的FAT10硫酯键形成活性。此外，删除UBA6的泛素折叠结构域（UFD）可消除肌苷对UBA6-USE1相互作用的抑制作用，且UBA6缺失消除了肌苷对T细胞介导肿瘤杀伤的增敏效应，表明肌苷通过直接抑制UBA6活性来增强肿瘤免疫原性。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"使用4T1细胞裂解液进行LiP-SMap筛选；使用HEK293细胞和纯化蛋白进行体外相互作用及硫酯活性测定；使用CRISPR敲除UBA6的4T1和B16-GMCSF肿瘤细胞系进行功能验证。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供血浆肌苷水平与接受ICB治疗患者生存期关联的临床队列数据，确立肌苷作为ICB疗效生物标志物的临床相关性。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在CheckMate 025肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列中，接受纳武利尤单抗（抗PD-1）治疗的患者的血浆肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）呈正相关：高肌苷组中位OS为33个月，低肌苷组为22个月；而在接受依维莫司（mTOR抑制剂）治疗的患者中无此关联。这表明高水平肌苷能为接受ICB治疗的患者带来持久的生存获益。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"分析CheckMate 025临床试验中394名接受纳武利尤单抗治疗和349名接受依维莫司治疗的RCC患者的血浆代谢谱；以代谢物中位数分组比较OS。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R15\\\"]}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"补充说明肌苷在肿瘤微环境（TME）中的浓度缺口或来源限制，指出虽然肌苷由肠道菌群产生并可进入循环，但其在TME局部的具体浓度动态及测量受限于腺苷的快速降解，暗示TME内有效肌苷浓度的维持可能存在挑战。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"讨论部分指出，尽管肌苷是腺苷的代谢产物且循环水平受饮食、基因和药物影响，但腺苷在体内可迅速降解为肌苷（约10秒）并在血浆中快速清除（约30秒），而肌苷的生物半衰期较长（约15小时）。由于样本缺失，研究未能在其临床队列中验证肌苷测量或转录组分析。这提示在评估TME中肌苷的实际有效浓度时，需考虑其前体腺苷的不稳定性以及局部摄取机制（如ENT转运体）的作用，目前TME内肌苷的具体浓度缺口及其对UBA6抑制效率的影响尚待进一步解析。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"基于文献综述和讨论部分的逻辑推断，结合研究中提到的腺苷半衰期短、肌苷半衰期长的药代动力学特征，以及未能直接在患者肿瘤组织中测量肌苷的事实。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R55\\\", \\\"R56\\\"]}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"本研究提出并验证了一个由肌苷调控的UBA6依赖性通路，该通路控制肿瘤的内在免疫原性，进而影响免疫检查点阻断（ICB）的敏感性。核心机制在于：肌苷作为一种嘌呤代谢物，能够直接进入肿瘤细胞（通过ENT转运体而非腺苷受体），并直接结合和抑制泛素激活酶UBA6的活性。UBA6不仅激活泛素，还激活泛素样蛋白FAT10。肌苷通过干扰UBA6与E2酶USE1的结合，抑制了UBA6介导的FAT10硫酯键形成。UBA6活性的降低导致肿瘤细胞内炎症信号通路（如TNF-α、IFN-γ响应基因）和抗原加工/呈递相关基因的上调，从而增加MHC-I表达和肿瘤免疫原性。这种增强的免疫原性使肿瘤细胞对CD8+ T细胞介导的细胞毒性更加敏感，从而克服肿瘤内在的ICB耐药性。临床数据显示，患者血浆中高水平的肌苷以及肿瘤组织中低水平的UBA6表达均与接受ICB治疗后的良好预后（更长的OS/PFS和更高的客观缓解率）相关。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"TME中肌苷的具体局部浓度及其动态变化尚未量化，特别是考虑到腺苷到肌苷的快速转化及清除过程。\\\", \\\"肌苷抑制UBA6后，下游具体的泛素化/FAT10化底物蛋白及其如何具体调控MHC-I上调的详细分子路径仍需进一步阐明。\\\", \\\"不同癌症类型中UBA6表达基线差异对肌苷疗效预测价值的普适性需更大规模队列验证。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"}],\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d93294b2fde7fbbbbceb24f3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-ee45627bb52c2a851316\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"missing\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-501f35983c2f020a5c71\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"missing\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-81ec1ef0c2a046851171\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"missing\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-d46f32b2af56fa1c47e2\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"missing\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-c0fd2c95dd50ca770222\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"missing\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-42c295d5bf79b23956eb\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"missing\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-37c988b582332c2f54a1\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"missing\"},{\"kind\":\"assets\",\"reason\":\"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\"status\":\"missing\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s043\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f268dc5a31e6509082426a96\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::915832e3eeeb6c7bf46b4dc7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0c9458faeedb93aae1481ce2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"研究采用多步骤计算与实验结合的策略：1) 利用TCGA bulk RNA-seq数据和ImmuCellAI去卷积算法，鉴定与免疫浸润负相关或正相关的TIIMGs；2) 使用L1000高通量筛选平台，针对TIIMGs筛选739种化合物的转录组扰动效应，并通过drug-to-cell recall验证；3) 在CT26小鼠模型中进行体内给药，收集肿瘤组织进行scRNA-seq，利用NMF算法从肿瘤细胞中提取异质性程序并聚类为12个MPs；4) 开发MP评分算法（结合Cluster 1激活与Cluster 2抑制的加权）量化TME重塑程度；5) 基于MP评分优先选择候选药物（oxypurinol及其前体allopurinol），通过流式细胞术、LC-MS/MS检测肌苷水平、体外共培养及体内协同实验验证机制；6) 回顾性分析人类膀胱癌患者队列中抗痛风药与抗PD-1治疗的生存关联。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::894b59684f5f72f52dd6cd62\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"建立了首个基于单细胞分辨率的药物诱导TME重塑量化框架（resTMe），定义了12个TME元程序（MPs）和MP评分算法，为预测药物-免疫疗法协同作用提供了新工具。\",\"limits\":\"核心scRNA-seq数据仅来源于小鼠模型（CT26），缺乏人源类器官或PDX模型的直接验证，限制了框架在人类复杂TME中的直接外推性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8ef0876af1bde6e00dba83aa\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"发现了别嘌醇（Allopurinol）作为抗PD-1疗法的潜在增效剂，阐明了其通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌、增强肿瘤免疫原性和T细胞功能的分子机制。\",\"limits\":\"机制验证主要在体外细胞系和小鼠模型中进行；人类临床证据仅来自小样本（n=50）、单中心的回顾性观察性研究，存在混杂因素风险，需前瞻性临床试验确认。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b30b08eb075f61505bc09741\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"证实了MDSCs的耗竭是响应性TME的关键标志物，并揭示了低剂量药物可能通过非细胞毒性机制重塑TME以促进免疫浸润。\",\"limits\":\"对于其他候选药物（如epirubicin, vemurafenib）的具体分子机制阐述不如AP深入；不同药物对特定免疫亚群的影响差异较大，尚未形成统一的普适性规则。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d89ef3a629b3edc8f1d5680d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"8种癌症类型TCGA数据分析\",\"finding\":\"鉴定出肿瘤细胞特异性免疫浸润调节基因（TIIMGs），其中COAD拥有最多的dpGenes（792个），KIRC最少，揭示了不同癌症间TME调控网络的异质性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f9f47d7274d6ce123558914d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"L1000平台筛选739种化合物\",\"finding\":\"识别出54种在多癌种中重复出现的候选药物，主要靶向CDKs、HDAC1、PI3K等通路。低剂量处理更倾向于产生非细胞毒性的免疫调节效应，而高剂量常伴随免疫抑制。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::13b75fe0affb6edd8981d33b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"CT26小鼠模型scRNA-seq分析\",\"finding\":\"药物处理导致肿瘤细胞比例下降，免疫细胞（特别是巨噬细胞、DCs）浸润增加，但MDSCs显著减少。oxypurinol表现出最强的TME重塑能力，显著降低MDSCs并增加抗原呈递相关细胞。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::59223824372c97eeae14a917\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"MP评分算法应用\",\"finding\":\"定义了12个MPs，其中Cluster 2（含MPs 1,3,6,8,10,12）与抗原加工和呈递通路高度相关。oxypurinol获得最高MP评分，提示其具有最强的TME重塑潜力。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4f486a10e036032c79861cfc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Allopurinol (AP) 联合抗PD-1治疗\",\"finding\":\"AP通过抑制黄嘌呤脱氢酶（XDH）增加肌苷合成并分泌至胞外，肌苷上调肿瘤细胞MHC I类和PD-L1表达，增强CD8+ T细胞介导的细胞毒性。在CT26模型中，AP联合抗PD-1实现4/6小鼠完全治愈。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c5b36a5dbcaf7631b8b07425\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"人类膀胱癌回顾性队列（n=50）\",\"finding\":\"在接受抗PD-1治疗的膀胱癌患者中，同时服用抗痛风药物（如AP或febuxostat）的患者组（n=7）的总生存期（OS）显著优于未服用组（n=43）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4a9ba68194211f72c5ff2998\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::309f1460bfa5781083656af4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"如何在复杂的肿瘤微环境中系统性地识别能够增强免疫疗法疗效的药物组合？目前缺乏量化药物诱导TME重塑的系统框架，且难以预测哪些非抗癌药物可作为免疫治疗的增效剂。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::732cd6b3522e68e0af8deae5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"研究聚焦于实体瘤（以小鼠结肠癌CT26模型和人类膀胱癌队列为主）的肿瘤微环境（TME），探讨药物诱导的TME重塑如何影响免疫检查点抑制剂（如抗PD-1/PD-L1）的疗效。研究对象包括8种癌症类型的TCGA数据、739种免疫调节化合物、小鼠体内的单细胞转录组数据以及临床回顾性队列。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::82ddeb3927993c2d17aa2d61\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"该研究旨在解决缺乏系统性框架来量化药物诱导的TME重塑的问题。作者首先通过TCGA数据和ImmuCellAI算法鉴定了肿瘤细胞特异性免疫浸润调节基因（TIIMGs），并利用L1000平台筛选出能显著调控这些基因的化合物。随后，在小鼠CT26肿瘤模型中，通过单细胞RNA测序（scRNA-seq）分析了多种药物处理后的TME变化，识别出12个与TME重塑相关的元程序（Meta-programs, MPs）。基于MP富集情况开发了MP评分算法，用于量化TME对药物的响应程度。该算法成功鉴定出别嘌醇（Allopurinol, AP），一种痛风药物，发现其能通过促进肌苷（inosine）的合成与分泌，上调肿瘤细胞的MHC I类和PD-L1表达，从而增强CD8+ T细胞的杀伤活性。在体内实验中，低剂量AP联合抗PD-1治疗实现了4/6的小鼠完全肿瘤清除。此外，一项包含50名膀胱癌患者的回顾性研究显示，接受抗痛风药物治疗的患者在抗PD-1治疗下的总生存期显著优于未使用者。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8ef9500030daca139659e570\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文为综述提供了关于‘非传统免疫调节药物’（老药新用）如何通过代谢重编程和TME重塑增强ICI疗效的具体案例和机制解释。它不直接涉及肠道菌群，但提供了一个重要的对比维度：即宿主代谢状态（如痛风药物干预）和肿瘤局部代谢产物（肌苷）如何独立于或协同于微生物组影响ICI疗效。其建立的MP评分框架可用于归类不同药物对TME细胞组成的影响模式。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::29799ff01275a5961dfa4b1f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"该研究未涉及肠道菌群，因此不能直接回答菌群如何调制ICI疗效的问题，只能作为平行机制或交互作用的潜在背景。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了非微生物来源的代谢物（肌苷）增强ICI疗效的证据。研究发现别嘌醇通过增加肌苷分泌，增强CD8+ T细胞功能，这与某些肠道菌群代谢产物（如丁酸盐、次级胆汁酸）调节免疫微环境的机制形成互补或对比视角。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cc0bd417229ac67f8358b8ee\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制仅限于别嘌醇-肌苷轴，不能推广为所有ICI增效剂的通用机制。人类证据仅为相关性，因果链条在人体中尚待确证。\",\"contribution\":\"详细阐述了别嘌醇增强ICI疗效的具体分子机制：抑制XDH -> 增加肌苷 -> 上调MHC I/PD-L1 -> 增强T细胞杀伤。同时指出MDSCs减少是响应性TME的标志。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ce5af135f0f54a3f33ded5af\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"基于小鼠模型数据，人类组织中MDSCs的功能异质性更大，需谨慎外推。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了MDSCs耗竭作为ICI响应生物标志物的实证支持。在scRNA-seq分析中，响应性TME显著特征为MDSCs比例降低。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::911473103290b79cdeaaf990\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"别嘌醇（痛风药）被鉴定为抗PD-1增效剂，并在回顾性临床队列中显示生存获益。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d608d3703ed2d823c7784427\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"MP评分算法和12个元程序的定义，量化了抗原呈递、盐应激反应等生物学过程在药物处理后的变化。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1c11e7ad8dda921d2c87e471\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"AP处理导致肌苷大量分泌，增强OT-I T细胞对B16-OVA肿瘤的杀伤力。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9a50fe6e4b2c8671f940ffb9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该研究的核心对象是小鼠模型和人类膀胱癌回顾性队列，未直接研究肠道菌群。在将其用于回答‘菌群如何调制ICI’问题时，必须明确其作为‘非菌群代谢机制’的对比或补充角色，而非直接证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::78212dc609fe90c3f037d637\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"人类临床数据仅为小样本回顾性观察（n=50），存在选择偏倚和混杂因素，不能作为因果关系的确凿证据，仅能作为假设生成的线索。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::125505f32ce06e79d94ca2a2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"别嘌醇的机制特异性强（肌苷轴），不能将其效果泛化为所有代谢调节药物或所有ICI增效剂的共同机制。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c058dc0771a54f0d89db5a07\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"MP评分和元程序是基于小鼠CT26模型定义的，在不同癌症类型或人源模型中的适用性需进一步验证。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::50e3812052714d3b820c4e72\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"supplement_material\"],\"value\":{\"auxiliary_material\":\"The study developed a meta-program (MP) scoring algorithm based on scRNA-seq data from mouse tumors to quantify TME remodeling, identifying myeloid-derived suppressor cell (MDSC) depletion as a hallmark of responsive TMEs. It established a resource (scIMD) and web tool (resTMe) for screening immunomodulatory drugs. The analysis covered eight cancer types for gene identification but performed in vivo validation primarily in the CT26 colon carcinoma model.\",\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-acf4314fb7d520c6\\\\round_2\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-h4sdftel\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_7df1939f2d\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"Use this study to support the mechanistic plausibility of inosine-mediated ICI enhancement and to cite indirect human clinical evidence linking xanthine oxidase inhibition to improved survival. However, explicitly state that direct human TME inosine quantification and concentration-response correlation data remain unavailable in this source. Future search strategies should target metabolomics studies profiling human tumor interstitial fluid or tissue specifically for purine metabolites in ICI-treated cohorts.\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"This material does not provide the absolute physiological concentration of inosine within the human tumor microenvironment (TME); the concentration data reported is from mouse cell culture supernatants. Furthermore, it does not report a direct statistical correlation between measured human TME inosine levels and ICI efficacy (e.g., ORR, PFS, OS). The human clinical evidence provided is an association between gout medication usage (as a proxy for inosine elevation) and survival, not a correlation based on quantified inosine metabolite levels in patient tissues or fluids. The study explicitly notes its limitation that drug scRNA-seq data were derived from mouse models.\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"unmet\",\"useful_material\":\"This study investigated the synergistic effect of allopurinol (AP) with anti-PD-1 therapy. In mouse CT26 cell cultures, LC-MS/MS analysis showed AP treatment increased extracellular inosine levels by approximately 500 to 1000-fold in supernatants, while cell lysate levels remained unchanged, indicating active export. Mechanistically, AP inhibits xanthine dehydrogenase (XDH), elevating hypoxanthine which is converted to inosine via the salvage pathway. In vivo, AP combined with anti-PD-1 achieved tumor-free outcomes in 4/6 mice. In a retrospective human cohort of 50 bladder cancer patients receiving anti-PD-1 therapy, the 7 patients concurrently taking gout medications (AP or febuxostat) showed significantly better overall survival compared to the 43 patients who did not. The authors propose that elevated inosine enhances tumor immunogenicity (upregulating MHC class I and PD-L1) and supports T-cell function.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::93b0bc69434a90089e6079fe\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"supplement_materials\"],\"value\":[{\"auxiliary_material\":\"The study developed a meta-program (MP) scoring algorithm based on scRNA-seq data from mouse tumors to quantify TME remodeling, identifying myeloid-derived suppressor cell (MDSC) depletion as a hallmark of responsive TMEs. It established a resource (scIMD) and web tool (resTMe) for screening immunomodulatory drugs. The analysis covered eight cancer types for gene identification but performed in vivo validation primarily in the CT26 colon carcinoma model.\",\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-acf4314fb7d520c6\\\\round_2\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-h4sdftel\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_7df1939f2d\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"Use this study to support the mechanistic plausibility of inosine-mediated ICI enhancement and to cite indirect human clinical evidence linking xanthine oxidase inhibition to improved survival. However, explicitly state that direct human TME inosine quantification and concentration-response correlation data remain unavailable in this source. Future search strategies should target metabolomics studies profiling human tumor interstitial fluid or tissue specifically for purine metabolites in ICI-treated cohorts.\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"This material does not provide the absolute physiological concentration of inosine within the human tumor microenvironment (TME); the concentration data reported is from mouse cell culture supernatants. Furthermore, it does not report a direct statistical correlation between measured human TME inosine levels and ICI efficacy (e.g., ORR, PFS, OS). The human clinical evidence provided is an association between gout medication usage (as a proxy for inosine elevation) and survival, not a correlation based on quantified inosine metabolite levels in patient tissues or fluids. The study explicitly notes its limitation that drug scRNA-seq data were derived from mouse models.\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"unmet\",\"useful_material\":\"This study investigated the synergistic effect of allopurinol (AP) with anti-PD-1 therapy. In mouse CT26 cell cultures, LC-MS/MS analysis showed AP treatment increased extracellular inosine levels by approximately 500 to 1000-fold in supernatants, while cell lysate levels remained unchanged, indicating active export. Mechanistically, AP inhibits xanthine dehydrogenase (XDH), elevating hypoxanthine which is converted to inosine via the salvage pathway. In vivo, AP combined with anti-PD-1 achieved tumor-free outcomes in 4/6 mice. In a retrospective human cohort of 50 bladder cancer patients receiving anti-PD-1 therapy, the 7 patients concurrently taking gout medications (AP or febuxostat) showed significantly better overall survival compared to the 43 patients who did not. The authors propose that elevated inosine enhances tumor immunogenicity (upregulating MHC class I and PD-L1) and supports T-cell function.\"}],\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::533541e5da218bf180bf8879\",\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-d48cd64bd12b302ad2ba\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-95bd9a77b14edf06222c\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-a7194a689f46f19f0fc9\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-5f82ba52a99d38e52a55\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-5bcddf895da96806b16c\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-c44cb221036f78d05573\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"kind\":\"assets\",\"missing\":[\"jitc-14-3-g001.jpg\",\"jitc-14-3-g002.jpg\",\"jitc-14-3-g003.jpg\",\"jitc-14-3-g004.jpg\",\"jitc-14-3-g005.jpg\",\"jitc-14-3-g006.jpg\",\"jitc-14-3-s001.docx\",\"jitc-14-3-s002.xlsx\",\"jitc-14-3-s003.xlsx\",\"jitc-14-3-s004.xlsx\",\"jitc-14-3-s005.xlsx\",\"jitc-14-3-s006.xlsx\",\"jitc-14-3-s007.xlsx\",\"jitc-14-3-s008.xlsx\",\"jitc-14-3-s009.xlsx\",\"jitc-14-3-s010.tif\"],\"reason\":\"graphic_members_unmatched\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"assets\",\"reason\":\"supplementary_bundle_had_no_safe_matching_images\",\"status\":\"unparsed\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s031\",\"s160\",\"s074\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::514f38127e84ad5c682c0de5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::908d9aeb78769ef90ff4fc57\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b8a5a05a2c4c46c244939963\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用单中心、随机对照试验设计。纳入符合RECIST v1.1标准的晚期实体瘤患者，按1:1比例随机分组。试验组接受标准免疫治疗联合肌苷（0.2g tid），对照组接受标准免疫治疗。疗效评估每6周进行一次，主要终点为ORR，次要终点为DCR、OS和PFS。使用Kaplan-Meier法计算生存曲线，Cox比例风险模型进行多因素分析，并对不同亚组（如肿瘤类型、炎症指标、转移部位）进行探索性分析以识别潜在受益人群。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::33a5c9e4d60f2557fa054a13\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了肌苷联合ICI治疗晚期实体瘤的首个随机对照临床II期数据，证实了肌苷在延长PFS方面的统计学显著性，并为“肠道代谢物调节免疫治疗”假说提供了初步临床支持。\",\"limits\":\"单中心设计导致样本量有限（每组86人）；非盲法设计可能存在偏倚；多肿瘤类型混合导致统计效能分散，OS结果受后续治疗影响较大；亚组分析为探索性，存在多重比较问题，需外部验证。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::44fd7d0fece39e6e515ee6c0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"全队列（N=172）\",\"finding\":\"肌苷组中位PFS显著长于对照组（7.00 vs 4.40个月，HR=0.63, p=0.011）；ORR为26.7% vs 15.1%（p=0.061，未显著）；中位OS两组无显著差异（HR=1.05, p=0.874）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d691120d6413e21d59a3ebbf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"肺癌亚组（N=57）\",\"finding\":\"肌苷组mPFS显著延长（13.80 vs 4.10个月，HR=0.45, p=0.018）；mOS趋势向好但未达显著（HR=0.46, p=0.100）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7efc4f3f1c27bfe2d678132b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"消化道恶性肿瘤亚组（N=55）\",\"finding\":\"肌苷组mPFS有延长趋势但未达显著（5.77 vs 3.50个月，HR=0.63, p=0.121）；mOS无显著差异。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2dffc3c3672a37974c931734\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"实验室指标亚组（PLR<229, NLR<4, LDH≥216, ENR≤0.012）\",\"finding\":\"在这些特定炎症/代谢标志物背景下，肌苷组PFS均显著优于对照组。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e163eddf36fc1e7cc27c2513\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"安全性评估\",\"finding\":\"肌苷组3-4级不良事件发生率为29%，对照组为36%（p=0.329），提示肌苷可能不增加且略有降低严重不良反应的风险。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d212be6d9591bb99f87b63b7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::326bcdfc7c44333ca4ea1aa5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管临床前研究表明肠道微生物代谢物肌苷可增强ICI疗效，但缺乏人体临床证据。本研究试图解决肌苷作为辅助治疗是否能提高晚期实体瘤患者对PD-1/PD-L1抑制剂的响应率及生存获益的问题。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::96c8a6d462cf5ee52975af40\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"单中心、前瞻性、随机、开放标签的II期临床试验。研究对象为晚期恶性实体瘤患者（包括肺癌、消化道肿瘤等），干预措施为在PD-1/PD-L1抑制剂基础上联合口服肌苷（0.2g，每日三次），对照组仅接受PD-1/PD-L1抑制剂±靶向±化疗。主要评估终点为客观缓解率（ORR）、无进展生存期（PFS）和总生存期（OS）。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1351c9ffeb3960925c4ddd82\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本研究旨在验证肠道微生物代谢物肌苷能否增强免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）在晚期实体瘤中的疗效。研究在北京友谊医院开展，将172名患者随机分配至肌苷组或对照组。结果显示，与对照组相比，肌苷组显著延长了中位PFS（7.00 vs 4.40个月，HR=0.63, p=0.011），ORR呈上升趋势但未达统计学显著性（26.7% vs 15.1%, p=0.061），OS两组无显著差异。亚组分析显示肌苷在多种基线特征下均能改善PFS。安全性方面，肌苷组3-4级不良反应发生率略低于对照组。结论认为肌苷有潜力增强ICI疗效并降低相关不良反应。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1f23585217c274f414ef0eb4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文提供了肌苷（一种已知的肠道微生物代谢物）在人体中增强ICI疗效的直接临床证据。对于综述而言，它是连接“肠道菌群代谢物”与“ICI疗效”的关键实证环节，特别是填补了从动物实验到人类临床应用的空白。其核心价值在于展示了具体代谢物干预的临床可行性、剂量方案及初步疗效信号，同时揭示了不同肿瘤类型和炎症状态下的异质性响应。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c624786259f743d00b397b1b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅在PFS上显示显著优势，ORR和OS未达到统计学显著性；结果受限于单中心和混合肿瘤类型，不能直接外推至所有实体瘤或替代一线标准疗法的地位。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肌苷作为肠道代谢物增强ICI疗效的人体临床数据。具体表现为：在全队列中显著延长PFS（HR=0.63），在肺癌亚组中大幅延长PFS（HR=0.45），并在特定炎症指标（低PLR/NLR，高LDH/ENR）亚组中表现出更显著的PFS获益。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7fc145947c92c1b9b4e13c3f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制部分主要基于作者引用的既往文献（Mager et al., Wang et al., Zhang et al.），本文本身未提供新的机制实验数据（如生物样本分析）。因此，机制解释属于理论支撑，而非本研究的直接发现。\",\"contribution\":\"虽然本文主要报告临床结果，但在背景和讨论中引用并整合了机制研究：肌苷通过抑制UBA6增加肿瘤细胞免疫原性、激活IFN-γ/TNF-α通路、促进CD8+ T细胞增殖、抑制MDSC介导的免疫抑制以及作为CD8+ T细胞的碳源。这些机制解释了为何肌苷能克服ICI耐药。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ad1c1e3f94a45a000796047a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"肌苷的安全性和经济性（已有数十年临床应用历史，用于肝炎辅助治疗），以及其降低3-4级不良反应的趋势（29% vs 36%）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ee3c0ca040f5f7857105c083\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"亚组分析显示，基线炎症指标（PLR, NLR, LDH, ENR）和吸烟/饮酒状态可能与肌苷疗效相关。例如，在非饮酒者、吸烟者、ECOG≥1、无肾上腺/骨/肺转移等亚组中PFS获益更明显。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::330b20611a2b60f0bfb9cb57\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"本文是II期单中心研究，样本量较小，OS结果不显著可能受随访时间不足或后续治疗干扰，解读时需谨慎，避免过度推断长期生存获益。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d7b8f615eb29b4d96eed30ee\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"亚组分析多为探索性且未预设校正，显著性结果可能存在假阳性风险，应视为假设生成而非确证。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::eaa3814986ed246e629fbab5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"机制描述依赖于文献综述，非本研究实测，需在综述中明确区分临床观察与理论机制。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::318bfbc9220c4ae9361634f9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"肌苷效果在不同肿瘤类型间存在异质性（肺癌显著，消化道肿瘤趋势不显著），不能笼统概括为对所有实体瘤均有效。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::530b529c34eddfdef2d6f9ae\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"supplement_material\"],\"value\":{\"auxiliary_material\":\"The authors cite preclinical mechanisms in the background and discussion, including inosine's role in inhibiting UBA6 to increase tumor immunogenicity, serving as a carbon source for CD8+ T cells, and activating IFN-γ/TNF-α pathways. The study design is a single-center, prospective, randomized, open-label Phase 2 trial registered at ClinicalTrials.gov (NCT05809336). The dosage regimen and safety data support the feasibility of repurposing inosine as an adjunct therapy.\",\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-b532f13f7ac0c36c\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-trstv1th\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_23b146d5b5\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"Search for pharmacokinetic or metabolomic studies that specifically quantify baseline inosine levels in human tumor biopsies or plasma prior to immunotherapy initiation. Look for correlative analyses linking these endogenous measurements to clinical response (ORR/PFS/OS) without exogenous intervention. Consider reviewing studies that utilize mass spectrometry on paired tumor-normal tissue samples to establish physiological ranges.\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"This study does not measure or report the absolute physiological concentration of inosine within the human tumor microenvironment (TME) or interstitial fluid. It evaluates the efficacy of administered supplementation rather than correlating baseline endogenous inosine levels with treatment outcomes. Consequently, the specific data regarding natural TME inosine concentrations and their statistical association with ICI efficacy (independent of supplementation) remain unavailable from this material.\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"unmet\",\"useful_material\":\"This study provides clinical evidence that exogenous inosine supplementation (0.2 g, three times/day) combined with PD-1/PD-L1 inhibitors significantly prolongs progression-free survival (median 7.00 months vs. 4.40 months; HR 0.63) compared to inhibitors alone in 172 patients with advanced solid tumors. It reports a trend toward improved objective response rate (26.7% vs. 15.1%) and an acceptable safety profile with reduced Grade 3-4 adverse reactions in the inosine group. Subgroup analyses indicate stronger PFS benefits in lung cancer patients and those with specific baseline inflammatory markers (e.g., low PLR/NLR).\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::16d078f32ef69dd5a1dca774\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"supplement_materials\"],\"value\":[{\"auxiliary_material\":\"The authors cite preclinical mechanisms in the background and discussion, including inosine's role in inhibiting UBA6 to increase tumor immunogenicity, serving as a carbon source for CD8+ T cells, and activating IFN-γ/TNF-α pathways. The study design is a single-center, prospective, randomized, open-label Phase 2 trial registered at ClinicalTrials.gov (NCT05809336). The dosage regimen and safety data support the feasibility of repurposing inosine as an adjunct therapy.\",\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-b532f13f7ac0c36c\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-trstv1th\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_23b146d5b5\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"Search for pharmacokinetic or metabolomic studies that specifically quantify baseline inosine levels in human tumor biopsies or plasma prior to immunotherapy initiation. Look for correlative analyses linking these endogenous measurements to clinical response (ORR/PFS/OS) without exogenous intervention. Consider reviewing studies that utilize mass spectrometry on paired tumor-normal tissue samples to establish physiological ranges.\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"This study does not measure or report the absolute physiological concentration of inosine within the human tumor microenvironment (TME) or interstitial fluid. It evaluates the efficacy of administered supplementation rather than correlating baseline endogenous inosine levels with treatment outcomes. Consequently, the specific data regarding natural TME inosine concentrations and their statistical association with ICI efficacy (independent of supplementation) remain unavailable from this material.\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"unmet\",\"useful_material\":\"This study provides clinical evidence that exogenous inosine supplementation (0.2 g, three times/day) combined with PD-1/PD-L1 inhibitors significantly prolongs progression-free survival (median 7.00 months vs. 4.40 months; HR 0.63) compared to inhibitors alone in 172 patients with advanced solid tumors. It reports a trend toward improved objective response rate (26.7% vs. 15.1%) and an acceptable safety profile with reduced Grade 3-4 adverse reactions in the inosine group. Subgroup analyses indicate stronger PFS benefits in lung cancer patients and those with specific baseline inflammatory markers (e.g., low PLR/NLR).\"}],\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8ea5b10c585bf0fccd8369c9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s166\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::17b5236c305aabb462e37fd0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d47d41f47a3b8d850aa49279\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::797d3a421d1f68362d67ff56\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用叙述性机制综述的方法，结合结构化文献检索。检索范围涵盖PubMed/MEDLINE、Embase和Scopus数据库（2010年1月至2026年3月）。筛选标准侧重于具有机制见解和临床应用价值的原创研究、临床试验和高影响力综述。数据提取聚焦于分类特征、生化通路和临床结果，并使用“机制框架分析”将发现归类为系统性免疫调节、局部肿瘤微环境变化和异生物质代谢。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fdbb1bb278c9d55b926ad36d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"系统性地整合了微生物组影响癌症治疗疗效和毒性的多种机制，包括代谢物介导的免疫调节、瘤内微生物群的直接药物相互作用以及性别特异性差异。\",\"limits\":\"作为叙述性综述，其证据等级依赖于所选文献的代表性和作者的解释框架；未提供新的原始实验数据或严格的荟萃分析统计结果；不同人群（如东西方）的微生物基线差异可能导致普适性限制。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b441a0e563eea1ef2fc56dea\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"接受免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的实体瘤患者\",\"finding\":\"特定的细菌组合（如Akkermansia muciniphila、Ruminococcaceae家族成员）及其产生的生物活性代谢物（肌苷、短链脂肪酸、色氨酸衍生物）是ICI成功的关键先决条件；抗生素使用与ICI疗效降低相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2ea197db957bf7d3cfdcc713\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"胰腺癌等实体瘤的微环境\",\"finding\":\"瘤内微生物群（主要是Gammaproteobacteria）表达胞苷脱氨酶（CDA），可将吉西他滨转化为无活性形式，导致化疗耐药；消除这些细菌可恢复药物疗效。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::509a27efd20b1e28804a2fdc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"全身免疫系统调节\",\"finding\":\"短链脂肪酸（特别是丁酸盐）作为组蛋白去乙酰化酶抑制剂，增强T细胞适应性；肌苷通过腺苷A2A受体信号通路增强Th1分化，绕过肿瘤微环境的抑制信号。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9e9df2e7f615e7f48d48fd7e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"异生物质代谢与毒性\",\"finding\":\"肠道细菌产生的β-葡萄糖醛酸酶可重新激活伊立替康，导致严重的黏膜损伤和腹泻；微生物特征可用于预测药物诱导的毒性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4b580cf8eb1d746db1a372d5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"造血干细胞移植（HSCT）后\",\"finding\":\"肠道微生物多样性丧失是移植相关死亡和移植物抗宿主病（GVHD）的独立风险因素；Blautia属与GVHD相关死亡率降低有关，而肠球菌属扩张加剧炎症。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f209ce7fa8f5c1d829658755\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7550f9285711774c6b8d8c12\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"现代肿瘤学正从将肿瘤视为孤立组织块转向将其视为复杂多物种生态系统的一部分。本研究旨在解决的关键问题是：微生物组（特别是肠道和瘤内微生物群）如何调节宿主抗肿瘤免疫，并具体通过哪些机制影响当前化疗和免疫治疗方案的疗效和毒性？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fa09930a8f323cd8b3d7bdfe\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"肿瘤治疗中的微生物组-宿主轴，涵盖肠道微生物群、瘤内微生物群及其对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）疗效和化疗毒性的影响。研究对象包括成人及儿科实体瘤和血液恶性肿瘤患者，涉及机制模型、临床队列和代谢组学数据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e69c0f1b8396d14a848d7c3e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇叙述性机制综述，旨在全面分析微生物组-宿主轴在癌症治疗中的作用。文章综合了57篇关键文献，探讨了特定细菌群落及其生物活性代谢物（如肌苷、短链脂肪酸、色氨酸衍生物）如何作为免疫检查点抑制剂成功的先决条件。此外，还讨论了细菌酶（如胞苷脱氨酶）在局部药物降解和化疗耐药中的作用，以及新兴的“微生物性别组”在治疗反应和毒性谱中的性别特异性差异。结论强调将微生物监测纳入标准临床协议对于个性化肿瘤治疗和长期生存质量的重要性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6a7cff23d275b7d35b240921\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物群如何调节实体瘤中免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）的疗效提供了详细的机制背景。它特别强调了特定细菌代谢物（如肌苷、SCFAs）和瘤内微生物酶（如CDA）的具体作用路径，这对于回答“微生物组如何调节ICI疗效”及其“介导机制”至关重要。同时，它也提供了关于抗生素使用、饮食干预和粪菌移植（FMT）等临床策略的背景信息。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4002992b9211ba4203b37df2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"主要基于综述引用的观察性研究和临床试验结果，具体关联强度因研究而异；未提供统一的量化效应值。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了特定肠道菌群（如Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium pseudolongum）与ICI疗效正相关的证据，以及抗生素使用导致疗效下降的观察结果。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3bca396122a57c5c6cb6d384\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制描述主要来源于体外实验和小鼠模型，部分在人体中的验证程度在所给材料中未完全交代；不同代谢物之间的协同作用细节有限。\",\"contribution\":\"详细阐述了肌苷通过A2A受体信号通路增强Th1分化的机制，以及短链脂肪酸（丁酸盐）通过表观遗传修饰和代谢重编程增强CD8+ T细胞功能的机制。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e8521b54ac3e1a3aea856bc8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"主要针对特定类型的化疗药物和特定肿瘤类型（如胰腺癌），其普遍性在其他实体瘤中尚需更多证据支持。\",\"contribution\":\"揭示了瘤内微生物群（如胰腺肿瘤中的Gammaproteobacteria）通过表达胞苷脱氨酶（CDA）直接降解化疗药物（吉西他滨）从而导致耐药的机制。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3968fa9c7bb42ff2c5b57f98\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"讨论部分提到儿童癌症幸存者长期存在的菌群改变与代谢综合征、肥胖等并发症的风险增加有关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::49b229ffc3f86574bd68db96\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"介绍“微生物性别组”概念，指出雌激素和雄激素可能通过影响肠道通透性和特定菌群丰度来调节治疗反应。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::29bc254425f7f72cdf267f30\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"总结了FMT克服ICI原发耐药性的临床试验结果，以及工程菌疗法的前景和风险。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a9b21bb5521d854910bc6f15\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述为叙述性综述，非系统评价或荟萃分析，因此其结论代表了作者的综合性观点而非严格的统计汇总。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::47ad2c025201af5d593c97c1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"所引用的机制研究多来自小鼠模型或体外实验，其在人体内的直接适用性和效力可能存在差异，需谨慎外推。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c02b5d6501d4c29b43a5f340\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"不同地理区域和饮食习惯导致的微生物基线差异可能影响某些菌群标志物的普适性，特别是在跨种族比较时。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9162fac3f0939bac1f86cf0b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"关于“微生物性别组”的内容较为新兴，具体机制和临床意义仍需更多研究证实，目前主要作为假设提出。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::876aed3948402262e111705c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0124\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s152\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b674221023c1dbcd1a299114\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c2620bcc444fc1598dd43ce6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0f036c918cd390f5edcdaebe\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用还原论视角，从生态水平的菌群相关性分析转向分子水平的机制解析。具体路线包括：1) 梳理建立相关性的大规模测序研究和动物模型实验；2) 验证相关性并识别宿主表型（如CD8+ T细胞浸润）；3) 深入探讨具体的分子机制，分为T细胞刺激、髓系细胞刺激和分子模拟三个子主题；4) 评估基于分子机制的工程化益生菌应用前景。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e6663c1509a79bf070ff83d5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"系统性地从分类学相关性过渡到分子机制，详细列举了多种微生物代谢物和蛋白质如何通过特定受体（GPCRs, A2AR, STING, NOD2, TLR5）和信号通路影响宿主免疫系统。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代具体的文献检索策略和纳入排除标准；主要依赖已发表的小鼠模型和少量临床数据，缺乏大规模前瞻性干预试验的直接证据；对于非细菌类微生物（真菌、古菌）及抑制性微生物的关注不足。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::efc4edd784b59555aab5bd43\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"小鼠模型及患者队列中的相关性研究\",\"finding\":\"特定细菌属（如双歧杆菌、拟杆菌、阿克曼氏菌、普拉梭菌）的存在与ICB疗效正相关，但不同研究间结果存在异质性，且相关性不等于因果性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::39351d21f351bf132aaa24af\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"粪菌移植（FMT）和单菌定植实验\",\"finding\":\"来自响应者的FMT可重现抗肿瘤效应，增加肿瘤内CD8+ T细胞浸润；特定菌株（如A. muciniphila, Bifidobacterium spp.）的单菌定植足以增强ICB疗效。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2a2ad8f127a3e2f7fb383b60\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）的作用\",\"finding\":\"SCFAs（如丁酸盐）对ICB的影响具有双重性：通常促进Treg和效应T细胞分化，但在某些情况下（如抗CTLA-4治疗）可能产生负面影响。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4abe48e8e01b0acc7b17e16a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"肌苷（Inosine）通路\",\"finding\":\"B. pseudolongum等产生的肌苷通过结合T细胞上的A2AR受体，协同TLR9激动剂增强抗CTLA-4疗效，但单独使用不足以完全重现表型。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::44f2d548690b4b10bf73e2c7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Akkermansia muciniphila与STING通路\",\"finding\":\"A. muciniphila产生cdAMP，激活STING信号，诱导I型干扰素产生，招募NK细胞和树突状细胞，从而增强抗肿瘤免疫。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e7fda87890cf100670bbed03\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Enterococcus sagA蛋白与NOD2通路\",\"finding\":\"肠球菌表达的SagA蛋白降解肽聚糖产生muropeptides，激活宿主NOD2受体，促进炎症环境和CD8+ T细胞浸润。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4a33dc878424e5c612918cf2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"分子模拟机制\",\"finding\":\"E. hirae中的噬菌体尾长测量蛋白（TMP）含有与宿主PSMB4蛋白相似的表位，引发交叉反应性CD8+ T细胞，增强抗PD-1疗效。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::41b69dd74275e596257e7f30\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4ecae2ad21b9875306feb272\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管已知特定微生物群与ICB疗效相关，但确切的分子机制尚不清楚，这限制了将微生物作为精准医疗手段加以利用的能力。本文试图回答：哪些具体的微生物分子特征（蛋白质、酶、代谢物）介导了这种调节作用？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::68dac395c061b642520773c2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"人类微生物群（特别是肠道菌群）与癌症免疫治疗中免疫检查点阻断（ICB，如抗PD-1/PD-L1和抗CTLA-4抗体）疗效之间的关系。研究范围涵盖从宏观的菌群组成相关性到微观的分子机制（代谢物、蛋白质、抗原模拟），以及基于这些机制的工程化益生菌策略。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c8095064895dfad406e569df\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述，旨在总结宿主-微生物相互作用在检查点抑制剂免疫治疗背景下的分子理解进展。文章首先回顾了通过小鼠模型和患者队列建立的菌群与ICB疗效之间的相关性，指出仅凭分类学关联难以确定因果关系。随后，重点阐述了具体的微生物分子机制，包括短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）、肌苷（inosine）、环二腺苷酸（cdAMP）、肽聚糖片段（muropeptides）和鞭毛蛋白（flagellin）如何分别通过T细胞刺激、髓系细胞激活或分子模拟来增强抗肿瘤免疫。最后，讨论了利用这些分子特征设计下一代工程化益生菌以改善治疗反应的潜力，并指出了当前研究在真菌/古菌、抑制性微生物及远端器官微生物方面的局限。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a33a88e41466a66d3f707572\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为解释肠道微生物群如何调节实体瘤免疫检查点阻断疗效提供了丰富的分子机制素材。它不仅列出了关键的关联物种，更重点揭示了具体的效应分子（如cdAMP, inosine, muropeptides）及其对应的宿主受体和信号通路，是构建“机制”部分的核心参考。同时，文中关于工程化益生菌的设计思路为讨论未来治疗策略提供了具体案例。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::599e6bf17709ba8cfbd90929\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这些机制大多基于小鼠模型或体外实验，部分已在早期临床试验中探索（如MRx0518），但尚未成为标准治疗指南；不同菌株间存在显著差异，不能简单外推至所有同种细菌。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物群影响ICB疗效的具体生物学途径和关键分子中介。例如，明确了A. muciniphila通过cdAMP-STING轴、肠球菌通过SagA-NOD2轴、以及双歧杆菌通过肌苷-A2AR轴增强抗肿瘤免疫的具体机制。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2a57617739887231108e77d5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制的复杂性在于多种微生物可能通过相同或不同的路径产生相似效果（冗余性），且单一代谢物往往不足以完全重现体内复杂的生态效应（如肌苷需配合TLR9激动剂）。\",\"contribution\":\"详细描述了介导效应的具体分子机制，包括代谢物（SCFAs, inosine, cdAMP）、蛋白质（SagA, flagellin）和抗原模拟（TMP）。解释了这些分子如何被宿主受体识别并触发下游信号级联反应（如I型干扰素产生、Th1分化、CD8+ T细胞浸润）。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4eb4f4671e999f3795550859\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述指出目前大多数研究集中在细菌，而忽略了真菌、古菌以及具有免疫抑制作用的负相关微生物；同时提到了远端器官（如肿瘤内部）微生物群的潜在作用。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::07f07877dcebdfd835240f4c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"对比了生态方法（FMT、饮食调整、定义菌群）与还原论方法（小分子、工程化益生菌）的优缺点。指出前者面临标准化和个体差异挑战，后者更具精准性但开发难度大。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3730e786b8b2831b6d7fa00a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的许多机制（如cdAMP, SagA）主要在小鼠模型中验证，其在人体内的确切效力和安全性仍需更多临床数据支持。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e90d9bb4a7244676654bef0a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"作者强调“还原论”方法的优势，但这并不意味着生态方法无效，两者应被视为互补而非对立。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3abfe02af60077a50b3004b3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"不同菌株甚至同一物种的不同菌株之间可能存在巨大的功能差异（如Bifidobacterium bifidum的不同菌株对PD-1阻断的影响不同），因此在引用具体机制时需严格限定菌株来源。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0d593217581a78566b8d13de\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"SCFAs（特别是丁酸盐）对ICB的影响具有情境依赖性（如对CTLA-4可能有负面作用），不能一概而论地认为其总是有益。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::54d4ead502cd94815f6b6dba\",\"source_handle\":\"P0251\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s187\",\"s107\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::47320b778a94a3f6e1bba0ee\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s061\",\"s286\",\"s214\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5b9018b036f8b7172a084833\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s061\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s214\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::eab85e6bee9c4b2fed5a5534\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e2c9835b96f8fc6dc09ac52b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\"limits\":\"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4f4f27ebf49eb4765b4072a3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\"finding\":\"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a1803946bf15951d555dd21c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\"finding\":\"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0698d1c77cb0d200e790e2f0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\"finding\":\"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::633e7982644fd55dc1491f2b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\"finding\":\"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7401efb4116390e74b3c0d15\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\"finding\":\"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c4c101d96abe914328c6abdc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s061\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s214\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5e3f0657dbc810fb682a25e8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f3675d08d336269e9d5f7b86\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1bc1f290c28d78622ffb8469\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::487a265dc168c8a0c9af82f3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"This review offers a structured framework for understanding how gut microbiota and metabolites modulate ICI efficacy and toxicity in solid tumors. It provides detailed mechanistic insights into specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO), along with an evaluation of clinical interventions like FMT and probiotics. It is particularly useful for mapping mechanistic pathways and identifying context-dependent biomarkers, while cautioning against universal generalizations due to cohort and methodological heterogeneity.\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e4fe0aec77d9cea7ccfbcb3b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\"contribution\":\"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bee8d56ffb923bd61271c4b9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\"contribution\":\"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2653a9eca08d3e9b4aabdd40\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6f7f1819fb2b6498ee2e73b4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::246f46b2e4daa7c0826508a1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::01a4eaf6f9130e6df88a4449\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c302f1d1ebc15fb248ecf95b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::297962d07c0123503e761a0c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4677960f83a51b4866588b1e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"supplement_material\"],\"value\":{\"auxiliary_material\":\"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_E_phase3_rct\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"State that no completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in ICI-treated patients was identified in this material. Note that the study is a narrative review summarizing preclinical and early-phase (I/II) evidence. Highlight that the authors explicitly call for future large-scale randomized controlled trials to validate findings, confirming the absence of such completed Phase III data in the current literature reviewed.\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"unmet\",\"useful_material\":\"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s061\",\"s286\",\"s214\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::368f88790e7cd7be69d3482e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"supplement_materials\"],\"value\":[{\"auxiliary_material\":\"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_E_phase3_rct\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"State that no completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in ICI-treated patients was identified in this material. Note that the study is a narrative review summarizing preclinical and early-phase (I/II) evidence. Highlight that the authors explicitly call for future large-scale randomized controlled trials to validate findings, confirming the absence of such completed Phase III data in the current literature reviewed.\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"unmet\",\"useful_material\":\"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"}],\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8d402e4e4dd606e12c0dadf8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-0c71639dc3330990d568\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-2c047b67f79872fa4042\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-2d4faf2da7bc361a24e6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"kind\":\"assets\",\"reason\":\"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\"status\":\"missing\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s056\",\"s286\",\"s060\",\"s208\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::782ec3f7244d0ab076658c3c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science Core Collection, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the effects of gut microbiota or metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction was guided by STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: first covering ICI mechanisms, then the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, followed by specific metabolite classes, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and finally microbiome-based interventions.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d7e9648a9d3a228b80acd4f6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut microbes and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, categorizing interventions by their molecular targets (STING, NOD2, AhR, etc.).\",\"limits\":\"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review acknowledges significant methodological heterogeneity across studies and notes that many proposed biomarkers and interventions require validation in large-scale, standardized longitudinal studies.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f6e33ef85bc9029ac9138418\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Melanoma patients treated with anti-CTLA-4 (ipilimumab)\",\"finding\":\"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (e.g., B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for antitumor efficacy.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::69bf00aad7ea27d8d011a5f9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"NSCLC patients treated with anti-PD-1\",\"finding\":\"High relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila (Akk-high) was associated with worse overall survival compared to Akk-low groups, challenging the binary 'good vs bad' bacteria concept and highlighting cohort/cancer-type dependency.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d3b8e49c5165f6a25f200eab\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Various ICI regimens\",\"finding\":\"Microbial influence is context-dependent; different ICIs rely on distinct microbial signatures (e.g., Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1 vs. Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4).\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f5a2ef1b4e9581d3a710c521\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Tryptophan metabolites (3-IAld, IPA)\",\"finding\":\"3-IAld alleviates colitis and enhances efficacy via AhR/IL-22; IPA provides cardioprotection via AhR/PI3K/AKT signaling.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::361feac329a052a7d78f53b7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"SCFAs (Butyrate, Propionate, Acetate)\",\"finding\":\"Butyrate protects against cardiotoxicity via PPARa-CYP4X1 and enhances antigen presentation via HDAC inhibition; Propionate/Acetate promote Treg homeostasis and memory CD8+ T-cell differentiation.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::120f673d74db8c5732a0396e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"TMAO\",\"finding\":\"Triggers immunogenic tumor cell death (pyroptosis) via PERK-GSDME pathway, recruiting CD8+ T cells.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1b3cf17eff823e01454721f6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Probiotics (LGG, BF839, Akk)\",\"finding\":\"LGG and BF839 activate cGAS-STING axis in dendritic cells to enhance CD8+ T cell infiltration; Akk produces c-di-AMP which directly activates STING.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0b0761c9932abc9ab5a5874d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"FMT interventions\",\"finding\":\"FMT from long-term responders to PD-1 therapy showed higher efficacy than healthy donors; response correlated with loss of deleterious baseline species rather than just engraftment of donor strains.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6c7424e735d637988d2eced9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"The clinical utility of ICIs is limited by interpatient variability in efficacy and the occurrence of systemic toxicities (irAEs). The review aims to systematically delineate the microbiome-metabolite-immune axis to understand these variations and optimize the balance between therapeutic gain and toxicity, ultimately guiding the development of precise microbial interventions.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b70d300ebe4f7a632702a5f0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"The review focuses on the gut microbiome and its metabolic byproducts as systemic regulators of immune function, specifically in the context of cancer immunotherapy using immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It covers mechanisms of ICI action (PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, TIM-3), the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions across different cancer types and cohorts, microbial metabolites (tryptophan derivatives, SCFAs, TMAO, inosine, bile acids, polyamines) as mediators of efficacy and toxicity, and microbiome-based interventions including probiotics, FMT, postbiotics, and dietary fiber.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e3b528b07174c7f2c4e9b9b5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and microbe-derived metabolites regulate the efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) of ICIs. It highlights specific taxa like Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, and Akkermansia muciniphila that potentiate therapeutic responses via pathways such as cGAS-STING and NOD2. The review also details how microbial metabolites protect organs like the heart and colon from inflammation while enhancing anti-tumor immunity. It evaluates emerging interventions like FMT and next-generation probiotics, noting that while preclinical and Phase I trials show feasibility, substantial hurdles remain regarding cohort heterogeneity, methodological standardization, and the need for large-scale longitudinal studies to establish reproducible predictive models.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7a16470a938828a019a65473\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Critiques the reliance on single-taxa abundance, advocates for topology-based approaches, and highlights logistical barriers like metagenomic turnaround times for precision nutrition.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bf0ea10d71d03a741315fcbb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Describes FMT from responders vs. healthy donors, encapsulation technologies for probiotics, and the double-edged nature of antibiotic preconditioning and high-fiber diets.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0cebf65ae6c2fb3a2b3291c3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Findings are based on a synthesis of various studies with differing methodologies; causal relationships are often inferred from preclinical models or observational data rather than definitive clinical trials.\",\"contribution\":\"Details the context-dependent nature of microbiome-ICI interactions, showing that beneficial taxa vary by cancer type and ICI regimen (e.g., Bacteroides for CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium for PD-1, variable role of Akk). It also discusses the trade-off between efficacy and toxicity, noting that some microbes protective in one context may be detrimental in another.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a2d90e74ef12c1e1106eacf6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Many mechanisms are described from murine models or in vitro studies; human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are noted as undefined.\",\"contribution\":\"Provides specific molecular mechanisms linking microbes/metabolites to immune modulation. For example, it describes how LGG and BF839 activate the cGAS-STING pathway, how tryptophan metabolites act via AhR, and how SCFAs influence T-cell function and barrier integrity through epigenetic and receptor-mediated pathways.\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::86223da55d78e8184ad44dcf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"This review offers a structured framework for understanding the 'gut-metabolite-immune' axis in the context of solid tumor immunotherapy. It provides detailed mechanistic insights into how specific microbial taxa and metabolites modulate ICI efficacy and toxicity, serving as a valuable resource for explaining biological mechanisms and contextualizing clinical heterogeneity. It also summarizes the current state of microbiome-based interventions, highlighting both promising strategies and translational barriers.\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::74ec76742b9f6daf3762643e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide quantitative meta-analytic results; effect sizes and statistical significance should not be inferred from this text alone.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::995110f30544c2be6aece91c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models (mice) or small clinical cohorts; extrapolation to broader human populations requires caution.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b16eb73c69f940a7edbd13bf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The role of specific microbes (e.g., Akkermansia) can be context-dependent and even contradictory across studies; avoid treating any single taxon as universally beneficial or detrimental.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8d7b3fab2b1cb1884ae2d02d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Claims about the efficacy of interventions like FMT or probiotics are primarily based on early-phase trials or preclinical data; robust clinical validation is still needed.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::de02bcabb5761d1a2aab77da\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A_variants\"],\"value\":[{\"approach\":\"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\"contribution_and_limits\":[{\"contribution\":\"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\"limits\":\"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"}],\"key_findings\":[{\"conditions\":\"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\"finding\":\"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"},{\"conditions\":\"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\"finding\":\"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"},{\"conditions\":\"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\"finding\":\"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"},{\"conditions\":\"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\"finding\":\"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"},{\"conditions\":\"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\"finding\":\"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"}],\"paper_kind\":\"review\",\"problem_or_question\":\"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\"research_scope\":\"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\"work_summary\":\"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\"}],\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1431bb03ae021761d8f92368\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B_variants\"],\"value\":[{\"broader_review_uses\":[{\"connection_to_review\":\"Sets the stage for why microbiome modulation is a critical area of research in overcoming ICI limitations.\",\"material\":\"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\",\"purpose\":\"Contextual background on ICI mechanisms and limitations\"},{\"connection_to_review\":\"Provides evidence on the feasibility and challenges of translating microbiome science into clinical practice, highlighting the gap between preclinical success and clinical implementation.\",\"material\":\"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\",\"purpose\":\"Evaluation of microbiome-based interventions\"},{\"connection_to_review\":\"Offers a critical perspective on the current state of the field, suggesting areas where future research needs to improve reproducibility and causal inference.\",\"material\":\"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\",\"purpose\":\"Methodological considerations and future directions\"}],\"facet_contributions\":[{\"boundaries\":\"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\"contribution\":\"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\",\"possible_uses\":\"Can be used to support arguments about the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions and the lack of a universal 'good' microbiome signature. Provides specific examples of taxa to discuss in the context of patient stratification.\"},{\"boundaries\":\"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\"contribution\":\"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\",\"possible_uses\":\"Provides mechanistic depth for explaining how the gut microbiome influences ICI efficacy and toxicity. Useful for discussing specific signaling pathways (STING, NOD2, AhR, NF-κB) and their role in remodeling the tumor microenvironment and protecting distal organs.\"}],\"planning_summary\":\"This review offers a structured framework for understanding how gut microbiota and metabolites modulate ICI efficacy and toxicity in solid tumors. It provides detailed mechanistic insights into specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO), along with an evaluation of clinical interventions like FMT and probiotics. It is particularly useful for mapping mechanistic pathways and identifying context-dependent biomarkers, while cautioning against universal generalizations due to cohort and methodological heterogeneity.\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\":[\"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\"],\"topic_handles\":[\"gut microbiome composition and diversity\",\"immune checkpoint inhibitors (PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT)\",\"microbial metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO, bile acids)\",\"immune-related adverse events (irAEs)\",\"fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT)\",\"probiotics and postbiotics\",\"precision nutrition and dietary fiber\",\"cGAS-STING pathway\",\"NOD2 signaling\",\"aryl hydrocarbon receptor (AhR)\"]}],\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bd2a31924b2f1b7a5c0db505\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s061\",\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2088384ebad86f83dd115cc2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s060\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::182a456925359bd5e4cb6b24\",\"source_handle\":\"P0333\",\"field_path\":[\"local_passages\"],\"value\":{\"external_calls\":0,\"passages\":[{\"best_sentence\":\"The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed.\",\"card_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\"limits\":[],\"match_terms\":[\"粪菌移植\",\"益生菌\",\"机制\",\"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\",\"mechanisms mediate effect\",\"ici\",\"i\",\"ii\",\"iii\",\"nsclc\",\"rct\"],\"material_depth\":\"fulltext\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:290154100\",\"pool_action\":\"already_in_pool\",\"reading_path\":\"\",\"score\":120.720283,\"section_path\":[\"Supplementary question reading\"],\"segment_kind\":\"directed_content\",\"source_handle\":\"P0584\",\"text\":\"{\\\"auxiliary_material\\\": \\\"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": [], \\\"gap_id\\\": \\\"case_E_phase3_rct\\\", \\\"judgment_path\\\": \\\"F:\\\\\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\\\\\outputs\\\\\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\\\\\03_external_closure\\\\\\\\runs\\\\\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\\\\\source_units\\\\\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\\\", \\\"limitations\\\": [], \\\"material_ready\\\": true, \\\"material_usefulness\\\": \\\"suppor…\",\"title\":\"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"usable_fields\":[],\"year\":\"2026\"},{\"best_sentence\":\"The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\"card_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\"limits\":[],\"match_terms\":[\"粪菌移植\",\"益生菌\",\"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\"],\"material_depth\":\"fulltext\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:290154100\",\"pool_action\":\"already_in_pool\",\"reading_path\":\"\",\"score\":17.613751,\"section_path\":[\"general understanding\",\"work summary\"],\"segment_kind\":\"card_work_summary\",\"source_handle\":\"P0584\",\"text\":\"taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. m, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\"title\":\"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"usable_fields\":[],\"year\":\"2026\"}],\"question\":\"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect? 微生物干预策略的临床转化现状 系统评估粪菌移植（FMT）、活体生物药（LBPs）、益生菌及饮食干预在实体瘤 ICI 治疗中的临床试验数据，区分初治与难治人群的疗效差异，明确证据等级（I/II 期 vs III 期），并分析供体选择、安全性及标准化挑战。 涵盖人体临床试验（I-III 期），聚焦实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、CRC 等）。包括 FMT（供体来源、给药途径）、定义菌群（如 CBM588、MRx0518）、益生菌及饮食干预。明确排除纯临床前研究（除非用于解释机制背景）及非 ICI 背景的微生物干预。严格区分观察性关联与干预性因果证据，标注试验设计类型（单臂 vs RCT）及人群特征（初治 vs 经治）。\",\"reading_mode\":\"focused_local_search\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s214\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9cb666a107fc8e343e94fb0e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cca7c1de9f7fc15ee3968e02\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::972e64916e571eefa7631020\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"研究采用多步骤实验设计：首先，使用六种临床相关抗生素处理C57BL/6J小鼠，建立不同的肠道菌群和代谢组状态，并结合ICT治疗评估肿瘤生长；其次，利用液相色谱-质谱联用技术（LC-MS）对粪便、血清和肿瘤组织进行非靶向代谢组学 profiling，筛选与肿瘤负荷相关的代谢物，并通过靶向定量验证候选分子（TDCA）；再次，通过体内回补实验测试不同胆汁酸对抗生素诱导的ICT低响应的挽救作用；接着，利用单细胞RNA测序（scRNA-seq）、流式细胞术和多因子蛋白检测分析肿瘤微环境中免疫细胞亚群的变化；最后，通过抗体耗竭实验确定关键效应细胞，并利用OT-I转基因小鼠模型和TGR5拮抗剂（SBI-115）在体外和体内验证TDCA通过TGR5受体直接增强CD8+ T细胞细胞毒性的机制。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::04d1653e627f38a25eb88134\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"识别出微生物衍生的胆汁酸TDCA是连接抗生素诱导的菌群紊乱与ICT低响应的关键代谢介质。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代TDCA在人体内的确切药代动力学特征及长期安全性数据；机制研究主要在预临床小鼠模型中进行，人类相关性主要基于之前的回顾性临床关联数据，缺乏前瞻性患者验证。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e73cb7c8039043ab17f7ea02\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"证明了单一微生物代谢物的补充即可逆转抗生素引起的免疫治疗失效，无需重建整个微生物组。\",\"limits\":\"未明确驱动TDCA丧失的具体微生物类群和酶促途径；TGR5的作用可能涉及其他细胞类型，本研究主要依赖药理学拮抗剂而非基因敲除，无法完全排除脱靶效应或其他细胞类型的贡献。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a8acea12fabd6b703f06ba14\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"阐明了TDCA通过TGR5受体直接增强CD8+ T细胞细胞毒性的新机制，区别于其他代谢物对T细胞分化的间接调节。\",\"limits\":\"TDCA对CD8+ T细胞下游的具体信号转导通路（如cAMP-PKA-mTOR）尚未完全阐明；TDCA的疗效可能具有肿瘤类型、免疫背景和剂量依赖性，其在其他实体瘤中的普适性需进一步验证。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7fea3693f3c5f89fd8b539c0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"C57BL/6J小鼠接种B16-F10黑色素瘤细胞，接受青霉素/链霉素（Pen/Strep）等抗生素处理及ICT治疗\",\"finding\":\"Pen/Strep处理显著减少肠道细菌总量并改变菌群结构，导致肿瘤体积增大和生存期缩短，表明抗生素特异性地降低了ICT的疗效而非直接影响肿瘤 intrinsic 生长。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8437e3e49f9c6298637b1691\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"非靶向代谢组学分析与临床数据交叉验证\",\"finding\":\"抗生素处理重塑了宿主代谢组，其中牛磺脱氧胆酸（TDCA）在肿瘤、血清和盲肠内容物中呈现一致的变化趋势，且在人类黑色素瘤ICT响应者中富集，被鉴定为ICT响应的关键代谢物。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4a5fd9f87fca22b5def42a90\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Pen/Strep处理后靶向定量肿瘤内胆汁酸\",\"finding\":\"抗生素处理导致肿瘤内初级结合胆汁酸（如TCDCA）增加，而微生物衍生的次级胆汁酸TDCA显著耗竭。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3ce8b9357b67d5a78510ea79\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"在抗生素+ICT背景下，向肿瘤内局部注射五种受抗生素影响的胆汁酸\",\"finding\":\"仅TDCA补充能显著抑制肿瘤生长并延长生存期，且仅在抗生素存在时发挥挽救作用，不影响无抗生素背景下的ICT疗效。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d4be51fd1e5e2dbe963267ba\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"在E0771乳腺癌模型和人源化NSG-SGM3小鼠A375黑色素瘤模型中补充TDCA\",\"finding\":\"TDCA补充在多种肿瘤模型中均能克服抗生素诱导的ICT低响应，显示其效应的广泛性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c795da1eca5470b6d5a3d608\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"单细胞RNA测序与流式细胞术分析肿瘤浸润免疫细胞\",\"finding\":\"TDCA处理增加了肿瘤内效应CD8+ T细胞、γδ T细胞和NK细胞的比例，减少了耗竭型CD8+ T细胞，并提高了IFN-γ、TNF-α和颗粒酶B等效应细胞因子的水平。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f703234a9a62db92de4c7264\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"CD4+ T细胞、CD8+ T细胞或NK细胞特异性耗竭实验\",\"finding\":\"CD8+ T细胞的完全耗竭消除了TDCA的抗肿瘤效应，证明CD8+ T细胞是TDCA介导肿瘤控制的主要效应细胞。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f500276a42430cc5a45e0812\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"OT-I转基因小鼠CD8+ T细胞体外杀伤实验及过继转移\",\"finding\":\"TDCA直接增强抗原特异性CD8+ T细胞的细胞毒性，促进靶细胞死亡；过继转移经TDCA处理的CD8+ T细胞可延缓肿瘤生长。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c862a9f0e53059cee0615b43\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"TGR5/FXR/VDR报告基因 assay 及体内TGR5拮抗剂（SBI-115）干预\",\"finding\":\"TDCA主要激活TGR5受体；药理学阻断TGR5可抵消TDCA对肿瘤生长的控制和CD8+ T细胞的效应功能，证实TDCA通过TGR5信号通路发挥作用。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fed6a02f4d94d96a258ecee9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8711e939876d048b7fecf9e5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"抗生素诱导的肠道菌群紊乱如何具体导致免疫检查点疗法（ICT）的低响应？是否存在特定的微生物衍生代谢物能够介导这一过程，并可通过补充该代谢物来逆转抗生素引起的免疫治疗失效？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5890e6775c83a71dc398f9a5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"本研究以小鼠黑色素瘤（B16-F10）、乳腺癌（E0771）及人源化小鼠黑色素瘤模型为研究对象，聚焦于抗生素干扰肠道菌群后对免疫检查点疗法（ICT）疗效的影响。研究范围涵盖多种临床常用抗生素的扰动效应、肿瘤微环境中的代谢组学变化、CD8+ T细胞的免疫反应机制以及特定微生物代谢物（TDCA）的替代治疗潜力。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::772b8bb0a0da67855f9d96c9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"该研究旨在解决抗生素使用导致癌症患者对免疫检查点疗法（ICT）低响应这一临床难题，探究其背后的微生物介导机制。作者通过联合应用多株抗生素扰动小鼠模型与非靶向代谢组学分析，识别出微生物衍生的次级胆汁酸牛磺脱氧胆酸（TDCA）作为ICT响应的关键决定因子。研究发现，抗生素（特别是青霉素/链霉素）显著降低肿瘤内TDCA水平，而外源性补充TDCA足以克服抗生素引起的ICT低响应，并在多种肿瘤模型中恢复抗肿瘤免疫。机制上，TDCA不直接作用于肿瘤细胞，而是通过结合TGR5受体，直接增强CD8+ T细胞的效应功能和细胞毒性。这项工作确立了“微生物代谢物-TGR5-CD8+ T细胞”轴在维持ICT疗效中的作用，并提出代谢物替代疗法作为缓解抗生素相关免疫治疗失效的策略。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::88ba99020e4af86bb1f71d78\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文提供了关于肠道微生物代谢物调控免疫检查点疗法（ICT）疗效的具体机制证据。它特别适用于解释抗生素如何通过耗竭特定有益代谢物（TDCA）来削弱ICT疗效，并展示了代谢物替代疗法作为一种可行的干预策略。对于综述而言，它提供了从‘菌群-代谢物-宿主免疫’角度解析ICT响应变异的详细案例，特别是针对抗生素干扰这一常见临床情境。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b486452b9ed92fdf3585969b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"主要基于小鼠模型，且针对的是特定抗生素组合和黑色素瘤/乳腺癌模型，不同抗生素种类和肿瘤类型的效果可能存在差异。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了抗生素干扰肠道菌群导致ICT疗效下降的具体代谢机制：抗生素（如Pen/Strep）导致微生物衍生的次级胆汁酸TDCA在肿瘤内耗竭，从而削弱抗肿瘤免疫。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3b164cce26337f952c15d4f4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制验证依赖于TGR5药理学拮抗剂，未排除其他潜在受体或细胞类型的作用；下游信号通路细节尚不明确。\",\"contribution\":\"揭示了TDCA通过直接结合TGR5受体，增强CD8+ T细胞的效应功能和细胞毒性，从而恢复ICT疗效的分子机制。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::511c6539987cda5f95a9cca8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"目前仅为概念验证，缺乏人体临床试验数据支持；需考虑代谢物的给药途径、剂量及稳定性问题。\",\"contribution\":\"提出了‘代谢物替代疗法’作为克服抗生素相关ICT低响应的潜在策略，证明了补充单一代谢物TDCA即可恢复疗效。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b0576011fdd7240f5fca0ecb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文中讨论了其他胆汁酸（如DCA、UDCA）在不同肿瘤背景下对免疫的不同影响（抑制或促进），以及其它代谢物（如肌醇、短链脂肪酸）的作用机制。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::107a3be4bd8567f3889b635f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文中指出不同抗生素对菌群和代谢组的扰动程度不同，导致ICT响应差异，这解释了为何临床研究中抗生素对免疫治疗的影响不一致。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7d029ff36f9ec29b337e4298\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"讨论部分指出代谢物替代避免了活菌疗法的定植困难、安全性和监管复杂性等问题。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::870daf920ef09f8d06d5dd8d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该研究的机制结论主要基于小鼠模型，虽然引用了之前的人类队列数据作为关联支持，但TDCA在人体内的确切疗效和安全性尚未在本研究中得到前瞻性验证。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0cd327c27a8ebee5fd1f368a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"TDCA的作用依赖于TGR5受体，但其下游信号通路（如cAMP-PKA-mTOR）的具体运作机制在本研究中仅为推测，需结合后续研究谨慎解读。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c333cd1be808b2bc7d897b03\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"不同胆汁酸在不同肿瘤类型中具有相反的免疫调节作用（如DCA在结直肠癌中抑制免疫，而在本研究中TDCA在黑色素瘤中促进免疫），因此在跨肿瘤类型推广时需特别注意上下文差异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bd7fef3939ea77630336d1de\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"抗生素对ICT的影响并非均一，不同抗生素导致的菌群和代谢组变化不同，因此不能简单地将所有抗生素视为同等负面因素。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8cf778affe1781ab11c7d82a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0481\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-8c71e871c7aa5482d545\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-f85da31c482f020fe5f7\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-a7a6e9bd3a48b1fef12e\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-12c6cac6a4bef2539d08\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-02faf8b9fedd6313c05e\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-3aa25875e4222837763e\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s048\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::845f1f0f9faa43750eb0252c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3e029480226395ee65355068\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a150faa5f38ad58aa803aa87\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"1. 队列构建：前瞻性招募uHCC患者，严格排除近期使用抗生素、益生菌等干扰因素者。分为训练集（OR vs PD，n=20 vs 21）和验证集（n=33）。 2. 样本处理：收集治疗前新鲜粪便，-80°C保存。 3. 微生物组分析：提取DNA，扩增16S rRNA V3-V4区，Illumina MiSeq测序。使用QIIME进行OTU聚类，SILVA数据库注释。计算Alpha多样性（Shannon, PD whole tree），Beta多样性（PCoA, Bray-Curtis, PERMANOVA）。使用LEfSe鉴定差异菌属。 4. 代谢物分析：LC-MS检测39种胆汁酸，HPLC检测短链脂肪酸。 5. 统计分析：相关性分析（Spearman）关联菌群与代谢物。ROC曲线确定最佳截断值。Kaplan-Meier法和Log-rank检验评估生存差异。Cox比例风险模型进行多变量生存分析。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0f3ad86f29db4aec656ccb78\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"首次在包含验证队列的HCC研究中，确立了基线肠道微生物组（特别是Lachnoclostridium/Prevotella 9平衡）和次级胆汁酸（UDCA/UCA）与ICI治疗疗效及生存期的关联。\",\"limits\":\"观察性研究，无法确立因果关系；机制需体外实验验证；主要基于病毒相关HCC，外推至非病毒性HCC需谨慎；未涵盖当前一线标准疗法（阿替利珠单抗+贝伐珠单抗）；缺乏动态监测和免疫微环境（如PBMC）数据。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::205a3810c4b95c603021af2d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"训练集（OR vs PD）\",\"finding\":\"OR患者粪便中Lachnoclostridium、Lachnospiraceae和Veillonella富集；PD患者中Prevotella 9富集。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::17127989af6f9015ee06d3c1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"训练集（OR vs PD）\",\"finding\":\"OR患者粪便中次级胆汁酸（UDCA, UCA, MDCA）显著高于PD患者；SCFA无显著差异。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0658b769e832eb1ea64e6389\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"相关性分析\",\"finding\":\"UDCA、UCA、MDCA的浓度与Lachnoclostridium丰度呈正相关，与Prevotella 9丰度呈负相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::81de4c9543a29d42bda91fff\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"生存分析（训练集）\",\"finding\":\"Lachnoclostridium高丰度且Prevotella 9低丰度的“良好”微生物特征组合显著预测更好的总生存期（OS）。在多变量Cox模型中，该特征仍是OS的独立预测因子。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0d88cc9ec2296d5ef9927be6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"验证集\",\"finding\":\"具有“良好”微生物特征的患者表现出更长的无进展生存期（PFS: 8.8 vs 1.8个月）和总生存期（OS: 未达vs 6.5个月，p<0.001）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ece6acafa06099b8b6423101\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::60020e34ec4b8c77e0d8f810\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"目前缺乏有效的生物标志物来预测uHCC患者对ICI治疗的反应。尽管有证据表明肠道微生物群可能调节肿瘤对免疫治疗的反应，但在HCC中的具体作用尚不明确。本研究试图回答：uHCC患者的基线肠道微生物组和代谢物是否与ICI治疗结局相关？能否识别出预测生存期的微生物特征？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0201844e7f6258c10ee9924c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"不可切除肝细胞癌（uHCC）患者，接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗；比较客观缓解（OR）、疾病进展（PD）及健康对照者的粪便微生物组与代谢物。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::15e6a333c649c99338c34cf2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本研究旨在探索肠道微生物群及其代谢产物作为预测uHCC患者ICI治疗疗效的生物标志物的潜力。研究采用前瞻性队列设计，在2018年5月至2020年2月期间，纳入94名初治uHCC患者，收集治疗前粪便样本。通过16S rRNA基因测序分析微生物组成，并通过LC-MS和HPLC分析胆汁酸（BA）和短链脂肪酸（SCFA）。训练集包含20例OR患者和21例PD患者，验证集为33例Child-Pugh A级患者。研究发现，基线时OR与PD患者的肠道菌群存在显著差异，特定菌属丰度及次级胆汁酸水平与治疗效果相关，且特定的微生物特征组合可独立预测总生存期（OS）。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::64bf9d437d1ef2ca6cb18e4b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文提供了关于肠道微生物群如何关联于实体瘤（具体为HCC）中ICI疗效的具体临床证据。它识别了特定的细菌属（Lachnoclostridium, Prevotella 9）和代谢物（次级胆汁酸）作为疗效预测因子，并提出了“微生物-胆汁酸轴”的可能联系。对于综述而言，这篇论文是连接“微生物组成”与“临床预后”的重要实证材料，特别适用于讨论HCC亚型中的特异性微生物特征及其与代谢物的耦合关系。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::326b44aebea94784d1e576bd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅限于uHCC人群；主要基于抗PD-1/PD-L1单药或联合TKI治疗，未直接验证阿替利珠单抗+贝伐珠单抗方案；关联性强于因果性。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了具体的微生物特征（Lachnoclostridium富集 + Prevotella 9耗竭）与uHCC患者ICI治疗客观缓解率（ORR）和无进展生存期（PFS）的正向关联证据。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::83aec2be22646133caa52f92\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"相关性而非因果性；机制假设（Clostridium scindens的作用）未被本实验直接证实，仅引用文献支持；未测量免疫细胞浸润或细胞因子水平以直接验证免疫调节机制。\",\"contribution\":\"揭示了特定细菌（Lachnoclostridium）与特定代谢物（次级胆汁酸UDCA/UCA）之间的强正相关性，并指出这些胆汁酸在响应者中富集。作者推测Lachnoclostridium可能通过转化CDCA生成具有化学预防作用的UDCA来介导效应。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::85a98285bb070f39fc5b770b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"引言部分回顾了HCC流行病学、ICI治疗现状（响应率16-20%）、现有生物标志物（PD-L1, CTNNB1, AFP）的局限性，以及肠道微生物群在其他癌症（黑色素瘤）中调节免疫治疗效果的已有证据。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9891353d147403f3d76c46ee\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"详细的16S rRNA测序流程、代谢物提取与分析方法、统计模型（LEfSe, Cox回归）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b157a758206c4af9a002c10c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该研究的发现主要基于台湾地区的病毒相关HCC患者，可能不适用于非病毒性HCC或其他种族群体。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8540bbaebe850fd2e0ab6a37\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"验证队列规模较小（n=33），且主要为Child-Pugh A级，限制了其在晚期肝病人群中的普适性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e0f143e6499a564f8b9b8c38\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"研究未区分ICI单药与联合治疗（如ICI+TKI）对微生物组的潜在不同影响，尽管分析显示既往TKI暴露未显著混淆结果，但联合治疗本身可能改变肠道环境。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a0bee8c0a20e76b35b352b7a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"作者声称的“首次包含验证队列”需注意其语境，即针对HCC ICI治疗这一特定细分领域，而非整个微生物组领域。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bde1cd61b2336480314a8bed\",\"source_handle\":\"P0424\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s182\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4a28d5e97bd70ca15780b288\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"abstract\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::44e2883db3f80d2e4ff54fcb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2b1327a2e56c81674bf43a74\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"1. 临床观察基础：引用BEWEL试验，确立BRB饮食富集毛螺菌科与增强ICI疗效的关联。 2. 体内功能验证：在C57BL/6小鼠异种移植模型（MC38细胞）中，分别单独补充三种毛螺菌科菌株（B. obeum, B. massiliensis, A. rectalis），并与IgG对照组及抗PD-1治疗组比较，评估其对ICI抗肿瘤活性的影响。 3. 比较基因组学分析：提取这三种菌株的全基因组序列，使用KEGGREST映射和clusterProfiler进行过度代表测试，以所有基因组编码的KO为背景，识别B. obeum和B. massiliensis共有但A. rectalis缺失的177个KEGG正交ologs。 4. 通路注释与机制推断：将识别出的独特KO映射到KEGG通路，重点分析与免疫代谢相关的四类通路（乙酸产生、维生素合成、细胞壁修饰、胆汁酸转化），以此推断潜在的生物学机制。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7f6c2dda0eed5148ca99cf62\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了具体的因果证据链：从临床饮食干预（BRB）到特定菌群富集，再到单一菌株的功能验证（B. obeum/massiliensis有效 vs A. rectalis无效），最后通过比较基因组学锁定潜在机制基因集。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代具体的肿瘤抑制率数据、统计学显著性水平、菌株定植效率验证细节、以及体内代谢物（如乙酸、维生素、胆汁酸）的实际浓度测量结果。机制推断主要基于基因组存在性，而非直接的代谢产物功能验证或宿主免疫细胞表型的直接检测。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::49075a4aa403451e95cfd0e7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"在小鼠异种移植模型中，单独补充B. obeum或B. massiliensis，联合抗PD-1治疗\",\"finding\":\"显著改善了ICI的抗肿瘤有效性\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d890857321a53b0ea271e5dc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"在小鼠异种移植模型中，单独补充A. rectalis，联合抗PD-1治疗\",\"finding\":\"未观察到对ICI有效性的改善\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e07affb6db39f836d72263d6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"比较B. obeum, B. massiliensis与A. rectalis的基因组\",\"finding\":\"鉴定出177个仅在有效菌株（B. obeum, B. massiliensis）中存在而在无效菌株（A. rectalis）中缺失的KEGG正交ologs\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::52462292839e9c73194026ae\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"对这177个独特KO进行KEGG通路富集分析\",\"finding\":\"发现四个关键通路：(1) Wood-Ljungdahl途径基因（产乙酸，T细胞能量来源）；(2) 叶酸(B9)和钴胺素(B12)合成基因（支持T细胞增殖）；(3) L-鼠李糖合成基因（细胞壁装饰，激活先天免疫）；(4) 胆汁酸转化为次级异构胆汁酸的基因（调节FXR/TGR5受体，影响Th17/Treg平衡）\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3b0923f43402a3ad6c97f803\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7247ccac03a0e89f056f79d4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管已知肠道微生物组影响ICI疗效，且BRB饮食能富集毛螺菌科并增强疗效，但具体是哪些毛螺菌科菌株起作用，以及它们通过何种分子机制介导这种疗效增强？特别是为何某些菌株有效而其他近缘菌株无效？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::16c32a22f7ba956f404fab1f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"研究对象为肠道共生菌毛螺菌科（Lachnospiraceae）中的特定菌株，包括 Blautia obeum、Blautia massiliensis 和 Agathobacter rectalis。情境涉及小鼠异种移植模型（MC38结肠癌细胞），干预措施包括饮食补充黑覆盆子汁（BRB）以富集微生物组，以及单独补充上述三种菌株。主要测量方式包括肿瘤生长对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI，抗PD-1）的反应、细菌基因组比较分析（KEGG正交ologs）、通路富集分析。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a82dcd72572ecce43a444ce9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"该研究旨在探究毛螺菌科成员如何影响免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）的疗效。基于BEWELL试验中BRB饮食能富集毛螺菌科并增强小鼠ICI抗肿瘤活性的背景，作者进一步通过单菌株补充实验，比较了三种相关菌株（B. obeum, B. massiliensis, A. rectalis）对ICI疗效的影响差异。研究发现前两种菌株能改善ICI效果，而后者不能。随后，通过对这三种菌株进行全基因组比较，识别出仅在前两种有效菌株中存在而在无效菌株中缺失的177个KEGG正交ologs。通过KEGG通路分析，这些独特基因被归类为四个与免疫和ICI反应相关的代谢/信号通路：乙酰辅酶A合成（Wood-Ljungdahl途径）、T细胞增殖所需维生素（叶酸B9和钴胺素B12）合成、L-鼠李糖合成（作为微生物相关分子模式激活先天免疫），以及胆汁酸转化为次级异构胆汁酸以调节Th17/Treg平衡。结论认为，BRB响应的毛螺菌科拥有富集的代谢和免疫调节基因程序，这可能解释了其与改善ICI肿瘤反应的关联。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2564653167b42e4ba3cc5f11\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文为综述提供了关于肠道微生物组调节ICI疗效的具体菌株特异性证据和潜在分子机制假设。它特别有价值地展示了如何通过比较有效与无效的近缘菌株来缩小机制研究的范围，并提出了四种具体的代谢/信号通路作为候选机制。这对于回答“哪些菌群成分重要”以及“可能的作用机制是什么”这两个子问题具有直接参考价值。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e86addc4efe0be3602bff7ba\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅限于毛螺菌科内的三个特定菌株；未涵盖其他门类的细菌；未提供人类临床试验的直接疗效数据，仅为小鼠模型和基因组关联。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了毛螺菌科内部不同菌株对ICI疗效影响的差异性证据。明确指出并非所有毛螺菌科成员都能增强ICI疗效，只有特定的Blautia物种（obeum, massiliensis）有效，而Agathobacter rectalis无效。这有助于在综述中细化“有益菌群”的定义，避免将毛螺菌科视为同质化整体。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::14bd5d132f3dc0569f4cb4e9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这些机制是基于基因组存在的预测（in silico），尚未在体内通过代谢物测量或基因敲除实验得到直接验证。例如，未证明乙酸确实达到了影响T细胞的浓度，也未证明L-鼠李糖确实发挥了MAMP作用。\",\"contribution\":\"提出了四种具体的潜在分子机制路径，基于基因组比较发现的有效菌株特有基因：(1) 乙酸生产（Wood-Ljungdahl途径）作为T细胞能量源；(2) 叶酸和钴胺素合成促进T细胞增殖；(3) L-鼠李糖合成作为MAMP激活先天免疫；(4) 胆汁酸转化调节Th17/Treg平衡。这些为理解微生物如何代谢调控宿主免疫提供了具体的生化线索。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::74e4dd989470e23c5e5af4a3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"BEWELL试验中BRB饮食富集毛螺菌科并增强ICI疗效的背景信息。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2ae9be8be2de26595260ab12\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"同一科内不同菌株对ICI疗效的不同影响（B. obeum/massiliensis vs A. rectalis）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::de9177c122051996908b7278\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该研究的机制结论完全基于基因组比对和通路富集分析，属于相关性或预测性证据，而非功能性验证。在综述中引用其机制部分时，应明确标注为“基因组预测的潜在机制”，而非已证实的生理机制。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bba4b9f5c75ccc1842a8848d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"研究对象为小鼠模型，且使用的是异种移植模型（MC38），其结果外推到人类实体瘤患者时需考虑物种差异和模型局限性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ccda48a2f8526b4cad07a206\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"仅涉及毛螺菌科内的三个菌株，不能代表整个肠道微生物组或毛螺菌科的全部多样性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::64dad4e04750325d5179277e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0186\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"no complete research body was indexed\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\"status\":\"partial\"}],\"material_scope\":\"abstract_only\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s176\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::028a1861bdb16c7dd44cc9f9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c188ef7c4a1b0e02639c83b6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::67c0059d7cc001159ec223da\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用系统性文献回顾与综合的方法。首先概述胆汁酸的生物学特性（合成、循环、微生物修饰）；其次，深入讨论微生物修饰胆汁酸对局部和全身效应的影响，重点分析FXR和TGR5等关键信号通路；接着，基于上述机制，归纳该轴在代谢紊乱、肝病、免疫失调和癌症等疾病发病机制中的贡献；最后，讨论靶向胆汁酸信号和肠道微生物群的 emerging therapeutic strategies（包括药物、饮食、益生菌/FMT），并指出未来研究方向。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::85de1bb0261a846dba4da0ee\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了胆汁酸-微生物-FXR轴的全面机制框架，整合了从基础生化到临床疾病的多个层面，特别强调了微生物衍生胆汁酸对新型受体（如RORγt, VDR）的调节作用。\",\"limits\":\"作为综述，其结论依赖于已发表的研究，未提供新的实验数据。部分机制（如特定微生物胆汁酸的长期安全性、组织特异性FXR调节的临床转化）仍存在争议或不确定性，需更多研究验证。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f66274dfbe30a093574d104e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"微生物群存在时\",\"finding\":\"肠道微生物通过BSH、bai操纵子等酶系将初级胆汁酸转化为次级/三级胆汁酸（如DCA, LCA, UDCA等），显著增加胆汁酸池的结构多样性和疏水性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d3b5c5db1396b7ca16c20673\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"FXR激活状态下\",\"finding\":\"FXR作为胆汁酸稳态的主调控因子，通过抑制CYP7A1减少胆汁酸合成，并通过FGF19/15介导肠-肝通讯调节代谢。组织特异性（肝vs肠）的FXR激活具有不同的代谢后果。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f89226d0f1ee80575413809b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"特定微生物胆汁酸存在时\",\"finding\":\"某些微生物衍生的胆汁酸（如3-oxo-LCA, isoalloLCA）可直接结合并调节非经典受体（如RORγt, NR4A1），从而调节Th17/Treg平衡和肠道免疫。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::36dab9c7aa4f16a75eb9549c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"高脂饮食或抗生素处理后\",\"finding\":\"饮食和环境因素可破坏胆汁酸-微生物轴，导致次级胆汁酸减少、初级胆汁酸积累，进而促进肥胖、脂肪肝、IBD和艰难梭菌感染等疾病。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::44594a369c08a2ddd1daab93\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6c348e8b52e606d43d9539ef\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"鉴于胆汁酸在宿主-微生物相互作用中的复杂性和重要性，亟需全面梳理胆汁酸-微生物轴的分子机制，特别是其在多种疾病病理生理学中的作用，并探讨基于此轴的治疗策略。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::063e2a1ae882f5afddbb1b65\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"肠道微生物群-胆汁酸-FXR信号轴在代谢性疾病、胃肠道疾病、免疫相关疾病及癌症中的分子机制与临床转化潜力。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::801377f5943780bca1d9dd82\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述，系统阐述了肠道微生物群通过酶促修饰改变胆汁酸（BAs）池组成，进而调节宿主核受体（如FXR、TGR5等）信号通路的机制。文章详细描述了初级胆汁酸的合成与肠肝循环、微生物对胆汁酸的脱共轭、去羟基化等生物转化过程，以及这些微生物衍生的胆汁酸如何作为信号分子影响葡萄糖/脂质代谢、肝脏纤维化、肠道炎症、感染防御和肿瘤发生。最后，文章评估了针对该轴的药物治疗、饮食干预和微生物疗法的治疗潜力与挑战。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a6cd4fb3e1731a47727f1555\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述虽不直接涉及免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs），但其关于肠道微生物群如何通过胆汁酸代谢产物调节宿主免疫系统（特别是T细胞分化、巨噬细胞极化和肠道屏障功能）的机制描述，为理解微生物群对实体瘤免疫治疗反应的潜在间接影响提供了重要的背景知识和机制类比。它揭示了微生物-代谢物-免疫细胞互作的一般性原则，可作为解释微生物群状态如何塑造抗肿瘤免疫微环境的理论支撑。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1a17e70d8a5c433f1597aa0d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"该综述聚焦于代谢和胃肠道炎症疾病中的免疫调节，未直接研究实体瘤中的ICI疗效。其描述的免疫调节主要发生在肠道局部或全身代谢背景下，不一定直接等同于肿瘤微环境中的ICI响应机制。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物群通过胆汁酸代谢产物调节宿主适应性免疫（Th17/Treg平衡）和固有免疫（巨噬细胞、ILC3s）的详细分子机制。例如，3-oxo-LCA抑制RORγt从而抑制Th17，isoalloLCA促进Treg分化。这些机制展示了微生物代谢物如何直接塑造免疫细胞表型。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::98f3fde1ee73d431facabc06\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"未直接关联ICI疗效。其关于微生物群影响宿主表型的论述主要集中在代谢和炎症领域，不能直接外推到ICI疗效上。\",\"contribution\":\"阐述了肠道微生物群组成变化（如BSH阳性菌丰度、bai操纵子携带菌）如何改变胆汁酸池，进而影响宿主生理状态（如肥胖、胰岛素抵抗、肠道炎症）。这表明微生物群的功能状态（而不仅仅是物种组成）是决定宿主表型的关键。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6ff39038a2035f6bf2b4dbc7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述中关于微生物胆汁酸（如3-oxo-LCA, isoalloLCA）调节RORγt和NR4A1从而影响Th17/Treg平衡的描述，以及FXR/TGR5在巨噬细胞和ILC3s中的作用。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::78c9f7c656d35c021b6882ad\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"胆汁酸被描述为关键的内分泌信号分子，通过FXR、TGR5等受体调节代谢和免疫。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::52bb2de93cb41287f72b5bf4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述强调肠道屏障完整性受胆汁酸和微生物群调节，屏障受损会导致炎症和免疫异常。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4ee02360080b6f3bf58a8f15\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述是2026年的前瞻性/综合性文章，其内容代表当前领域的最新共识和观点，但需注意其预测性和建议部分可能尚未完全得到独立验证。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9f0fe3779e2eb2b71ea6022b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的许多机制基于动物模型（如小鼠），在人类中的适用性需谨慎评估，特别是不同物种间胆汁酸谱和受体功能的差异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ec1a8ef58dd4a3380990ae49\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述未直接研究免疫检查点抑制剂，因此其关于微生物群对ICI疗效影响的任何推论都是间接的、推测性的，不能作为直接证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1f2873b6526c39e558200c56\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的某些微生物胆汁酸的作用可能存在情境依赖性（如剂量、受体表达水平、其他共存代谢物），不能一概而论。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::07c3f62291bdfb019fabf875\",\"source_handle\":\"P0180\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s077\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::65d56d6b9b71c6b373afdf05\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"abstract\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0601691302a47dec3e01d95c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6f25342d3bad59d009d18374\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用观察性队列设计。首先，对38名HCC患者进行基线或治疗期间的血清采样，使用液相色谱-高分辨质谱（LC-HRMS）定量10种特定的血清吲哚代谢物。其次，根据临床结局（TTP>8个月，RFS>2年）对患者进行分层，使用Kaplan-Meier曲线和Mann-Whitney U检验比较高低代谢物水平组的生存差异。第三，针对其中8名不可切除患者进行粪便样本采集，进行16S v4 rDNA测序以鉴定细菌群落结构。最后，结合实验数据与计算预测（TrpNet工具，基于贝叶斯逻辑回归），将检测到的代谢物与其潜在的微生物来源（细菌科属）进行关联分析。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e5ca089d04dca02121c44868\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了初步证据，表明血清吲哚丙酸（IPA）水平与不可切除HCC患者对ICI治疗的持久反应（TTP）正相关。\",\"limits\":\"样本量极小（总N=38，微生物组N=8），结果可能缺乏统计效力；仅针对不可切除患者有显著发现，可切除患者无关联；微生物组与代谢物的因果联系依赖于计算预测（TrpNet）和小样本测序，尚未在大队列中验证。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8273ce1dd66befbb9da6a702\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"识别了与ICI初始响应相关的特定细菌科（Pasteurellaceae, Lachnospiraceae）及其代谢产物前体。\",\"limits\":\"细菌丰度变化与临床响应的因果关系未确立；TrpNet工具的预测准确性依赖于已知数据库，可能存在偏差；摘要未提供具体的P值或置信区间，难以评估效应大小。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6692abd574e774a546b124b4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"不可切除HCC患者，接受ICI治疗\",\"finding\":\"血清中吲哚丙酸（IPA）水平较高的患者比水平较低的患者更有可能达到TTP>8个月（50% vs 10%）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8a2b32891cdf12db9a305d2c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"初始响应ICI的不可切除HCC患者\",\"finding\":\"产生IPA前体（吲哚丙酮酸）的细菌科——Pasteurellaceae和Lachnospiraceae的相对丰度显著升高。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::45f3c38c38478f985f509a86\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"可切除HCC患者子集\",\"finding\":\"未观察到明显的代谢物与微生物组关联。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0007362e116150e68c571f49\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c758f86153459a5d38b36c65\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管免疫检查点抑制剂是HCC最有前景的治疗手段，但患者反应异质性大，急需延长生存的策略。具体问题是：能否找到微生物来源的代谢物作为ICI持久反应的生物标志物？这些代谢物的微生物来源是什么？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::12e13cb458d5910465edb27d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"不可切除、新辅助及辅助治疗阶段的肝细胞癌（HCC）患者，接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI，包括anti-PD1/PL1方案如nivo+/-ipi, atezo+bev）治疗。研究涉及血清代谢物分析与粪便微生物组测序，样本量较小（38名患者测代谢物，8名患者测微生物组）。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cfd8dd39d204ce91cf712e92\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本研究旨在识别与HCC患者ICI持久反应相关的微生物来源代谢物生物标志物，并探索其微生物来源。研究团队在38名接受ICI治疗的HCC患者中通过LC-HRMS测量了10种血清吲哚代谢物，并通过Kaplan-Me分析和Mann-Whitney U检验评估了时间至进展（TTP）和无复发生存期（RFS）。同时，在8名不可切除患者的重叠队列中进行16S v4 rDNA测序以表征肠道微生物组，并使用TrpNet工具预测代谢物的潜在微生物来源。研究发现，在不可切除患者中，升高水平的吲哚丙酸（IPA）与改善的预后相关，且初步关联了特定细菌家族与IPA及其前体的产生。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::870b5f35d127537f370968e0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文为综述提供了关于肠道微生物代谢物（特别是吲哚类）调节实体瘤（HCC）免疫治疗反应的具体实证素材。它直接连接了“微生物-代谢物-宿主免疫”轴与ICI疗效，指出了特定代谢物（IPA）和细菌科（Pasteurellaceae, Lachnospiraceae）作为潜在生物标志物的价值，同时也揭示了当前研究的局限性（小样本、特定亚组有效），适合用于讨论机制的复杂性和生物标志物转化的挑战。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::61a6c6feff3f391baf725303\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅限不可切除HCC患者；样本量小；未涵盖所有类型的实体瘤；相关性不等于因果性。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了HCC患者中血清IPA水平与ICI治疗持久反应（TTP）正相关的临床观察数据。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ecd58694847575793224fe55\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"微生物来源主要基于计算预测（TrpNet）和小样本测序验证，需注明其推测性质；未直接展示CD8+ T细胞激活等下游机制的实验细节。\",\"contribution\":\"提出了IPA及其前体（indole pyruvate）的微生物来源假设，并关联了Pasteurellaceae和Lachnospiraceae与初始ICI响应的关系。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c716f233da1565b22b481db3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"介绍了色氨酸代谢的三条路径（犬尿氨酸、血清素、吲哚），并强调吲哚通路主要由肠道微生物介导，具有抗癌特性（抑制增殖、激活CD8+ T细胞）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::442263aa2ce95228340f5b22\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"描述了使用LC-HRMS测量血清代谢物和16S测序分析微生物组的方法，以及结合TrpNet工具进行多组学整合分析的思路。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::08acf77fb02a098f1c740306\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该研究仅在不可切除HCC亚组中观察到显著关联，可切除患者中未发现，因此在推广结论时需严格限定人群。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9713d79110f9458c94ae66c0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"微生物组与代谢物的关联部分依赖于TrpNet的计算预测，而非全面的宏基因组功能验证，需谨慎解读因果链条。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f7d6ed626fff3c999e5b9404\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"样本量非常有限（N=38总体，N=8微生物组），统计效力低，结果应视为探索性发现，而非确证性证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ae366677c559e033e3b97358\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"作者声称IPA具有抗癌特性（激活CD8+ T细胞等），但本摘要主要报告的是临床相关性（TTP/RFS），未在本研究中直接验证其免疫机制。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e7214fda191b40431a8fd6d4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0209\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"no complete research body was indexed\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\"status\":\"partial\"}],\"material_scope\":\"abstract_only\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s057\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::020e47b4a6107b83e3368e3b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7981205e813fc34e82ebdf2c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8d63cceec4e933723074cf7e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"研究设计分为三个主要部分：1. 生物信息学整合分析：收集5个公开ICB治疗研究的宏基因组数据，使用MMUPHin进行批次校正和功能通路定量，比较物种水平与通路水平的变异性，并计算基于健康参考群体的“功能性菌群失调”评分以评估其与临床响应的相关性。2. 纵向队列验证与关联分析：在独立的MMR-d/MSI-H前瞻性队列中，采集基线、治疗中和进展期的粪便样本进行宏基因组和代谢组测序，结合肿瘤转录组数据，分析特定代谢通路（MEP、核黄素合成）的动态变化及其与肿瘤浸润免疫细胞（Vδ2 T细胞、MAIT细胞）丰度的关联。3. 体外机制验证：收集能产生或不能产生HMBPP/5-OP-RU的细菌上清液，与PBMC及患者来源肿瘤类器官（PDTO）共培养，通过流式细胞术检测T细胞活化标志物（CD25, CD137）、细胞因子分泌（IFNγ, TNFα）及杀伤活性，并使用阻断抗体验证受体依赖性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d8452cd5677d3a95c634274f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提出了以代谢通路而非物种为核心的微生物组分析框架，证明了功能谱的稳定性优于物种组成，为解决跨研究不一致性问题提供了新视角。\",\"limits\":\"宏基因组数据仅反映功能潜力（基因存在与否），未直接测量基因表达或实际代谢物浓度（尽管结合了代谢组数据，但HMBPP因稳定性低难以直接检测，主要依赖间接证据）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::af8a28b5add7a55c9ec1c731\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"揭示了MEP通路-Vδ2 T细胞轴和核黄素合成通路-MAIT细胞轴作为微生物组调节ICB疗效的具体免疫机制，特别是强调了人类特有T细胞亚群的作用。\",\"limits\":\"体外类器官实验虽使用了患者来源组织，但仍属于简化模型，未能完全模拟体内复杂的微环境及全身系统性免疫网络；不同肿瘤类型（如结直肠癌与非胃肠道肿瘤）的微生物背景差异可能影响通路的普遍适用性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8192f3205093c480c99dd82a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"建立了功能性菌群失调评分作为预测ICB疗效的生物标志物，并验证了其在纵向监测中的动态变化价值。\",\"limits\":\"功能性菌群失调评分的计算依赖于健康参考群体，对于非健康或非典型状态的解读可能存在偏差；因果关系的最终确立仍需临床试验干预验证。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::da46d716c70c6bd2a11c3e81\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"跨癌种ICB治疗患者队列（Microbe-ICB）\",\"finding\":\"微生物代谢通路的功能谱比物种组成在个体间更保守；高程度的功能性菌群失调与非响应显著相关，且在非响应者治疗期间失调程度加剧。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::56b7494e3ac63fd5336cede7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"MMR-d/MSI-H前瞻性纵向队列\",\"finding\":\"MEP通路丰度在响应者中更高，并与较低的功能性菌群失调相关；核黄素合成通路在非响应者中随时间上调。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9edc6a56f4559f6669964526\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"PDTO与PBMC共培养体系\",\"finding\":\"产HMBPP细菌的上清液通过BTN3A1/2/3受体特异性激活Vδ2 T细胞，增强其对肿瘤类器官的杀伤作用；核黄素前体5-OP-RU诱导MAIT细胞增殖并抑制CD4+ T细胞的增殖与活化。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f605c5022d6c7fd992a64555\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"MMR-d/MSI-H队列生存分析\",\"finding\":\"在高肿瘤内MAIT细胞丰度的患者中，高肠道核黄素水平与较差的无进展生存期（PFS）和总生存期（OS）显著相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8331764f7987194d4c701584\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::53ffe05b16b243d809bd1e7a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"既往针对特定细菌物种与ICB疗效关联的研究结果缺乏一致性，且微生物组调节免疫的具体分子机制尚不清楚。本研究试图回答：是否可以通过更稳定的微生物代谢功能通路来预测ICB疗效？具体的代谢通路如何通过特定的免疫细胞亚群（如Vδ2 T细胞和MAIT细胞）影响抗肿瘤免疫反应？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c7739e35c44d1fdc5775445a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"研究对象为接受免疫检查点阻断（ICB）治疗的实体瘤患者，涵盖黑色素瘤、肾细胞癌、非小细胞肺癌以及错配修复缺陷/微卫星高度不稳定（MMR-d/MSI-H）的晚期癌症。情境包括多中心公共队列整合分析与前瞻性独立验证队列（DRUP），重点考察肠道微生物组功能与抗肿瘤免疫反应及临床疗效之间的关联。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0998f4d3e9d8319917d7810f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"该研究旨在解决既往微生物组研究中物种组成不一致且机制不明的局限，转而关注微生物组的代谢功能输出对ICB疗效的指导作用。作者首先构建并整合了包含781个样本的多癌种ICB治疗患者宏基因组数据集（Microbe-ICB），证实相较于物种水平，代谢通路水平的功能谱在个体间更为保守和稳定。随后，通过计算“功能性菌群失调”评分，发现非响应者表现出更高的菌群功能失调，且这种失调在治疗期间进一步加剧。利用基因集富集分析（GSEA）和纵向队列验证，研究识别出两条关键代谢通路：促进ICB响应的甲基赤藓糖醇4-磷酸（MEP）通路，其产物HMBPP可激活Vδ2 T细胞介导的抗肿瘤活性；以及与耐药相关的核黄素合成通路，其产物5-OP-RU诱导MAIT细胞介导的免疫抑制。这些发现通过患者来源肿瘤类器官（PDTO）与免疫细胞的共培养实验得到了机制层面的验证。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cb639fa62f35997738dca3da\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Microbe-ICB数据集构建流程、MMUPHin批次校正方法、DRUP队列的纵向采样设计。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::40ce62c2d6facb92a508b0b9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"高核黄素+高MAIT细胞患者的较差生存结局（HR=0.103 for OS）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::64d3412604bbb378fa4ee2c5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"讨论部分关于MEP通路激活剂（如双膦酸盐）的比较，以及对人源化模型必要性的论述。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::eff2c324f099469aba355172\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"该结论基于宏基因组推断的功能潜力，需结合代谢组数据佐证；不同肿瘤类型的基线失调程度存在差异（如结直肠癌较高）。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了微生物组功能谱（代谢通路）比物种组成更稳定且更能预测ICB疗效的证据。指出功能性菌群失调程度与非响应正相关，且在治疗过程中恶化。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0e92dfc24b958435823b4b8a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制验证主要在体外PDTO模型中进行，体内因果关系需结合临床队列中的相关性数据（如MAIT细胞丰度与核黄素水平的生存分析）谨慎外推。\",\"contribution\":\"详细阐述了MEP通路产生HMBPP，通过BTN3A1/2/3受体激活Vδ2 T细胞，进而增强其对肿瘤细胞的杀伤作用这一促炎/抗肿瘤机制。同时阐述了核黄素合成产生5-OP-RU，激活MAIT细胞并抑制CD4+ T细胞增殖这一抗炎/抑制机制。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ac8bde68e0604c7c72fcd13a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文为综述提供了关于微生物组影响免疫检查点抑制剂（ICB）疗效的机制性素材，核心贡献在于从“物种组成”转向“代谢功能”，并具体阐明了两条相反的免疫调节路径：MEP通路通过HMBPP激活Vδ2 T细胞促进抗肿瘤免疫，而核黄素合成通路通过5-OP-RU激活MAIT细胞导致免疫抑制。此外，论文提出的“功能性菌群失调”概念可作为评估微生物组整体状态与ICB疗效关联的重要维度。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9acff39a4b1c1a9f04af1ee5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"MEP通路和核黄素合成通路的发现主要基于MMR-d/MSI-H队列的验证，虽然Microbe-ICB包含多种癌种，但在推广至所有实体瘤时需考虑肿瘤特异性的免疫微环境差异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::334d1ac0a37066e3f64b8cc6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"HMBPP的直接检测受限于其化学不稳定性，因此Vδ2 T细胞的激活机制主要基于细菌上清液实验和受体阻断实验，属于间接证据链。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1c3b4a69891ab96af2e858b2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"MAIT细胞的抑制作用是在体外共培养中观察到的，临床队列中仅观察到其与核黄素水平及不良预后的相关性，直接的因果抑制效应在体内尚未完全排除其他混杂因素。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::76b7187225f0ef809966b3b7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0444\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"pdf\",\"reason\":\"full-page text extracted; page positions retained\",\"status\":\"fitz\"},{\"kind\":\"fitz\",\"reason\":\"layout, table relations, formulas, figure pixels, and scanned text may be lost\",\"status\":\"known_gap\"},{\"kind\":\"xml_text_cleanup\",\"reason\":\"removed 85 XML 1.0 forbidden characters from derived PDF text; original PDF and page positions retained\",\"status\":\"normalized\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s095\",\"s186\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2197b24db15e09730e6ef22f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b291d239db17425f7c7959bb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d0fdfae02db57b040a70827b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"作为一篇综述，本文采用系统性回顾和综合的方法：1. 梳理实体瘤微环境的代谢特征，重点阐述腺苷的产生机制及其对T细胞功能的抑制通路；2. 总结基于ADA1的代谢工程策略，包括其生化机制、细胞表面锚定技术（如CD26结合）、以及对T细胞表型和功能的改善效果；3. 汇总临床前研究数据，评估该策略的有效性和安全性；4. 讨论当前技术瓶颈、生物学争议（如次黄嘌呤对肿瘤细胞的潜在影响）及未来临床试验的设计方向。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::527fc8d3a78c58311f7c03a5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"系统阐述了腺苷在实体瘤微环境中的免疫抑制机制及其作为代谢屏障的作用；总结了ADA1介导的代谢重编程在CAR T细胞工程中的最新进展和机制基础。\",\"limits\":\"这是一篇综述文章，主要汇总和评述现有文献及作者团队的观点，未提供新的原始实验数据；所引用的临床前结果主要来自小鼠模型，尚未涉及人体临床试验数据；对于ADA1策略在人类患者中的长期安全性和有效性尚不明确。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4e667d3b6945c7c0550ec065\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"体外及小鼠实体瘤模型（如肝细胞癌、非小细胞肺癌）\",\"finding\":\"工程化表达ADA1的CAR T细胞能够将免疫抑制性的腺苷转化为次黄嘌呤，减少细胞耗竭，增强代谢灵活性，提高增殖能力和肿瘤浸润能力，从而显著提升抗肿瘤疗效。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f2b78e53e56c4c766b079e78\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"ADA1在CAR T细胞上的不同定位策略\",\"finding\":\"膜结合型ADA1（特别是通过肿瘤激活的scFv锚定）比胞质或分泌型ADA1具有更高的肿瘤特异性和局部清除效率，且能招募内源性T细胞产生旁观者效应。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a85cc757fb60640bf0895e79\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"ADA1与CD26共表达\",\"finding\":\"CD26作为ADA1的主要膜锚定受体，确保ADA1在免疫突触或肿瘤-免疫界面局部富集，最大化局部腺苷解毒和代谢支持效果。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c0cf18522f86d4dfa85ad3e7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ae5d6f8ef96bc3926dfb3e73\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"实体瘤微环境中存在严重的营养剥夺和免疫抑制代谢物（如腺苷），导致CAR T细胞功能受损、耗竭和持久性差。如何设计有效的代谢重编程策略以增强CAR T细胞在实体瘤中的疗效？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::59d9b319d3ab8b62dd0b8957\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"CAR T细胞疗法在实体瘤中的应用，重点聚焦于肿瘤微环境中的代谢障碍（特别是腺苷积累）以及ADA1介导的代谢重编程策略。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c7ef47e96a724197bbaa8c9a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述，旨在探讨如何通过代谢重编程克服CAR T细胞在实体瘤治疗中的局限性。文章首先分析了实体瘤微环境的免疫抑制特性，特别是由CD39/CD73轴产生的高浓度腺苷对T细胞的抑制作用及代谢竞争机制。随后，重点介绍了腺苷脱氨酶1（ADA1）的工程化应用，即通过表达ADA1将免疫抑制性的腺苷转化为具有代谢价值的次黄嘌呤，从而改善CAR T细胞的存活、迁移和抗肿瘤活性。文中还讨论了ADA1与CD26的协同作用、不同定位策略的影响、临床前模型的结果，并展望了该策略面临的挑战、争议及未来转化方向。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a841dcee462b478b9bf68ca6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述提供了关于CAR T细胞在实体瘤中面临代谢挑战的详细背景，特别是腺苷介导的免疫抑制机制。虽然其主要关注点是代谢工程而非微生物组，但它为理解实体瘤微环境的复杂性、免疫抑制机制以及除检查点抑制剂外的其他增强策略（如代谢调节）提供了重要背景。对于综述主题“肠道微生物组如何调节实体瘤中免疫检查点抑制剂的疗效”，本文可作为对比或补充材料，说明除了免疫检查点阻断外，代谢微环境也是限制疗效的关键因素，且可能存在联合干预的空间。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::85c00a54a8339aa2c6c0c73a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"本文不直接涉及肠道微生物组，也不直接研究免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）与微生物组的相互作用。其关于代谢的内容是独立于微生物组的背景信息。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了实体瘤微环境中除免疫检查点信号外，代谢抑制（特别是腺苷积累）如何限制免疫治疗（包括CAR T和潜在的ICI疗效）的背景知识。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::45a2d2d150848ea97ad3c766\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"同样不涉及微生物组介导的机制。不能用于直接回答微生物组如何调节ICI疗效的问题，仅能提供微环境代谢层面的机制参考。\",\"contribution\":\"详细描述了腺苷通过A2A受体抑制T细胞功能的具体分子机制（cAMP升高、TCR信号抑制、耗竭相关受体上调）。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8eada48af5e965fa22388d80\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述中关于TME代谢特征、腺苷积累及其对T细胞功能影响的详细描述。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1eb394e283b6e6c4c632e383\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"关于ADA1-CAR T与ICI联合应用的讨论及前景。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::dbd2caa866bdfd956421dbe0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"本文是综述性质，其结论基于对已有研究的综合，而非新的实证研究。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0badce835488d86bf463dff5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的ADA1策略主要针对CAR T细胞，虽然机制上可能与ICI有交集（如都受TME代谢影响），但不能直接推断其对ICI疗效的影响。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::391cc08ec0f0e91c6f687697\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"不要将文中关于CAR T细胞的发现直接外推为对ICI疗效的解释，除非有明确的联合研究证据支持。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d5fcd282d4316ec261a103bd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"本文未涉及肠道微生物组，因此在回答关于微生物组的问题时，只能提供间接的背景或对比视角。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::991ed6ab74d7da974894a51f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"supplement_material\"],\"value\":{\"auxiliary_material\":[\"Description of the CD39/CD73 axis responsible for adenosine generation in the tumor microenvironment.\",\"Details on T cell metabolic states (naïve, effector, memory, exhausted) and their vulnerability to adenosine.\",\"Engineering strategies for localizing ADA1 on T cell surfaces (e.g., via CD26 or scFv).\",\"Safety considerations regarding metabolic engineering, including risks of fueling tumor cells with inosine.\",\"Statement that no clinical trials of ADA1/CAR T cells in humans have been conducted to date.\"],\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level1\\\\external\\\\N76e5cbf6bca57e729afb-df9b777a93e759ce\\\\round_3\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-qeheq06s\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_77e152397a\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"['Search for clinical metabolomics studies that profile purine metabolites (including inosine) in baseline tumor biopsies or blood from ICI-treated patients.', 'Look for microdialysis or mass spectrometry imaging studies quantifying inosine specifically in human tumor microenvironments.', 'Investigate literature linking gut microbiome-derived inosine to ICI efficacy, as the topic context involves microbiome-ICI interactions.', 'Prioritize studies that explicitly report statistical associations (e.g., hazard ratios, p-values) between metabolite levels and clinical endpoints.']\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"['No absolute concentration data for inosine (μM or ng/mL) in human tumor tissue or microdialysis fluid is provided.', 'No statistical correlation between endogenous inosine levels and ICI response (ORR/PFS/OS) in human patients is reported.', 'The efficacy data presented is primarily from preclinical CAR T cell models, not ICI monotherapy or combination trials in humans.', 'The review explicitly states that clinical validation for ADA1-based strategies is pending, implying a lack of human inosine-ICI outcome data in this source.']\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"unmet\",\"useful_material\":[\"Mechanism description: ADA1 enzyme converts immunosuppressive adenosine to inosine, which can serve as an alternative carbon source for T cells.\",\"General TME metabolite context: Extracellular adenosine concentrations in tumors can reach 100–200 μM, significantly higher than in healthy tissue.\",\"Metabolic rationale: Inosine supplementation or generation supports T cell metabolism (glycolytic and pentose phosphate pathways) under glucose restriction.\",\"Preclinical evidence: ADA1-expressing CAR T cells show reduced exhaustion and improved persistence in mouse models, linked to inosine availability.\",\"Combination concept: The authors discuss potential integration of metabolic reprogramming (like ADA1) with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) as a future strategy.\"]},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8d683ee79fb0b745479b7aed\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"supplement_materials\"],\"value\":[{\"auxiliary_material\":[\"Description of the CD39/CD73 axis responsible for adenosine generation in the tumor microenvironment.\",\"Details on T cell metabolic states (naïve, effector, memory, exhausted) and their vulnerability to adenosine.\",\"Engineering strategies for localizing ADA1 on T cell surfaces (e.g., via CD26 or scFv).\",\"Safety considerations regarding metabolic engineering, including risks of fueling tumor cells with inosine.\",\"Statement that no clinical trials of ADA1/CAR T cells in humans have been conducted to date.\"],\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level1\\\\external\\\\N76e5cbf6bca57e729afb-df9b777a93e759ce\\\\round_3\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-qeheq06s\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_77e152397a\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"['Search for clinical metabolomics studies that profile purine metabolites (including inosine) in baseline tumor biopsies or blood from ICI-treated patients.', 'Look for microdialysis or mass spectrometry imaging studies quantifying inosine specifically in human tumor microenvironments.', 'Investigate literature linking gut microbiome-derived inosine to ICI efficacy, as the topic context involves microbiome-ICI interactions.', 'Prioritize studies that explicitly report statistical associations (e.g., hazard ratios, p-values) between metabolite levels and clinical endpoints.']\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"['No absolute concentration data for inosine (μM or ng/mL) in human tumor tissue or microdialysis fluid is provided.', 'No statistical correlation between endogenous inosine levels and ICI response (ORR/PFS/OS) in human patients is reported.', 'The efficacy data presented is primarily from preclinical CAR T cell models, not ICI monotherapy or combination trials in humans.', 'The review explicitly states that clinical validation for ADA1-based strategies is pending, implying a lack of human inosine-ICI outcome data in this source.']\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"unmet\",\"useful_material\":[\"Mechanism description: ADA1 enzyme converts immunosuppressive adenosine to inosine, which can serve as an alternative carbon source for T cells.\",\"General TME metabolite context: Extracellular adenosine concentrations in tumors can reach 100–200 μM, significantly higher than in healthy tissue.\",\"Metabolic rationale: Inosine supplementation or generation supports T cell metabolism (glycolytic and pentose phosphate pathways) under glucose restriction.\",\"Preclinical evidence: ADA1-expressing CAR T cells show reduced exhaustion and improved persistence in mouse models, linked to inosine availability.\",\"Combination concept: The authors discuss potential integration of metabolic reprogramming (like ADA1) with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) as a future strategy.\"]}],\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1e48c2992c7cee19feac4ede\",\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s282\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d6eee809d3a5fb9398bc336e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2bf4fe63f420d8b697f638a7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::195234883ee2c22f9c7f65b8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用统一的操作框架（Microbiome → Metabolites → Immune Modulation → TME State → ICI Response）进行综合。首先从机制层面分析微生物代谢物（SCFAs、胆汁酸、色氨酸衍生物、多胺）对适应性免疫细胞（CD8+ T细胞、Treg、Th1/Th17）和固有免疫效应细胞（巨噬细胞、DC、NK细胞）的重编程作用。其次，回顾2015-2018年 landmark 临床研究及后续FMT概念验证试验，评估微生物组成与ICI预后的关联。最后，基于证据等级（观察性数据 vs. 随机对照试验缺失、样本量限制、技术异质性）对FMT、益生菌、饮食干预及下一代微生物制剂进行转化潜力和临床就绪度评估。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2185cc3f8d466cf3b2e9e28c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提出了一个统一的机制-临床整合框架，明确了肠道微生物组通过代谢物介导的TME重编程路径。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代具体的文献检索策略、纳入排除标准及偏倚风险评估方法。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e3b16c024dc89bf6c3b836ae\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"澄清了SCFAs作用的上下文依赖性（Context-dependent），解释了其在不同微环境中的双重角色，纠正了盲目补充的误区。\",\"limits\":\"关于SCFAs在人体肿瘤中的确切浓度-反应关系尚不明确，所给材料未提供具体的人体肿瘤内SCFA浓度数据。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::dce060fe112e7c5c200443c9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"批判性地评估了微生物组生物标志物的临床就绪度，指出了技术异质性、缺乏前瞻性验证和地理差异等关键局限。\",\"limits\":\"结论基于已发表的观察性和小规模干预研究，尚未包含大规模多中心前瞻性验证结果。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e0b9df36406c4784f1e045e1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"为临床实践提供了分层建议：立即实施抗生素管理，谨慎对待饮食/益生菌，严格限制FMT于临床试验。\",\"limits\":\"这些建议主要基于观察性关联和小规模概念验证研究，缺乏大型随机对照试验的直接证据支持所有干预措施。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::97fe898ec59111e2c6a2b1fb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"在健康黏膜稳态下\",\"finding\":\"SCFAs促进Foxp3+ Treg分化，维持黏膜免疫稳态。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::99a1b5aa57e1a934b35e704d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"在肿瘤免疫微环境中（IFN-γ高表达），且浓度适宜时\",\"finding\":\"SCFAs增强CD8+ T细胞功能（降低PD-1/TIM-3/LAG-3表达）并促进M1型巨噬细胞极化，具有抗肿瘤免疫促进作用。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cef29ad0d40807f5c4be0301\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"盲法补充SCFA或高剂量纤维，未考虑肿瘤免疫表型和基线微生物组状态\",\"finding\":\"缺乏临床支持，可能无效或产生矛盾效果。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7b46ba1efa0ccf7ee2e70db2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"黑色素瘤和NSCLC患者中\",\"finding\":\"较高的肠道微生物多样性及特定菌属（如Faecalibacterium prausnitzii, Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium longum）富集与更好的ICI预后相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d6b776dc4db8bded3cc7ef35\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"接受ICI治疗的晚期黑色素瘤耐药患者\",\"finding\":\"来自ICI响应者的FMT可部分逆转ICI耐药（概念验证阶段），伴随肿瘤内CD8+ T细胞浸润增加。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e451d2eb6eaaa774d9144e9f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"ICI治疗前后30-60天内使用广谱抗生素\",\"finding\":\"与较短的无进展生存期（PFS）和总生存期（OS）一致相关，支持抗生素管理，但存在混杂因素（疾病严重程度）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0d6057781943de584e9cf1f2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"商业益生菌使用\",\"finding\":\"观察性数据显示可能与较差的PFS趋势相关，不支持常规推荐。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5338ed7691dfb4a70f43c749\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::400987067f9112654469f325\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管ICI改变了多种恶性肿瘤的治疗格局，但持久响应率仍然有限。需要厘清肠道微生物组作为系统性免疫调节因子，如何通过代谢产物重塑肿瘤微环境（TME）从而影响ICI疗效；同时需要评估将微生物组特征转化为临床预测生物标志物或治疗策略的可行性与局限性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::89c40541a350639004f2a39b\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"聚焦肠道微生物组（gut microbiome）对实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs，如抗PD-1/PD-L1、抗CTLA-4）疗效的系统性调节作用。明确排除肿瘤内微生物组（intratumoral microbiome），主要涵盖黑色素瘤和非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）等实体瘤的临床与机制证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4eb0ae361131e5d9242f99aa\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述，旨在整合肠道微生物组影响ICI疗效的机制证据与临床发现。文章提出并应用“微生物组→代谢物→免疫调节→TME状态→ICI反应”的统一操作框架，系统梳理了短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）、次级胆汁酸、色氨酸代谢物和多胺等关键代谢轴的作用机制。同时，文章批判性地评估了现有临床关联研究、粪菌移植（FMT）概念验证试验及饮食/益生菌干预的证据等级，指出目前尚无经临床验证的生物标志物，并基于当前证据为临床医生提供了抗生素管理、饮食建议及实验性疗法使用的具体指导原则。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::68caaada83db2b18ac5c6e97\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物组如何调节实体瘤ICI疗效提供了全面的机制背景和临床现状评估。其核心价值在于提供了一个整合性的分析框架（代谢物-免疫-TME），并详细区分了已确立的关联（如抗生素负面影响、特定菌群富集）与尚未验证的临床应用（如FMT、益生菌、生物标志物）。对于综述而言，它不仅是机制解释的来源，更是界定当前领域边界、识别研究空白（如缺乏前瞻性验证、技术标准化不足）以及制定临床实践指南的重要依据。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7922c614bdcb79bda3feb1d5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制描述主要基于前临床模型（小鼠）和部分人类体外/体内观察，部分人体内的确切浓度-效应关系未知。\",\"contribution\":\"详细阐述了四种主要代谢轴（SCFAs、胆汁酸、色氨酸、多胺）的具体分子机制。包括SCFAs通过HDAC抑制和GPCR信号通路调节T细胞耗竭和巨噬细胞极化；色氨酸代谢中宿主IDO酶与细菌吲哚途径的竞争；胆汁酸受体信号对T细胞的抑制；以及多胺对髓系细胞的免疫抑制作用。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::eb76630b77251fb97c0e9d0a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"证据主要来自黑色素瘤和NSCLC，其他实体瘤数据较少；相关性不等于因果性；生物标志物尚未 validated。\",\"contribution\":\"总结了关键临床观察：特定菌群（F. prausnitzii, A. muciniphila, B. longum）与ICI响应正相关；抗生素使用与预后不良相关；FMT在概念验证研究中显示部分逆转耐药的潜力。同时指出了这些发现的局限性（回顾性设计、小样本、技术异质性）。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4f161335a98ee48efcf29983\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"基于现有小规模研究和专家共识，缺乏大型RCT证据支持所有干预措施的长期安全性和有效性。\",\"contribution\":\"评估了转化策略的临床就绪度：FMT处于早期试验阶段，需标准化供体和监管批准；商业益生菌可能有害，不建议常规使用；高纤维饮食可作为健康优化建议，但非特异性抗癌治疗。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::399ef5b58554b3c04c7d8c9d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文章明确指出当前领域缺乏前瞻性验证、技术标准化不足、地理多样性缺乏，并呼吁开展大型多中心队列研究和随机干预试验。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7b406131f04b8af6ade460d3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文章给出了具体的临床行动建议：避免不必要的广谱抗生素、推荐地中海式高纤维饮食、不推荐商业益生菌和SCFA补充剂、FMT仅限临床试验。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7dca157fb29354115581be76\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文章强调了SCFAs作用的上下文依赖性（Context-dependent），即同一代谢物在不同微环境下可能产生相反效果。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::35253ee716d91b56449feb1f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述明确排除了肿瘤内微生物组（intratumoral microbiome），仅关注肠道微生物组的系统性影响。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::18e093e9c0650c0adb6a76bd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的临床关联多为观察性研究，不能直接推断因果关系；FMT等证据来自小规模概念验证试验，效力有限。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ea8815a44607a8b77c2201dc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"所提机制多基于前临床模型，人体内的确切生理浓度和效应阈值尚不明确。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1be3f40b9e3ba9019333cb48\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"不同研究间的技术异质性和地理差异可能导致菌群-疗效关联的不一致性，需谨慎外推。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d4894969daf36d135d810ad5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::349f23b247bb74e7f21b4e09\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"local_passages\"],\"value\":{\"external_calls\":0,\"passages\":[{\"best_sentence\":\"Landmark clinical and preclinical studies linking the gut microbiome to immune checkpoint inhibitor response and tumor microenvironment modulationImmune checkpoint inhibitor, NSCLC: Non-small cell lung cancer, RCC: Renal cell carcinoma, PFS/OS: Progression-free survival/overall survival, CTLA-4: cytotoxic T-lymphocyte-associated protein 4, FMT: Fecal microbiota transplantation, IFN: Interferon FMT from defined donors, and precision microbial consortia with ICI efficacy as primary endpoints, stratified by tumor immune phenotype.(3) Geographic diversity in study populations to establish generalizability across non-Western cohorts.(4) Longitudinal rather than single-baseline microbiome profiling to capture dynamic changes during ICI treatment.(5) Multivariate predictive modeling integrating microbiome functional data with tumor genomics, host immune profiling, and germline genetics.\",\"card_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\9db1c1ced73dca207c6289b20b4a2914a09ca2b1\\\\0e352726189f698ed7200afeb2df9e1f\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\"doi\":\"10.25259/ijmio_8_2026\",\"limits\":[],\"match_terms\":[\"粪菌移植\",\"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\",\"ici\",\"nsclc\",\"rcc\"],\"material_depth\":\"fulltext\",\"paper_id\":\"9db1c1ced73dca207c6289b20b4a2914a09ca2b1\",\"pool_action\":\"already_in_pool\",\"reading_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\materials\\\\9db1c1ced73dca207c6289b20b4a2914a09ca2b1\\\\snapshot-a22ccfd4fa2ec07e546e769c\",\"score\":45.119645,\"section_path\":[],\"segment_kind\":\"document_block\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"text\":\"Practical clinical considerations for microbiome-related interventions in patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors Landmark clinical and preclinical studies linking the gut microbiome to immune checkpoint inhibitor response and tumor microenvironment modulationImmune checkpoint inhibitor, NSCLC: Non-small cell lung cancer, RCC: Renal cell carcinoma, PFS/OS: Progression-free survival/overall survival, CTLA-4: cytotoxic T-lymphocyte-associated protein 4, FMT: Fecal microbiota transplantation, IFN: Interferon FMT from defined donors, and precision microbial consortia with ICI efficacy as primary endpoints, stratified by tumor immune phenotype.(3) Geographic diversity in study populations to establish generalizability across non-Western cohorts.(4) Longitudinal rather than single-baseline microbiome profiling to capture dynamic changes during ICI treatment.(5) Multivariate predictive modeling integrating microbiome functional data with tumor genomics, host immune profiling, and germline genetics. Artificial intelligence (AI)-assisted language tools were used during manuscript drafting and language refinement.All scientific content, interpretation, refere\",\"title\":\"The gut microbiome–tumor microenvironment axis in immunotherapy response: Mechanistic insights and clinical implications\",\"usable_fields\":[],\"year\":\"2026\"}],\"question\":\"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect? 微生物干预策略的临床转化现状 系统评估粪菌移植（FMT）、活体生物药（LBPs）、益生菌及饮食干预在实体瘤 ICI 治疗中的临床试验数据，区分初治与难治人群的疗效差异，明确证据等级（I/II 期 vs III 期），并分析供体选择、安全性及标准化挑战。 涵盖人体临床试验（I-III 期），聚焦实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、CRC 等）。包括 FMT（供体来源、给药途径）、定义菌群（如 CBM588、MRx0518）、益生菌及饮食干预。明确排除纯临床前研究（除非用于解释机制背景）及非 ICI 背景的微生物干预。严格区分观察性关联与干预性因果证据，标注试验设计类型（单臂 vs RCT）及人群特征（初治 vs 经治）。\",\"reading_mode\":\"focused_local_search\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0b6134a90e57fc9c6e1be952\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d08eb04ea89d1be1e33a047e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f5b4029a4db9047fd36c2c50\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用系统性文献回顾与综合的方法。作者检索并整理了从临床前研究到临床研究的相关证据，按照代谢物的化学类别（SCFAs、肌苷、TMAO、色氨酸衍生物、胆汁酸及其他分子）进行分类叙述。对于每一类代谢物，综述了其在动物模型和临床试验中的观察结果，归纳了其作用的免疫细胞类型（如CD8+ T细胞、Treg、巨噬细胞等）及关键信号通路（如HDAC、mTOR、GPRs、AhR、NOD2等）。同时，对比分析了同一代谢物在不同治疗背景下的矛盾发现，以评估其复杂性和情境依赖性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::596759d47ba6a21459261d96\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"系统性地汇总了肠道微生物代谢物调节ICIs疗效的多维证据，特别是揭示了同一代谢物（如SCFAs）在不同ICIs靶点（PD-1 vs CTLA-4）下可能具有截然相反的免疫调节作用，强调了治疗策略的情境依赖性。\",\"limits\":\"作为综述，依赖于已发表研究的总结，未提供新的原始实验数据；部分机制（如肌苷的双重作用、特定代谢物的精确剂量效应）仍需更多临床验证；未能涵盖所有可能的微生物代谢物种类。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e6a84e8e4a4530184c544641\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"接受PD-1/PD-L1阻断治疗的实体瘤患者及小鼠模型\",\"finding\":\"粪便中高浓度的短链脂肪酸（SCFAs，如丙酸、丁酸、戊酸）与较长的无进展生存期（PFS）及更好的治疗反应相关；SCFAs通过抑制HDAC、激活GPRs和调节mTOR通路增强CD8+ T细胞的细胞毒性和分化。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4ccaa4344a587186290f3b5e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"接受CTLA-4阻断治疗的转移性黑色素瘤患者及小鼠模型\",\"finding\":\"血清中高浓度的丁酸和丙酸与较差的ICIs疗效负相关；丁酸抑制记忆T细胞的积累和树突状细胞上CD80/CD86的上调，增加Treg比例，从而削弱抗CTLA-4疗效。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::36d5718059c065b3b3c074a7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"膀胱癌和小肠癌小鼠模型\",\"finding\":\"肠道菌群产生的肌苷（Inosine）可通过A2aR-cAMP-PKA通路促进Th1分化，增加IFN-γ+ CD4+和CD8+ T细胞浸润，增强抗CTLA-4和抗PD-L1疗效；但在缺乏外源IFN-γ时可能抑制Th1分化，且需CpG共刺激。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1e1bdc01a956b0ad950e688c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"小鼠肿瘤模型及部分临床数据\",\"finding\":\"氧化三甲胺（TMAO）通过激活PERK介导的内质网应激和Gasdermin-E介导的细胞焦亡，增强CD8+ T细胞介导的抗肿瘤免疫，提高抗PD-1疗效；高血浆TMAO水平与较长PFS相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::93ea60f675ed97e4c3550dac\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"胰腺导管腺癌小鼠模型 vs. 结肠癌/乳腺癌模型\",\"finding\":\"乳酸杆菌来源的吲哚类色氨酸代谢物（如Indoles）在胰腺癌中通过激活TAMs上的A2aR抑制CD8+ T细胞释放IFN-γ，抑制免疫；而双歧杆菌产生的ILA可诱导结肠癌细胞凋亡，IPA可抑制乳腺癌生长，显示出色氨酸代谢物效应的异质性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d07bb8210ca700dedb9a661a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"多种癌症模型\",\"finding\":\"次级胆汁酸代谢物3-oxoLCA和isoLCA通过抑制ROR-γt抑制Th17细胞分化；去氧胆酸（DCA）在某些情况下促进血管生成模拟。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::377cc3be601df49761f64750\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a7dc402b2fc8a26ccd9ea6a0\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管ICIs显著改善了癌症患者生存率，但客观缓解率仍低于30%。肠道微生物群已知能调节ICIs疗效，但其具体作用模式尚不明确。本研究旨在解决：肠道微生物代谢物如何具体调节抗肿瘤免疫？它们作为ICIs疗效增强剂或生物标志物的潜力如何？其背后的分子机制是什么？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9820954a67cf06885ec681f4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"肠道微生物群及其衍生的代谢物（如短链脂肪酸、肌苷、TMAO、色氨酸代谢物、次级胆汁酸等）对实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs，包括PD-1/PD-L1和CTLA-4抗体）疗效的调节作用及潜在机制。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::45f928c5f233046daedb50ad\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述，旨在梳理肠道微生物群通过其代谢产物调节抗肿瘤免疫并影响ICIs疗效的证据与机制。文章首先介绍了肿瘤微环境与免疫细胞的关系，随后分类详细讨论了短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）、肌苷、氧化三甲胺（TMAO）、色氨酸代谢物和次级胆汁酸等主要代谢物的功能、产生菌及分子机制（如HDAC抑制、GPR受体激活、AhR通路等）。文中特别指出了不同代谢物在不同癌症模型或ICIs类型中可能存在的相反效果（如丁酸盐在抗PD-1治疗中的促进作用与在抗CTLA-4治疗中的抑制作用），并探讨了基于代谢物的生物标志物预测、免疫佐剂开发及饮食干预等未来策略。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f38cbed5b61790a8d5171261\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物代谢物如何作为‘敌人或朋友’调节ICIs疗效提供了详细的机制图谱和临床关联证据。其核心价值在于揭示了代谢物效应的异质性和双向性（如SCFAs的双刃剑效应），以及具体的分子通路（HDAC, GPR, AhR等）。这有助于在综述中解释为何某些微生物特征在不同研究中表现出不一致的预后价值，并为基于代谢物的联合治疗策略提供理论依据。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5f8472029adf0f3c82178aab\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这些关联多为观察性或相关性，因果链条需结合机制部分理解；不同研究间的样本量和检测方法差异可能导致结果不可直接比较。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了肠道微生物代谢物与ICIs疗效关联的临床队列数据和动物模型结果。例如，指出粪便SCFAs浓度与PD-1治疗PFS正相关，但血清丁酸与CTLA-4治疗疗效负相关；TMAO高水平与较好响应相关。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6a458b7805c18e2d16c9bfdb\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"机制多在体外或小鼠模型中验证，人体内的确切效力和剂量依赖关系尚不完全清楚；部分机制存在争议或复杂性（如肌苷在有无IFN-γ时的不同作用）。\",\"contribution\":\"详细阐述了多种代谢物的分子机制。包括：SCFAs通过抑制HDAC、激活GPR41/43和调节mTOR通路影响T细胞分化和细胞因子产生；肌苷通过A2aR-cAMP-PKA通路促进Th1分化；TMAO通过PERK/Gasdermin-E途径诱导细胞焦亡；色氨酸代谢物通过AhR通路调节巨噬细胞和T细胞功能；次级胆汁酸通过抑制ROR-γt抑制Th17。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::692ff74a4b546e35a604cdb7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这些矛盾结果提示了复杂的调控网络，不能简单地将某一代谢物归类为‘好’或‘坏’。\",\"contribution\":\"指出了代谢物效应的矛盾性和情境依赖性。例如，SCFAs在抗PD-1中有益，在抗CTLA-4中可能有害；色氨酸代谢物在胰腺癌中抑制免疫，在结肠癌中可能抑制肿瘤发生。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3227041e5510f7fefbcc15e1\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文章引言部分概述了ICIs面临的挑战（ORR<30%）以及肠道微生物群通过代谢物调节宿主免疫的整体概念。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1da8ee278ec36b4bcb262a40\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"文章第三部分讨论了基于代谢物的免疫佐剂、生物标志物、粪菌移植（FMT）、合成工程微生物和饮食干预等策略。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2b584d6203efddc1cb5bbb65\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提到了非代谢物类的微生物成分，如Enterococci产生的muropeptides（通过NOD2）、Lactobacillus产生的EPS-R1（通过CCR6）、E. coli的FimH（通过TLR4）以及多酚Castalagin。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2b636c18bea65c211e130ee5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述涵盖了多种代谢物，但重点在于其与ICIs（主要是PD-1/PD-L1和CTLA-4）的相互作用。对于其他免疫疗法（如CAR-T）的提及较少，需注意适用范围。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cbc4edad599286a29e2b282d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中引用的临床数据多来自小样本队列或回顾性分析，需谨慎推断其普遍性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::15b3947a221324e9c92b50fc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"同一代谢物在不同癌症类型和不同ICIs靶点下可能具有相反的作用，解读时必须严格区分具体情境，避免过度泛化。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::132652ec51f2cc7c95b9f7e4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"机制描述主要基于动物模型和体外实验，人体内的实际生理病理过程可能存在差异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bf0925e52c7b5299e2f07666\",\"source_handle\":\"P0413\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s270\"]}],\"snapshot_index\":{\"s016\":\"snapshot::145e68ca2e945fe75d99a541\",\"s003\":\"snapshot::01759670cec0ae86b898b9ca\",\"s139\":\"snapshot::80ee6d0031e9d81e9747aece\",\"s155\":\"snapshot::8966721c01adb52dbb888ee6\",\"s116\":\"snapshot::729cb791ca6edfe6c11639b5\",\"s014\":\"snapshot::10f6f83feb179745fdb9234e\",\"s175\":\"snapshot::9c38714850a8edbe294a4d75\",\"s137\":\"snapshot::806dfb73f7648b306867b1fd\",\"s226\":\"snapshot::c74ceafaf0f44d4428d1f44c\",\"s043\":\"snapshot::307f071228c50505d3184f8a\",\"s031\":\"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\"s160\":\"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\"s074\":\"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\",\"s166\":\"snapshot::93c6a2bc5ca1c43be2fd189f\",\"s152\":\"snapshot::880a4cdb0c38e0b0bd47c6f0\",\"s187\":\"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\"s107\":\"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\",\"s056\":\"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\"s061\":\"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\"s286\":\"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\"s214\":\"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\"s208\":\"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\",\"s060\":\"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\"s048\":\"snapshot::3655ccef0398dfb4668a6047\",\"s182\":\"snapshot::a43af420403a250e3f63baf0\",\"s176\":\"snapshot::9cc12751d782ca6db2e16bcd\",\"s077\":\"snapshot::517e4ff3db173ff08232081b\",\"s057\":\"snapshot::3e241ae4a3e5d38d53cd830c\",\"s095\":\"snapshot::623b881452a1bbc406a2e4b5\",\"s186\":\"snapshot::a6fc0ba0bd562126f2100785\",\"s282\":\"snapshot::f91812ead0c570146868b193\",\"s071\":\"snapshot::4c223c48c000f6845789e3b9\",\"s047\":\"snapshot::34a888801e8e6d821b264263\",\"s270\":\"snapshot::ec2a02729d6c1d88e1ca4fe5\"},\"tool_materials\":[{\"tool_id\":\"tool::259afce0b6a9a5349ecdd23d9d631668cd45c48e3ca878154e765edccbb485ae\",\"value\":{\"need_id\":\"N76e5cbf6bca57e729afb-df9b777a93e759ce\",\"question\":\"人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷（inosine）的生理浓度及其与 ICI 疗效的具体相关性数据是什么？\",\"intended_use\":\"mechanism\",\"decision\":\"external_research\",\"usable_content\":\"现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告其与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效的具体统计关联。P0582 研究在人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列中仅检测了血浆中的肌苷水平，发现高基线血浆肌苷与尼莫鲁单抗治疗后的较长总生存期相关（中位 OS 33个月 vs. 22个月），但明确说明由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性的代理指标；该研究还指出肌苷在血浆中半衰期较长（约15小时），但未提供具体的血浆或组织浓度数值。P0588 研究主要关注体外 T 细胞代谢及小鼠模型，虽提及血液血浆中肌苷浓度为低微摩尔范围、坏死/缺氧微环境中可积累至数百微摩尔，但这些是引用外部文献的一般性陈述，并非本研究中对人类患者的实测数据，且明确指出缺乏人类临床相关性数据。P0587 综述同样未提取具体浓度值，仅引用其他研究关于粪便短链脂肪酸或精氨酸的数据示例。因此，当前材料无法回答人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷的具体浓度及其与 ICI 疗效的相关性问题。\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷（inosine）的绝对生理浓度数据，也未见其与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效（如ORR、PFS或OS）的具体统计关联结果。多项研究指出这是当前文献中的关键缺失环节：尽管有临床观察显示接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的肾细胞癌患者血浆中肌苷水平较高与总生存期延长相关（中位OS 33个月 vs 22个月），但研究者承认由于样本完整性问题，未能在其22人的临床队列中直接测量肌苷，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的替代指标；另有综述和机制研究引用外部文献提及坏死或缺氧微环境中肌苷可能积累至数百微摩尔（hundreds of micromolar），但这并非针对接受ICI治疗的人类患者的实测数据。此外，虽然有小鼠模型证实口服肌苷可增强ICB疗效，且体外实验显示T细胞可利用肌苷作为碳源，但这些前临床数据无法直接外推为人体内的具体浓度阈值或疗效相关性。目前缺乏将人源肿瘤组织或间质液中的肌苷定量值与ICI响应直接挂钩的证据。\\n\\n[\\\"这项研究在人体数据方面提供了两方面的关键证据：首先，通过分析 CheckMate 025 临床试验中肾细胞癌（RCC）患者的血浆代谢组数据（n=394 接受 nivolumab 治疗），发现血浆肌苷水平高低与总生存期（OS）显著相关（高肌苷组中位 OS 33 个月 vs 低肌苷组 22 个月），证实了循环肌苷水平与 ICI 疗效的临床关联。其次，在一个包含 22 名接受抗 PD-1 治疗的多癌种患者的小型队列中，作者检测了肿瘤组织内的 UBA6 蛋白表达（作为肌苷作用的下游靶点），发现低 UBA6 表达与更高的客观缓解率（ORR 50% vs 17%）及 CD8+ T 细胞浸润相关。然而，作者明确指出由于样本缺失，未能在该人体肿瘤队列中直接检测肌苷浓度。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"研究在小鼠模型（B16-F0, 4T1 等）中证实了外源性肌苷补充可增强 ICI 疗效，并揭示了分子机制：肌苷直接进入肿瘤细胞，抑制泛素激活酶 UBA6，从而解除 UBA6 对炎症信号和抗原呈递通路的抑制，提高肿瘤免疫原性。研究还指出肌苷在血浆中的半衰期较长（约 15 小时），而腺苷极短，这影响了体内测量的稳定性。此外，研究提到肌苷来源具有多源性（肠道微生物、饮食、癌细胞分泌），且在不同肿瘤类型中效果可能依赖基础 UBA6 表达水平（如在低 UBA6 的 MC38 模型中无效）。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告其与ICI疗效在组织层面的直接定量关联。P0582研究仅提供了人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者血浆中的肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）的相关性：在高肌苷组中，接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的患者中位OS为33个月，而低肌苷组为22个月。该研究明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的代理指标。P0588研究虽然指出文献报道肌苷在血浆中为低微摩尔范围，而在坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔，但这属于引用外部文献的理论背景，并非本研究对ICI响应患者的实测数据，且该研究主要关注T细胞代谢机制而非临床浓度-疗效关联。P0587综述同样未提取具体的肌苷浓度数值。因此，关于“人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷的生理浓度及其与ICI疗效的具体相关性数据”这一具体问题，当前材料缺失核心的绝对浓度测量值及对应的组织层面统计关联。\\nHuman RCC patients (CheckMate 025 trial, nivolumab-treated cohort) / Median Overall Survival: High inosine group 33 months vs. Low inosine group 22 months / Baseline plasma levels measured prior to or at start of treatment; survival follow-up：High plasma inosine: 33 months；Low plasma inosine: 22 months\\nMouse models (B16-F0, 4T1, etc.) and Human T cells (in vitro) / General concentration ranges cited from external literature (not measured in this study's human samples): Plasma low micromolar range; TME hundreds of micromolar range / Theoretical/External citation context for physiological relevance：Plasma (cited): low micromolar；TME (cited): hundreds of micromolar\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度及其与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效的具体相关性数据。多项研究明确指出，目前文献中缺乏将肌苷等代谢物在粪便、血液、肿瘤组织及间质液中的配对定量测量与临床结局关联的证据。具体而言：P0582 报告了肾细胞癌患者血浆中肌苷水平与生存期的关联（高肌苷组中位总生存期33个月 vs 低肌苷组22个月），但明确说明未在人肿瘤样本中验证或测量肌苷浓度，仅以UBA6表达作为通路活性代理指标；P0588 指出虽然理论推测坏死/缺氧微环境中肌苷可达数百微摩尔，但该研究本身未在人类患者中测量TME内的肌苷浓度，且其引用的数值为外部文献的一般性陈述而非本研究数据；P0587 和 P0589 均强调，尽管有微生物产生肌苷增强小鼠ICI疗效的机制证据，但缺乏人体肿瘤组织或间质液中肌苷浓度的直接定量数据，且现有的SCFA数据多局限于粪便样本，未链接至TME浓度或ICI结果。因此，关于人体TME内肌苷的具体浓度阈值及其对ORR/PFS/OS的统计关联，当前材料显示为未满足的研究空白。\\n\\n[\\\"该研究确认了腺苷脱氨酶（ADA）将腺苷（Ado）转化为肌苷（Ino）的酶动力学参数（Km=0.05, Vmax=53µmol/min），并在体外实验中证实了腺苷暴露会抑制免疫细胞杀伤力，而转化为肌苷可恢复免疫功能。研究提及使用 LC-MS 评估 ADA 动力学和活性，表明肌苷及相关代谢物在实验体系中是可测量的。这为肌苷在肿瘤微环境中具有免疫刺激作用而非抑制作用提供了机制性证据，支持了微环境代谢重编程可能影响免疫治疗效果的假设。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"研究对象为工程化非致病性大肠杆菌（E. coli K12 DH5α），通过表面展示 IL-12 和 ADA 融合蛋白发挥作用。体内实验主要在免疫 competent 的 B16-F10 黑色素瘤小鼠模型和 WEHI-3 AML 小鼠模型中进行，观察到细菌在骨髓和肿瘤部位的聚集。免疫效应主要评估了 NK 细胞的活化标志物（CD25, NKp30）及细胞因子（IFNγ, TNFα），未直接报告 T 细胞检查点抑制剂（ICI）的使用或响应数据。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告其与ICI疗效在组织层面的直接定量关联。P0582研究仅提供了人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者血浆中的肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）的相关性：在高肌苷组中，接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的患者中位OS为33个月，而低肌苷组为22个月。该研究明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的代理指标。P0588研究虽然指出文献报道肌苷在血浆中为低微摩尔范围，而在坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔，但这属于引用外部文献的理论背景，并非本研究对ICI响应患者的实测数据，且该研究主要关注T细胞代谢机制而非临床浓度-疗效关联。P0587综述同样未提取具体的肌苷浓度数值。因此，关于“人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷的生理浓度及其与ICI疗效的具体相关性数据”这一具体问题，当前材料缺失核心的绝对浓度测量值及对应的组织层面统计关联。\\nHuman RCC patients (CheckMate 025 trial, nivolumab-treated cohort) / Median Overall Survival: High inosine group 33 months vs. Low inosine group 22 months / Baseline plasma levels measured prior to or at start of treatment; survival follow-up：High plasma inosine: 33 months；Low plasma inosine: 22 months\\nMouse models (B16-F0, 4T1, etc.) and Human T cells (in vitro) / General concentration ranges cited from external literature (not measured in this study's human samples): Plasma low micromolar range; TME hundreds of micromolar range / Theoretical/External citation context for physiological relevance：Plasma (cited): low micromolar；TME (cited): hundreds of micromolar\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据。研究P0582仅报告了人体血浆（血清）中肌苷水平与免疫检查点阻断（ICB）疗效的关联：在肾细胞癌（RCC）患者中，基线血浆肌苷水平较高者接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的中位总生存期为33个月，显著高于低水平组的22个月。该研究明确指出，由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中直接验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的替代指标。此外，P0582提到腺苷降解为肌苷的半衰期差异（约15小时），暗示了检测策略的挑战，但未给出具体的人体组织浓度数值。其他材料如P0588和P0596主要基于小鼠模型或体外实验，其中P0588引用文献指出肌苷在坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔，但这并非本研究在人体中的实测数据；P0596提供了体外培养中使用的短链脂肪酸浓度，而非人体内源性肌苷浓度。P0639虽然建立了尿液中肌苷的定量方法并报告了膀胱癌患者术前术后尿液浓度的变化（术后24小时升高约1.7倍），但尿液浓度不能直接等同于肿瘤微环境或血清中的浓度。因此，目前缺乏将人体肿瘤组织或间质液中肌苷的具体绝对浓度（μM或ng/mL）与ICI响应（ORR/PFS/OS）直接挂钩的实证数据。\\n人体血浆中的肌苷浓度与ICB疗效的相关性 / 接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的RCC患者的总生存期（OS） / CheckMate 025临床试验队列，基线血浆测量值：P0582_High_Inosine: 33 months (median OS)；P0582_Low_Inosine: 22 months (median OS)\\n\\n[[\\\"Mechanism description: ADA1 enzyme converts immunosuppressive adenosine to inosine, which can serve as an alternative carbon source for T cells.\\\", \\\"General TME metabolite context: Extracellular adenosine concentrations in tumors can reach 100–200 μM, significantly higher than in healthy tissue.\\\", \\\"Metabolic rationale: Inosine supplementation or generation supports T cell metabolism (glycolytic and pentose phosphate pathways) under glucose restriction.\\\", \\\"Preclinical evidence: ADA1-expressing CAR T cells show reduced exhaustion and improved persistence in mouse models, linked to inosine availability.\\\", \\\"Combination concept: The authors discuss potential integration of metabolic reprogramming (like ADA1) with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) as a future strategy.\\\"]]\\n\\n[[\\\"Description of the CD39/CD73 axis responsible for adenosine generation in the tumor microenvironment.\\\", \\\"Details on T cell metabolic states (naïve, effector, memory, exhausted) and their vulnerability to adenosine.\\\", \\\"Engineering strategies for localizing ADA1 on T cell surfaces (e.g., via CD26 or scFv).\\\", \\\"Safety considerations regarding metabolic engineering, including risks of fueling tumor cells with inosine.\\\", \\\"Statement that no clinical trials of ADA1/CAR T cells in humans have been conducted to date.\\\"]]\",\"conditions\":[\"人体血浆中的肌苷浓度与ICB疗效的相关性\",\"CheckMate 025临床试验队列，基线血浆测量值\"],\"limits\":[\"需要找到直接在人体肿瘤组织活检、间质液或微透析液中测量肌苷绝对浓度，并将其与ICI治疗响应（如ORR、PFS、OS）进行统计关联的研究。目前的证据仅限于血浆水平的间接关联或动物模型/体外实验。\"],\"still_missing\":\"人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷（inosine）的生理浓度及其与 ICI 疗效的具体相关性数据是什么？\",\"allowed_use\":[\"background_context\",\"explicit_objectives\",\"explicit_method_summaries\",\"explicit_reported_findings\",\"explicit_leads\"],\"sources\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"title\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"title\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:220699268\",\"title\":\"Inosine is an alternative carbon source for CD8+ T cell function under glucose restriction\",\"year\":\"2020\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s42255-020-0219-4\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:220699268\",\"title\":\"Inosine is an alternative carbon source for CD8+ T cell function under glucose restriction\",\"year\":\"2020\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s42255-020-0219-4\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:280543786\",\"title\":\"The gut microbiota in cancer immunity and immunotherapy\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41423-025-01326-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"title\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:291235137\",\"title\":\"Non-nutritive sweeteners, the gut microbiome, and tumor immunity: evidence hierarchy and a sucralose-centered translational model\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fnut.2026.1868431\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0589\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286562058\",\"title\":\"Immunomodulatory effects of short-chain fatty acids and immune-supporting nutrients on slice cultures of head and neck tumors\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fnut.2026.1731077\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0596\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"7f1c43ec9ba638ccffb6291e9f21c1e1b48f6fc6\",\"title\":\"Multifaceted role of inosine in complex diseases and human health.\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1093/nutrit/nuae029\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0599\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0580\",\"paper_id\":\"c5e74d5eebf19335caebc97bdb8300261fcb0ee5\",\"title\":\"Targeting ribosomes reprograms the tumour microenvironment and augments cancer immunotherapy\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41416-025-03109-y\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0579\",\"paper_id\":\"1e76d13192f1c1a75fec92c6e6a2de5934fc6a1f\",\"title\":\"Characterisation of an autochthonous mouse ccRCC model of immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy resistance\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41598-025-04917-1\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0581\",\"paper_id\":\"5e59b9ca9a72cc8a626d875743ecc0ce1315af76\",\"title\":\"Artemin and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) efficacy in metastatic colorectal cancer (mCRC): A correlative analysis of the Canadian Cancer Trials Group (CCTG) CO.26 trial.\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1200/jco.2024.42.16_suppl.3587\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0639\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:259947308\",\"title\":\"Targeted quantitative metabolomics with a linear mixed-effect model for analysis of urinary nucleosides and deoxynucleosides from bladder cancer patients before and after tumor resection\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/s00216-023-04826-0\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0634\",\"paper_id\":\"680707c522895f780f927da2a5894def6930a602\",\"title\":\"Abstract 5175: DX-002, a dual EP2 and EP4 antagonist, alters the tumor microenvironment to enhance tumor immunogenicity and responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1538-7445.am2023-5175\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:280543786\",\"title\":\"The gut microbiota in cancer immunity and immunotherapy\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41423-025-01326-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0634\",\"paper_id\":\"680707c522895f780f927da2a5894def6930a602\",\"title\":\"Abstract 5175: DX-002, a dual EP2 and EP4 antagonist, alters the tumor microenvironment to enhance tumor immunogenicity and responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1538-7445.am2023-5175\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0609\",\"paper_id\":\"d69f29862a6e18da7c70e3c9d22cd4b7cabc18a3\",\"title\":\"Abstract B028: Multimodal approach to characterization of metabolism and immune modulation with insights from spatial metabolomics and transcriptomics\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1557-3265.targetedtherap-b028\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286562058\",\"title\":\"Immunomodulatory effects of short-chain fatty acids and immune-supporting nutrients on slice cultures of head and neck tumors\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fnut.2026.1731077\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0596\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0581\",\"paper_id\":\"5e59b9ca9a72cc8a626d875743ecc0ce1315af76\",\"title\":\"Artemin and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) efficacy in metastatic colorectal cancer (mCRC): A correlative analysis of the Canadian Cancer Trials Group (CCTG) CO.26 trial.\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1200/jco.2024.42.16_suppl.3587\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0639\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:259947308\",\"title\":\"Targeted quantitative metabolomics with a linear mixed-effect model for analysis of urinary nucleosides and deoxynucleosides from bladder cancer patients before and after tumor resection\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/s00216-023-04826-0\"},{\"canonical_paper_id\":\"OpenAlex:W4296038319\",\"title\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0586\",\"paper_id\":\"04c11cfcf5a3539fa2c39d0839134cb7fc2116bd\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"04c11cfcf5a3539fa2c39d0839134cb7fc2116bd\",\"title\":\"Dual-function engineered bacteria remodel AML tumor microenvironment via IL-12 delivery and adenosine depletion to sustain NK cell immunity\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1182/blood-2025-5912\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"paper_id\":\"OpenAlex:W7116840248\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"OpenAlex:W7116840248\",\"title\":\"ADA1-Driven Metabolic Refueling Enhances CAR T Cell Therapy for Solid Tumors\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.3390/cancers18010034\"}],\"provenance\":{\"downloads\":0,\"model_calls\":1,\"source\":\"judge+focused_local_read\",\"whole_paper_rereads\":0},\"chapter_ids\":[\"Ch3\"],\"unit_key\":\"\"}},{\"tool_id\":\"tool::9d8059d85014492a70b811c05d67e8513c873c193e432bc07d6d2f094b63eb27\",\"value\":{\"need_id\":\"Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-acf4314fb7d520c6\",\"question\":\"人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷（inosine）的生理浓度及其与 ICI 疗效的具体相关性数据是什么？\",\"intended_use\":\"mechanism\",\"decision\":\"external_research\",\"usable_content\":\"现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告其与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效的具体统计关联。P0582 研究在人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列中仅检测了血浆中的肌苷水平，发现高基线血浆肌苷与尼莫鲁单抗治疗后的较长总生存期相关（中位 OS 33个月 vs. 22个月），但明确说明由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性的代理指标；该研究还指出肌苷在血浆中半衰期较长（约15小时），但未提供具体的血浆或组织浓度数值。P0588 研究主要关注体外 T 细胞代谢及小鼠模型，虽提及血液血浆中肌苷浓度为低微摩尔范围、坏死/缺氧微环境中可积累至数百微摩尔，但这些是引用外部文献的一般性陈述，并非本研究中对人类患者的实测数据，且明确指出缺乏人类临床相关性数据。P0587 综述同样未提取具体浓度值，仅引用其他研究关于粪便短链脂肪酸或精氨酸的数据示例。因此，当前材料无法回答人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷的具体浓度及其与 ICI 疗效的相关性问题。\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷（inosine）的绝对生理浓度数据，也未见其与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效（如ORR、PFS或OS）的具体统计关联结果。多项研究指出这是当前文献中的关键缺失环节：尽管有临床观察显示接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的肾细胞癌患者血浆中肌苷水平较高与总生存期延长相关（中位OS 33个月 vs 22个月），但研究者承认由于样本完整性问题，未能在其22人的临床队列中直接测量肌苷，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的替代指标；另有综述和机制研究引用外部文献提及坏死或缺氧微环境中肌苷可能积累至数百微摩尔（hundreds of micromolar），但这并非针对接受ICI治疗的人类患者的实测数据。此外，虽然有小鼠模型证实口服肌苷可增强ICB疗效，且体外实验显示T细胞可利用肌苷作为碳源，但这些前临床数据无法直接外推为人体内的具体浓度阈值或疗效相关性。目前缺乏将人源肿瘤组织或间质液中的肌苷定量值与ICI响应直接挂钩的证据。\\n\\n[\\\"这项研究在人体数据方面提供了两方面的关键证据：首先，通过分析 CheckMate 025 临床试验中肾细胞癌（RCC）患者的血浆代谢组数据（n=394 接受 nivolumab 治疗），发现血浆肌苷水平高低与总生存期（OS）显著相关（高肌苷组中位 OS 33 个月 vs 低肌苷组 22 个月），证实了循环肌苷水平与 ICI 疗效的临床关联。其次，在一个包含 22 名接受抗 PD-1 治疗的多癌种患者的小型队列中，作者检测了肿瘤组织内的 UBA6 蛋白表达（作为肌苷作用的下游靶点），发现低 UBA6 表达与更高的客观缓解率（ORR 50% vs 17%）及 CD8+ T 细胞浸润相关。然而，作者明确指出由于样本缺失，未能在该人体肿瘤队列中直接检测肌苷浓度。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"研究在小鼠模型（B16-F0, 4T1 等）中证实了外源性肌苷补充可增强 ICI 疗效，并揭示了分子机制：肌苷直接进入肿瘤细胞，抑制泛素激活酶 UBA6，从而解除 UBA6 对炎症信号和抗原呈递通路的抑制，提高肿瘤免疫原性。研究还指出肌苷在血浆中的半衰期较长（约 15 小时），而腺苷极短，这影响了体内测量的稳定性。此外，研究提到肌苷来源具有多源性（肠道微生物、饮食、癌细胞分泌），且在不同肿瘤类型中效果可能依赖基础 UBA6 表达水平（如在低 UBA6 的 MC38 模型中无效）。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告其与ICI疗效在组织层面的直接定量关联。P0582研究仅提供了人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者血浆中的肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）的相关性：在高肌苷组中，接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的患者中位OS为33个月，而低肌苷组为22个月。该研究明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的代理指标。P0588研究虽然指出文献报道肌苷在血浆中为低微摩尔范围，而在坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔，但这属于引用外部文献的理论背景，并非本研究对ICI响应患者的实测数据，且该研究主要关注T细胞代谢机制而非临床浓度-疗效关联。P0587综述同样未提取具体的肌苷浓度数值。因此，关于“人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷的生理浓度及其与ICI疗效的具体相关性数据”这一具体问题，当前材料缺失核心的绝对浓度测量值及对应的组织层面统计关联。\\nHuman RCC patients (CheckMate 025 trial, nivolumab-treated cohort) / Median Overall Survival: High inosine group 33 months vs. Low inosine group 22 months / Baseline plasma levels measured prior to or at start of treatment; survival follow-up：High plasma inosine: 33 months；Low plasma inosine: 22 months\\nMouse models (B16-F0, 4T1, etc.) and Human T cells (in vitro) / General concentration ranges cited from external literature (not measured in this study's human samples): Plasma low micromolar range; TME hundreds of micromolar range / Theoretical/External citation context for physiological relevance：Plasma (cited): low micromolar；TME (cited): hundreds of micromolar\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度及其与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效的具体相关性数据。多项研究明确指出，目前文献中缺乏将肌苷等代谢物在粪便、血液、肿瘤组织及间质液中的配对定量测量与临床结局关联的证据。具体而言：P0582 报告了肾细胞癌患者血浆中肌苷水平与生存期的关联（高肌苷组中位总生存期33个月 vs 低肌苷组22个月），但明确说明未在人肿瘤样本中验证或测量肌苷浓度，仅以UBA6表达作为通路活性代理指标；P0588 指出虽然理论推测坏死/缺氧微环境中肌苷可达数百微摩尔，但该研究本身未在人类患者中测量TME内的肌苷浓度，且其引用的数值为外部文献的一般性陈述而非本研究数据；P0587 和 P0589 均强调，尽管有微生物产生肌苷增强小鼠ICI疗效的机制证据，但缺乏人体肿瘤组织或间质液中肌苷浓度的直接定量数据，且现有的SCFA数据多局限于粪便样本，未链接至TME浓度或ICI结果。因此，关于人体TME内肌苷的具体浓度阈值及其对ORR/PFS/OS的统计关联，当前材料显示为未满足的研究空白。\\n\\n[\\\"该研究确认了腺苷脱氨酶（ADA）将腺苷（Ado）转化为肌苷（Ino）的酶动力学参数（Km=0.05, Vmax=53µmol/min），并在体外实验中证实了腺苷暴露会抑制免疫细胞杀伤力，而转化为肌苷可恢复免疫功能。研究提及使用 LC-MS 评估 ADA 动力学和活性，表明肌苷及相关代谢物在实验体系中是可测量的。这为肌苷在肿瘤微环境中具有免疫刺激作用而非抑制作用提供了机制性证据，支持了微环境代谢重编程可能影响免疫治疗效果的假设。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"研究对象为工程化非致病性大肠杆菌（E. coli K12 DH5α），通过表面展示 IL-12 和 ADA 融合蛋白发挥作用。体内实验主要在免疫 competent 的 B16-F10 黑色素瘤小鼠模型和 WEHI-3 AML 小鼠模型中进行，观察到细菌在骨髓和肿瘤部位的聚集。免疫效应主要评估了 NK 细胞的活化标志物（CD25, NKp30）及细胞因子（IFNγ, TNFα），未直接报告 T 细胞检查点抑制剂（ICI）的使用或响应数据。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告其与ICI疗效在组织层面的直接定量关联。P0582研究仅提供了人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者血浆中的肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）的相关性：在高肌苷组中，接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的患者中位OS为33个月，而低肌苷组为22个月。该研究明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的代理指标。P0588研究虽然指出文献报道肌苷在血浆中为低微摩尔范围，而在坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔，但这属于引用外部文献的理论背景，并非本研究对ICI响应患者的实测数据，且该研究主要关注T细胞代谢机制而非临床浓度-疗效关联。P0587综述同样未提取具体的肌苷浓度数值。因此，关于“人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷的生理浓度及其与ICI疗效的具体相关性数据”这一具体问题，当前材料缺失核心的绝对浓度测量值及对应的组织层面统计关联。\\nHuman RCC patients (CheckMate 025 trial, nivolumab-treated cohort) / Median Overall Survival: High inosine group 33 months vs. Low inosine group 22 months / Baseline plasma levels measured prior to or at start of treatment; survival follow-up：High plasma inosine: 33 months；Low plasma inosine: 22 months\\nMouse models (B16-F0, 4T1, etc.) and Human T cells (in vitro) / General concentration ranges cited from external literature (not measured in this study's human samples): Plasma low micromolar range; TME hundreds of micromolar range / Theoretical/External citation context for physiological relevance：Plasma (cited): low micromolar；TME (cited): hundreds of micromolar\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据。研究P0582仅报告了人体血浆（血清）中肌苷水平与免疫检查点阻断（ICB）疗效的关联：在肾细胞癌（RCC）患者中，基线血浆肌苷水平较高者接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的中位总生存期为33个月，显著高于低水平组的22个月。该研究明确指出，由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中直接验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的替代指标。此外，P0582提到腺苷降解为肌苷的半衰期差异（约15小时），暗示了检测策略的挑战，但未给出具体的人体组织浓度数值。其他材料如P0588和P0596主要基于小鼠模型或体外实验，其中P0588引用文献指出肌苷在坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔，但这并非本研究在人体中的实测数据；P0596提供了体外培养中使用的短链脂肪酸浓度，而非人体内源性肌苷浓度。P0639虽然建立了尿液中肌苷的定量方法并报告了膀胱癌患者术前术后尿液浓度的变化（术后24小时升高约1.7倍），但尿液浓度不能直接等同于肿瘤微环境或血清中的浓度。因此，目前缺乏将人体肿瘤组织或间质液中肌苷的具体绝对浓度（μM或ng/mL）与ICI响应（ORR/PFS/OS）直接挂钩的实证数据。\\n人体血浆中的肌苷浓度与ICB疗效的相关性 / 接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的RCC患者的总生存期（OS） / CheckMate 025临床试验队列，基线血浆测量值：P0582_High_Inosine: 33 months (median OS)；P0582_Low_Inosine: 22 months (median OS)\\n\\n[[\\\"Mechanism description: ADA1 enzyme converts immunosuppressive adenosine to inosine, which can serve as an alternative carbon source for T cells.\\\", \\\"General TME metabolite context: Extracellular adenosine concentrations in tumors can reach 100–200 μM, significantly higher than in healthy tissue.\\\", \\\"Metabolic rationale: Inosine supplementation or generation supports T cell metabolism (glycolytic and pentose phosphate pathways) under glucose restriction.\\\", \\\"Preclinical evidence: ADA1-expressing CAR T cells show reduced exhaustion and improved persistence in mouse models, linked to inosine availability.\\\", \\\"Combination concept: The authors discuss potential integration of metabolic reprogramming (like ADA1) with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) as a future strategy.\\\"]]\\n\\n[[\\\"Description of the CD39/CD73 axis responsible for adenosine generation in the tumor microenvironment.\\\", \\\"Details on T cell metabolic states (naïve, effector, memory, exhausted) and their vulnerability to adenosine.\\\", \\\"Engineering strategies for localizing ADA1 on T cell surfaces (e.g., via CD26 or scFv).\\\", \\\"Safety considerations regarding metabolic engineering, including risks of fueling tumor cells with inosine.\\\", \\\"Statement that no clinical trials of ADA1/CAR T cells in humans have been conducted to date.\\\"]]\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的直接生理浓度测量值，也未提供基于直接TME测量的疗效相关性数据。P0582研究在人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列中仅报告了血浆中的肌苷水平，发现高血浆肌苷水平与免疫检查点阻断（ICB）治疗后的更长总生存期相关（中位OS：高水平组33个月 vs. 低水平组22个月），并指出ICB治疗后血浆肌苷水平下降。该研究未进行人体肿瘤组织内的直接定量，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的替代指标。P0589研究利用患者来源异种移植（PDX）小鼠模型结合微透析技术，证实了在人源肿瘤组织中可检测到肌苷且存在瘤内差异，但未报告具体的绝对浓度数值，也未涉及ICI疗效的相关性分析。P0588综述提及一般文献中血浆肌苷为低微摩尔级，而坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔级，但这属于引用的一般性背景陈述，并非本研究对特定人体TME的实测数据。因此，关于“人体肿瘤微环境内”的具体浓度及其与ICI疗效的直接量化关联，当前材料缺失核心实证数据。\\nHuman RCC patients (CheckMate 025 trial, nivolumab cohort) / Median Overall Survival: High inosine group 33 months vs. Low inosine group 22 months / Baseline plasma levels prior to or during ICB treatment：High plasma inosine: 33 months；Low plasma inosine: 22 months\\nMouse models (B16-F0, 4T1) and human RCC patients / Plasma inosine levels decreased after ICB treatment compared to baseline/pre-treatment states / During/after ICB therapy：Post-ICB (Mice & Humans): Reduced levels (qualitative)\\nGeneral physiological context (cited literature) / Concentration ranges: Blood plasma low micromolar; Necrotic/hypoxic TME hundreds of micromolar / General physiological conditions：Blood plasma: Low micromolar range；Necrotic/Hypoxic TME: Hundreds of micromolar range\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷（inosine）的绝对生理浓度及其与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效的具体相关性数据。多项研究明确指出，目前文献中缺乏针对人类肿瘤组织或间质液中代谢物的配对定量测量，特别是将肌苷等代谢物浓度与ICI临床结局直接关联的数据。具体而言：P0582 在 CheckMate 025 队列中报告了接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的肾细胞癌患者血浆肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）的显著正相关（高肌苷组中位 OS 33个月 vs. 低肌苷组 22个月），但作者明确说明由于样本完整性问题，未在该临床队列中验证或直接测量肌苷浓度，而是以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性的代理指标；P0589 利用患者来源异种移植（PDX）模型结合体内微透析技术证实了人源肿瘤组织中肌苷的可检测性及瘤区与非瘤区的差异，但该数据来源于小鼠模型而非直接的人体患者样本，且未报告与 ICI 疗效的相关性；P0588 指出虽然血液血浆中肌苷浓度通常为低微摩尔范围，而在坏死、缺氧或炎症微环境中可积累至数百微摩尔，但这些数值是引用外部文献的一般性陈述，并非本研究中对人类患者的实测数据；P0596 和 P0634 分别提供了体外培养中使用的短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）实验浓度及前列腺素 E2 (PGE2) 的临床背景，但未涉及人体 TME 内肌苷的内源性浓度测定。此外，P0581 关于血清 Artemin 的研究虽提供了具体的血清蛋白浓度阈值（1.051 ng/ml）与 MSS mCRC 患者预后的关联，但这属于宿主来源因子，非微生物代谢物肌苷。综上，当前证据主要停留在机制假设、动物模型验证或血浆水平的间接关联上，缺乏直接量化人体肿瘤内部肌苷浓度并证实其与 ICI 响应关系的临床数据。\\n\\n[\\\"该研究在人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列（CheckMate 025 试验，n=394 接受 nivolumab 治疗）中检测了基线血浆肌苷水平，发现高肌苷组中位总生存期（OS）为 33 个月，显著高于低肌苷组的 22 个月，确立了循环肌苷水平与 ICI 疗效的临床统计关联。在另一个包含 22 名接受抗 PD-1 治疗的多癌种患者的小型队列中，作者检测了肿瘤组织内的 UBA6 蛋白表达（作为肌苷作用的下游靶点），发现低 UBA6 表达与更高的客观缓解率（ORR 50% vs 17%）及 CD8+ T 细胞浸润相关。研究明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未能在该人体肿瘤队列中直接检测肿瘤微环境（TME）内的肌苷浓度，而是以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性的代理指标。\\\", \\\"该综述在第 6.3 节明确将肌苷（inosine）归类为微生物组衍生的代谢物生物标志物，指出目前仅有临床前研究证明微生物衍生的肌苷可通过促进抗肿瘤 T 细胞活性来增强检查点阻断反应（引用文献 184），但并未建立其作为已验证的人类预测性生物标志物的地位。文章强调循环代谢物浓度受饮食、抗生素暴露、地理因素及宿主代谢等多种混杂因素影响，且目前缺乏标准化的前分析程序和可重复的阈值，因此将其定义为探索性工具而非临床决策依据。此外，文章区分了短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）在人类患者中已有血浆/粪便浓度与生存期关联的报道，但肌苷在本文语境下主要仍停留在临床前证据阶段，未提供人体实测浓度数据。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"研究在小鼠模型（B16-F0, 4T1 等）中证实了外源性肌苷补充（400 mg/kg）可增强 ICI 疗效，并揭示了分子机制：肌苷直接进入肿瘤细胞，抑制泛素激活酶 UBA6，从而解除 UBA6 对炎症信号和抗原呈递通路的抑制。研究引用外部文献指出肌苷在血浆中为低微摩尔范围，而在坏死/缺氧微环境中可积累至数百微摩尔，但强调这些是理论背景而非本研究中对人类患者的实测数据。此外，研究提到肌苷在血浆中的半衰期较长（约 15 小时），而腺苷极短，这影响了体内测量的稳定性。\\\", \\\"文章第 2 节提出的‘预测性与预后性生物标志物’概念框架，可用于评估未来若发现肌苷浓度数据时，需验证其是否为治疗特异性预测指标而非仅反映疾病负荷或全身炎症。第 10 节讨论了外周血与肿瘤微环境（TME）之间的生物学脱节问题，提示外周血肌苷水平可能无法完全代表 TME 内的局部浓度。表 2 总结了微生物衍生代谢物作为新兴生物标志物平台的技术障碍（如低生物量污染、标准化缺乏）。\\\"]\\n\\n[[\\\"该研究在 CheckMate 025 临床试验的肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列（n=394 接受 nivolumab 治疗）中，通过血浆代谢组分析发现基线血浆肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）显著相关：高肌苷组中位 OS 为 33 个月，低肌苷组为 22 个月。\\\", \\\"该研究在一个包含 22 名接受抗 PD-1 治疗的多癌种患者的小型队列中，检测了肿瘤组织内的 UBA6 蛋白表达（作为肌苷作用通路的下游代理指标），发现低 UBA6 表达与更高的客观缓解率（ORR 50% vs 17%）及 CD8+ T 细胞浸润相关。\\\", \\\"该研究明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未能在其人体肿瘤队列中直接验证或测量肿瘤微环境（TME）内的肌苷浓度，而是以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性的替代指标。\\\", \\\"该研究提供了肌苷增强 ICB 疗效的分子机制证据：肌苷直接进入肿瘤细胞，抑制泛素激活酶 UBA6，从而解除 UBA6 对炎症信号和抗原呈递通路的抑制，提高肿瘤免疫原性。\\\", \\\"该研究指出肌苷在血浆中的半衰期较长（约 15 小时），而腺苷极短，这影响了体内测量的稳定性，并提及未来研究需进一步解析两者关系。\\\"], \\\"该研究提供了胰腺导管腺癌（PDAC）肿瘤微环境（TME）中癌症相关成纤维细胞（CAFs）介导免疫抑制的具体机制证据，表明 CAFs 通过产生细胞外基质成分、促进肿瘤生长及下调免疫细胞浸润来阻碍免疫治疗。研究展示了通过 IL-15 联合化疗（吉西他滨）可显著增加效应 T 细胞（CD4+/CD8+）和 NK 细胞浸润及活化（IFNγ, Granzyme B），从而在体外 3D 异型球体模型中实现抗肿瘤效果。这为综述提供了除微生物代谢物（如肌苷）之外，宿主基质成分如何作为物理/生物屏障影响 ICI 疗效的对照案例，支持了‘微环境重塑是增强 ICI 疗效途径’的广泛假设。\\\", \\\"This study investigated the synergistic effect of allopurinol (AP) with anti-PD-1 therapy. In mouse CT26 cell cultures, LC-MS/MS analysis showed AP treatment increased extracellular inosine levels by approximately 500 to 1000-fold in supernatants, while cell lysate levels remained unchanged, indicating active export. Mechanistically, AP inhibits xanthine dehydrogenase (XDH), elevating hypoxanthine which is converted to inosine via the salvage pathway. In vivo, AP combined with anti-PD-1 achieved tumor-free outcomes in 4/6 mice. In a retrospective human cohort of 50 bladder cancer patients receiving anti-PD-1 therapy, the 7 patients concurrently taking gout medications (AP or febuxostat) showed significantly better overall survival compared to the 43 patients who did not. The authors propose that elevated inosine enhances tumor immunogenicity (upregulating MHC class I and PD-L1) and supports T-cell function.\\\"]\\n\\n[[\\\"该研究引用外部文献指出肌苷在坏死/缺氧微环境中可积累至数百微摩尔（hundreds of micromolar），但这属于理论背景陈述，并非本研究对人类患者的实测数据。\\\", \\\"该研究在小鼠模型（B16-F0, 4T1 等）中证实了外源性肌苷补充（400 mg/kg 口服）可增强 ICI 疗效，并揭示了 UBA6 缺失可替代肌苷效果的体内证据。\\\", \\\"该研究提到肌苷来源具有多源性（肠道微生物、饮食、癌细胞分泌），且在不同肿瘤类型中效果可能依赖基础 UBA6 表达水平（如在低 UBA6 的 MC38 模型中无效）。\\\"], \\\"研究构建了包含患者来源肿瘤细胞、CAFs 及健康供体 PBMCs 的 3D 体外异型球体模型，并利用成像质谱流式（IMC）进行空间分析，展示了 CAFs 对免疫细胞分布的影响。研究明确指出下一步计划是在体内同基因 PDAC 原位模型中评估该策略对抗 PD-1 疗法的增敏作用，但目前摘要中尚未报告 ICI 联合使用的实际响应数据。\\\", \\\"The study developed a meta-program (MP) scoring algorithm based on scRNA-seq data from mouse tumors to quantify TME remodeling, identifying myeloid-derived suppressor cell (MDSC) depletion as a hallmark of responsive TMEs. It established a resource (scIMD) and web tool (resTMe) for screening immunomodulatory drugs. The analysis covered eight cancer types for gene identification but performed in vivo validation primarily in the CT26 colon carcinoma model.\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告其与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效的具体统计关联。P0582 研究在人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列中仅检测了血浆中的肌苷水平，发现高基线血浆肌苷与尼莫鲁单抗治疗后的较长总生存期相关（中位 OS 33个月 vs. 22个月），但明确说明由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性的代理指标；该研究还指出肌苷在血浆中半衰期较长（约15小时），但未提供具体的血浆或组织浓度数值。P0588 研究主要关注体外 T 细胞代谢及小鼠模型，虽提及血液血浆中肌苷浓度为低微摩尔范围、坏死/缺氧微环境中可积累至数百微摩尔，但这些是引用外部文献的一般性陈述，并非本研究中对人类患者的实测数据，且明确指出缺乏人类临床相关性数据。P0587 综述同样未提取具体浓度值，仅引用其他研究关于粪便短链脂肪酸或精氨酸的数据示例。因此，当前材料无法回答人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷的具体浓度及其与 ICI 疗效的相关性问题。\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷（inosine）的绝对生理浓度数据，也未见其与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效（如ORR、PFS或OS）的具体统计关联结果。多项研究指出这是当前文献中的关键缺失环节：尽管有临床观察显示接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的肾细胞癌患者血浆中肌苷水平较高与总生存期延长相关（中位OS 33个月 vs 22个月），但研究者承认由于样本完整性问题，未能在其22人的临床队列中直接测量肌苷，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的替代指标；另有综述和机制研究引用外部文献提及坏死或缺氧微环境中肌苷可能积累至数百微摩尔（hundreds of micromolar），但这并非针对接受ICI治疗的人类患者的实测数据。此外，虽然有小鼠模型证实口服肌苷可增强ICB疗效，且体外实验显示T细胞可利用肌苷作为碳源，但这些前临床数据无法直接外推为人体内的具体浓度阈值或疗效相关性。目前缺乏将人源肿瘤组织或间质液中的肌苷定量值与ICI响应直接挂钩的证据。\\n\\n[\\\"这项研究在人体数据方面提供了两方面的关键证据：首先，通过分析 CheckMate 025 临床试验中肾细胞癌（RCC）患者的血浆代谢组数据（n=394 接受 nivolumab 治疗），发现血浆肌苷水平高低与总生存期（OS）显著相关（高肌苷组中位 OS 33 个月 vs 低肌苷组 22 个月），证实了循环肌苷水平与 ICI 疗效的临床关联。其次，在一个包含 22 名接受抗 PD-1 治疗的多癌种患者的小型队列中，作者检测了肿瘤组织内的 UBA6 蛋白表达（作为肌苷作用的下游靶点），发现低 UBA6 表达与更高的客观缓解率（ORR 50% vs 17%）及 CD8+ T 细胞浸润相关。然而，作者明确指出由于样本缺失，未能在该人体肿瘤队列中直接检测肌苷浓度。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"研究在小鼠模型（B16-F0, 4T1 等）中证实了外源性肌苷补充可增强 ICI 疗效，并揭示了分子机制：肌苷直接进入肿瘤细胞，抑制泛素激活酶 UBA6，从而解除 UBA6 对炎症信号和抗原呈递通路的抑制，提高肿瘤免疫原性。研究还指出肌苷在血浆中的半衰期较长（约 15 小时），而腺苷极短，这影响了体内测量的稳定性。此外，研究提到肌苷来源具有多源性（肠道微生物、饮食、癌细胞分泌），且在不同肿瘤类型中效果可能依赖基础 UBA6 表达水平（如在低 UBA6 的 MC38 模型中无效）。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告其与ICI疗效在组织层面的直接定量关联。P0582研究仅提供了人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者血浆中的肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）的相关性：在高肌苷组中，接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的患者中位OS为33个月，而低肌苷组为22个月。该研究明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的代理指标。P0588研究虽然指出文献报道肌苷在血浆中为低微摩尔范围，而在坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔，但这属于引用外部文献的理论背景，并非本研究对ICI响应患者的实测数据，且该研究主要关注T细胞代谢机制而非临床浓度-疗效关联。P0587综述同样未提取具体的肌苷浓度数值。因此，关于“人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷的生理浓度及其与ICI疗效的具体相关性数据”这一具体问题，当前材料缺失核心的绝对浓度测量值及对应的组织层面统计关联。\\nHuman RCC patients (CheckMate 025 trial, nivolumab-treated cohort) / Median Overall Survival: High inosine group 33 months vs. Low inosine group 22 months / Baseline plasma levels measured prior to or at start of treatment; survival follow-up：High plasma inosine: 33 months；Low plasma inosine: 22 months\\nMouse models (B16-F0, 4T1, etc.) and Human T cells (in vitro) / General concentration ranges cited from external literature (not measured in this study's human samples): Plasma low micromolar range; TME hundreds of micromolar range / Theoretical/External citation context for physiological relevance：Plasma (cited): low micromolar；TME (cited): hundreds of micromolar\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度及其与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效的具体相关性数据。多项研究明确指出，目前文献中缺乏将肌苷等代谢物在粪便、血液、肿瘤组织及间质液中的配对定量测量与临床结局关联的证据。具体而言：P0582 报告了肾细胞癌患者血浆中肌苷水平与生存期的关联（高肌苷组中位总生存期33个月 vs 低肌苷组22个月），但明确说明未在人肿瘤样本中验证或测量肌苷浓度，仅以UBA6表达作为通路活性代理指标；P0588 指出虽然理论推测坏死/缺氧微环境中肌苷可达数百微摩尔，但该研究本身未在人类患者中测量TME内的肌苷浓度，且其引用的数值为外部文献的一般性陈述而非本研究数据；P0587 和 P0589 均强调，尽管有微生物产生肌苷增强小鼠ICI疗效的机制证据，但缺乏人体肿瘤组织或间质液中肌苷浓度的直接定量数据，且现有的SCFA数据多局限于粪便样本，未链接至TME浓度或ICI结果。因此，关于人体TME内肌苷的具体浓度阈值及其对ORR/PFS/OS的统计关联，当前材料显示为未满足的研究空白。\\n\\n[\\\"该研究确认了腺苷脱氨酶（ADA）将腺苷（Ado）转化为肌苷（Ino）的酶动力学参数（Km=0.05, Vmax=53µmol/min），并在体外实验中证实了腺苷暴露会抑制免疫细胞杀伤力，而转化为肌苷可恢复免疫功能。研究提及使用 LC-MS 评估 ADA 动力学和活性，表明肌苷及相关代谢物在实验体系中是可测量的。这为肌苷在肿瘤微环境中具有免疫刺激作用而非抑制作用提供了机制性证据，支持了微环境代谢重编程可能影响免疫治疗效果的假设。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"研究对象为工程化非致病性大肠杆菌（E. coli K12 DH5α），通过表面展示 IL-12 和 ADA 融合蛋白发挥作用。体内实验主要在免疫 competent 的 B16-F10 黑色素瘤小鼠模型和 WEHI-3 AML 小鼠模型中进行，观察到细菌在骨髓和肿瘤部位的聚集。免疫效应主要评估了 NK 细胞的活化标志物（CD25, NKp30）及细胞因子（IFNγ, TNFα），未直接报告 T 细胞检查点抑制剂（ICI）的使用或响应数据。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告其与ICI疗效在组织层面的直接定量关联。P0582研究仅提供了人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者血浆中的肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）的相关性：在高肌苷组中，接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的患者中位OS为33个月，而低肌苷组为22个月。该研究明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的代理指标。P0588研究虽然指出文献报道肌苷在血浆中为低微摩尔范围，而在坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔，但这属于引用外部文献的理论背景，并非本研究对ICI响应患者的实测数据，且该研究主要关注T细胞代谢机制而非临床浓度-疗效关联。P0587综述同样未提取具体的肌苷浓度数值。因此，关于“人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷的生理浓度及其与ICI疗效的具体相关性数据”这一具体问题，当前材料缺失核心的绝对浓度测量值及对应的组织层面统计关联。\\nHuman RCC patients (CheckMate 025 trial, nivolumab-treated cohort) / Median Overall Survival: High inosine group 33 months vs. Low inosine group 22 months / Baseline plasma levels measured prior to or at start of treatment; survival follow-up：High plasma inosine: 33 months；Low plasma inosine: 22 months\\nMouse models (B16-F0, 4T1, etc.) and Human T cells (in vitro) / General concentration ranges cited from external literature (not measured in this study's human samples): Plasma low micromolar range; TME hundreds of micromolar range / Theoretical/External citation context for physiological relevance：Plasma (cited): low micromolar；TME (cited): hundreds of micromolar\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据。研究P0582仅报告了人体血浆（血清）中肌苷水平与免疫检查点阻断（ICB）疗效的关联：在肾细胞癌（RCC）患者中，基线血浆肌苷水平较高者接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的中位总生存期为33个月，显著高于低水平组的22个月。该研究明确指出，由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中直接验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的替代指标。此外，P0582提到腺苷降解为肌苷的半衰期差异（约15小时），暗示了检测策略的挑战，但未给出具体的人体组织浓度数值。其他材料如P0588和P0596主要基于小鼠模型或体外实验，其中P0588引用文献指出肌苷在坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔，但这并非本研究在人体中的实测数据；P0596提供了体外培养中使用的短链脂肪酸浓度，而非人体内源性肌苷浓度。P0639虽然建立了尿液中肌苷的定量方法并报告了膀胱癌患者术前术后尿液浓度的变化（术后24小时升高约1.7倍），但尿液浓度不能直接等同于肿瘤微环境或血清中的浓度。因此，目前缺乏将人体肿瘤组织或间质液中肌苷的具体绝对浓度（μM或ng/mL）与ICI响应（ORR/PFS/OS）直接挂钩的实证数据。\\n人体血浆中的肌苷浓度与ICB疗效的相关性 / 接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的RCC患者的总生存期（OS） / CheckMate 025临床试验队列，基线血浆测量值：P0582_High_Inosine: 33 months (median OS)；P0582_Low_Inosine: 22 months (median OS)\\n\\n[[\\\"Mechanism description: ADA1 enzyme converts immunosuppressive adenosine to inosine, which can serve as an alternative carbon source for T cells.\\\", \\\"General TME metabolite context: Extracellular adenosine concentrations in tumors can reach 100–200 μM, significantly higher than in healthy tissue.\\\", \\\"Metabolic rationale: Inosine supplementation or generation supports T cell metabolism (glycolytic and pentose phosphate pathways) under glucose restriction.\\\", \\\"Preclinical evidence: ADA1-expressing CAR T cells show reduced exhaustion and improved persistence in mouse models, linked to inosine availability.\\\", \\\"Combination concept: The authors discuss potential integration of metabolic reprogramming (like ADA1) with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) as a future strategy.\\\"]]\\n\\n[[\\\"Description of the CD39/CD73 axis responsible for adenosine generation in the tumor microenvironment.\\\", \\\"Details on T cell metabolic states (naïve, effector, memory, exhausted) and their vulnerability to adenosine.\\\", \\\"Engineering strategies for localizing ADA1 on T cell surfaces (e.g., via CD26 or scFv).\\\", \\\"Safety considerations regarding metabolic engineering, including risks of fueling tumor cells with inosine.\\\", \\\"Statement that no clinical trials of ADA1/CAR T cells in humans have been conducted to date.\\\"]]\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的直接生理浓度测量值，也未提供基于直接TME测量的疗效相关性数据。P0582研究在人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列中仅报告了血浆中的肌苷水平，发现高血浆肌苷水平与免疫检查点阻断（ICB）治疗后的更长总生存期相关（中位OS：高水平组33个月 vs. 低水平组22个月），并指出ICB治疗后血浆肌苷水平下降。该研究未进行人体肿瘤组织内的直接定量，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的替代指标。P0589研究利用患者来源异种移植（PDX）小鼠模型结合微透析技术，证实了在人源肿瘤组织中可检测到肌苷且存在瘤内差异，但未报告具体的绝对浓度数值，也未涉及ICI疗效的相关性分析。P0588综述提及一般文献中血浆肌苷为低微摩尔级，而坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔级，但这属于引用的一般性背景陈述，并非本研究对特定人体TME的实测数据。因此，关于“人体肿瘤微环境内”的具体浓度及其与ICI疗效的直接量化关联，当前材料缺失核心实证数据。\\nHuman RCC patients (CheckMate 025 trial, nivolumab cohort) / Median Overall Survival: High inosine group 33 months vs. Low inosine group 22 months / Baseline plasma levels prior to or during ICB treatment：High plasma inosine: 33 months；Low plasma inosine: 22 months\\nMouse models (B16-F0, 4T1) and human RCC patients / Plasma inosine levels decreased after ICB treatment compared to baseline/pre-treatment states / During/after ICB therapy：Post-ICB (Mice & Humans): Reduced levels (qualitative)\\nGeneral physiological context (cited literature) / Concentration ranges: Blood plasma low micromolar; Necrotic/hypoxic TME hundreds of micromolar / General physiological conditions：Blood plasma: Low micromolar range；Necrotic/Hypoxic TME: Hundreds of micromolar range\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷（inosine）的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告内源性肌苷水平与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效之间的具体相关性统计。目前证据主要局限于以下层面：1. 临床队列关联：在肾细胞癌（RCC）患者中，较高的基线血浆肌苷水平与接受纳武利尤单抗治疗后的更长总生存期相关（中位 OS 33个月 vs 22个月），但这是血浆数据而非肿瘤组织/间质液数据，且未提供具体的浓度数值（如 μM 或 ng/mL）。2. 机制与药代动力学背景：肌苷可直接抑制肿瘤细胞内的泛素激活酶 UBA6，增强肿瘤免疫原性；其在血浆中的半衰期约为 15 小时，而腺苷降解极快。体外及小鼠模型显示，在葡萄糖受限条件下，效应 T 细胞可利用肌苷作为替代碳源支持增殖和功能，且在肿瘤细胞无法利用肌苷的模型中，外源性补充肌苷可增强 ICI 疗效。3. 方法学可行性：基质辅助激光解吸电离质谱成像（MALDI-MSI）和微透析技术已被证明可在人类非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）组织和患者来源异种移植（PDX）模型中检测肌苷等代谢物，但相关研究未结合 ICI 治疗结果进行定量关联分析。4. 干预性试验：一项 II 期临床试验显示，外源性补充肌苷联合 PD-1/PD-L1 抑制剂可延长晚期实体瘤患者的无进展生存期（HR 0.63），但这属于外源性干预效果，不能直接反映内源性 TME 肌苷浓度的自然变异及其与疗效的剂量-反应关系。综上，缺乏针对人体肿瘤局部（组织或间质液）肌苷浓度的直接定量测量及其与 ICI 响应（ORR/PFS/OS）的统计学关联数据。\\n\\n[[\\\"这项研究在 CheckMate 025 临床试验的肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列（n=394 接受 nivolumab 治疗）中分析了血浆代谢组数据，发现基线血浆肌苷水平较高与总生存期（OS）延长显著相关（高肌苷组中位 OS 33 个月 vs 低肌苷组 22 个月），证实了循环肌苷水平与 ICI 疗效的临床关联。\\\", \\\"研究在一个包含 22 名接受抗 PD-1 治疗的多癌种患者的小型队列中检测了肿瘤组织内的 UBA6 蛋白表达（作为肌苷作用的下游靶点），发现低 UBA6 表达与更高的客观缓解率（ORR 50% vs 17%）及 CD8+ T 细胞浸润相关。\\\", \\\"作者明确指出由于样本完整性问题（intact samples missing），未能在该人体肿瘤队列中直接检测或验证肌苷浓度，而是以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性的代理指标。\\\", \\\"研究揭示了肌苷增强 ICB 疗效的分子机制：肌苷直接进入肿瘤细胞，抑制泛素激活酶 UBA6，从而解除 UBA6 对炎症信号和抗原呈递通路的抑制，提高肿瘤免疫原性。\\\"], [\\\"该综述详细阐述了肌苷（inosine）作为肠道微生物代谢物调节抗肿瘤免疫的三大分子机制：(1) 特异性抑制肿瘤细胞内的泛素样修饰激活酶 6（UBA6）活性，提高肿瘤免疫原性；(2) 结合 T 淋巴细胞上的腺苷 A2A 受体，激活 cAMP-CREB 信号级联，促进 Th1 细胞分化及肿瘤浸润；(3) 在葡萄糖受限的肿瘤微环境（TME）中作为替代能源底物维持效应 T 细胞的生存和细胞毒性功能。\\\", \\\"文中指出肌苷由特定肠道菌群（如假长双歧杆菌 Bifidobacterium pseudolongum、约氏乳杆菌 Lactobacillus johnsonii 等）合成，并在免疫检查点阻断（ICB）治疗破坏肠道屏障完整性后易位至体循环，从而激活抗肿瘤 T 细胞。\\\", \\\"综述提及了临床转化潜力，指出在存在肌苷代谢缺陷的实体瘤中，外源性肌苷补充可能恢复免疫细胞代谢适应性，从而增强 ICI 疗效，这为理解肌苷浓度与疗效的关系提供了理论框架。\\\"]]\\n\\n[[\\\"研究在小鼠模型（B16-F0, 4T1 等）中证实了外源性肌苷补充（口服 400 mg/kg）可增强 ICI 疗效，并揭示了肌苷在血浆中的半衰期较长（约 15 小时），而腺苷极短，这影响了体内测量的稳定性。\\\", \\\"体外实验中使用了 100 μM 的肌苷浓度处理肿瘤细胞以观察 UBA6 抑制效果，但这并非人体内源性浓度的实测数据。\\\", \\\"研究指出肌苷来源具有多源性（肠道微生物、饮食、癌细胞分泌），且在不同肿瘤类型中效果可能依赖基础 UBA6 表达水平（如在低 UBA6 的 MC38 模型中无效）。\\\"], [\\\"综述提供了“肠道微生物群 - 代谢物 - 免疫轴”的整体概念框架，解释了代谢物如何作为分子信使从肠腔易位至体循环并调节全身及局部抗肿瘤免疫。\\\", \\\"文中还总结了其他核心代谢物（如短链脂肪酸、色氨酸代谢物、胆汁酸）调节免疫的具体机制及在不同肿瘤类型（如食管癌、胃癌、肝癌、结直肠癌、黑色素瘤、肾细胞癌）中的微生物特征签名，为理解肌苷在整体代谢网络中的位置提供了背景。\\\", \\\"讨论了针对微生物组的干预策略（如 FMT、益生菌、工程菌）在增强 ICI 疗效方面的转化潜力和当前面临的标准化、安全性及监管挑战。\\\"]]\",\"conditions\":[\"人体血浆中的肌苷浓度与ICB疗效的相关性\",\"CheckMate 025临床试验队列，基线血浆测量值\"],\"limits\":[\"需要寻找直接在人体肿瘤组织活检、间质液或微透析样本中测定肌苷绝对浓度（μM/ng/mL）的研究，并确认这些浓度数据是否与接受 ICI 治疗的患者的临床结局（如 ORR、PFS、OS）存在显著的相关性或因果联系。\"],\"still_missing\":\"该研究未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据（如 μM 或 ng/mL），也未报告 TME 内肌苷浓度与 ICI 疗效（如 ORR、PFS 或 OS）的直接定量统计关联。虽然提供了血浆肌苷水平与生存期的相关性以及肿瘤组织 UBA6 表达与缓解率的相关性，但作者明确承认由于样本缺失，未在人类肿瘤组织中直接测量肌苷浓度，因此核心的'TME 内肌苷具体浓度阈值’及‘组织层面浓度 - 疗效直接挂钩’的证据在此材料中缺失。\",\"allowed_use\":[\"background_context\",\"explicit_objectives\",\"explicit_method_summaries\",\"explicit_reported_findings\",\"explicit_leads\"],\"sources\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"title\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"title\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:220699268\",\"title\":\"Inosine is an alternative carbon source for CD8+ T cell function under glucose restriction\",\"year\":\"2020\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s42255-020-0219-4\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:220699268\",\"title\":\"Inosine is an alternative carbon source for CD8+ T cell function under glucose restriction\",\"year\":\"2020\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s42255-020-0219-4\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:280543786\",\"title\":\"The gut microbiota in cancer immunity and immunotherapy\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41423-025-01326-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"title\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:291235137\",\"title\":\"Non-nutritive sweeteners, the gut microbiome, and tumor immunity: evidence hierarchy and a sucralose-centered translational model\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fnut.2026.1868431\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0589\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286562058\",\"title\":\"Immunomodulatory effects of short-chain fatty acids and immune-supporting nutrients on slice cultures of head and neck tumors\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fnut.2026.1731077\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0596\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"7f1c43ec9ba638ccffb6291e9f21c1e1b48f6fc6\",\"title\":\"Multifaceted role of inosine in complex diseases and human health.\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1093/nutrit/nuae029\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0599\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0580\",\"paper_id\":\"c5e74d5eebf19335caebc97bdb8300261fcb0ee5\",\"title\":\"Targeting ribosomes reprograms the tumour microenvironment and augments cancer immunotherapy\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41416-025-03109-y\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0579\",\"paper_id\":\"1e76d13192f1c1a75fec92c6e6a2de5934fc6a1f\",\"title\":\"Characterisation of an autochthonous mouse ccRCC model of immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy resistance\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41598-025-04917-1\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0581\",\"paper_id\":\"5e59b9ca9a72cc8a626d875743ecc0ce1315af76\",\"title\":\"Artemin and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) efficacy in metastatic colorectal cancer (mCRC): A correlative analysis of the Canadian Cancer Trials Group (CCTG) CO.26 trial.\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1200/jco.2024.42.16_suppl.3587\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0639\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:259947308\",\"title\":\"Targeted quantitative metabolomics with a linear mixed-effect model for analysis of urinary nucleosides and deoxynucleosides from bladder cancer patients before and after tumor resection\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/s00216-023-04826-0\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0634\",\"paper_id\":\"680707c522895f780f927da2a5894def6930a602\",\"title\":\"Abstract 5175: DX-002, a dual EP2 and EP4 antagonist, alters the tumor microenvironment to enhance tumor immunogenicity and responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1538-7445.am2023-5175\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:280543786\",\"title\":\"The gut microbiota in cancer immunity and immunotherapy\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41423-025-01326-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0634\",\"paper_id\":\"680707c522895f780f927da2a5894def6930a602\",\"title\":\"Abstract 5175: DX-002, a dual EP2 and EP4 antagonist, alters the tumor microenvironment to enhance tumor immunogenicity and responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1538-7445.am2023-5175\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0609\",\"paper_id\":\"d69f29862a6e18da7c70e3c9d22cd4b7cabc18a3\",\"title\":\"Abstract B028: Multimodal approach to characterization of metabolism and immune modulation with insights from spatial metabolomics and transcriptomics\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1557-3265.targetedtherap-b028\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286562058\",\"title\":\"Immunomodulatory effects of short-chain fatty acids and immune-supporting nutrients on slice cultures of head and neck tumors\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fnut.2026.1731077\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0596\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0581\",\"paper_id\":\"5e59b9ca9a72cc8a626d875743ecc0ce1315af76\",\"title\":\"Artemin and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) efficacy in metastatic colorectal cancer (mCRC): A correlative analysis of the Canadian Cancer Trials Group (CCTG) CO.26 trial.\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1200/jco.2024.42.16_suppl.3587\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0639\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:259947308\",\"title\":\"Targeted quantitative metabolomics with a linear mixed-effect model for analysis of urinary nucleosides and deoxynucleosides from bladder cancer patients before and after tumor resection\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/s00216-023-04826-0\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0589\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:219269178\",\"title\":\"Abstract LB-317: Use ofin vivomicrodialysis to evaluate biomarker levels in the tumor and tumor free flank of freely-moving PDX mice\",\"year\":\"2019\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1538-7445.am2019-lb-317\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0589\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"paper_id\":\"OpenAlex:W7116840248\",\"title\":\"ADA1-Driven Metabolic Refueling Enhances CAR T Cell Therapy for Solid Tumors\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.3390/cancers18010034\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0609\",\"paper_id\":\"d69f29862a6e18da7c70e3c9d22cd4b7cabc18a3\",\"title\":\"Abstract B028: Multimodal approach to characterization of metabolism and immune modulation with insights from spatial metabolomics and transcriptomics\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1557-3265.targetedtherap-b028\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:272644866\",\"title\":\"Inosine enhances the efficacy of immune‐checkpoint inhibitors in advanced solid tumors: A randomized, controlled, Phase 2 study\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1002/cam4.70143\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0589\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:219269178\",\"title\":\"Abstract LB-317: Use ofin vivomicrodialysis to evaluate biomarker levels in the tumor and tumor free flank of freely-moving PDX mice\",\"year\":\"2019\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1538-7445.am2019-lb-317\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0589\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:280543786\",\"title\":\"The gut microbiota in cancer immunity and immunotherapy\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41423-025-01326-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"CorpusId:280543786\",\"identity_status\":\"unresolved_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286644045\",\"title\":\"Single-cell-based identification of drug synergy with immunotherapy via tumor microenvironment remodeling\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2025-014132\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"paper_id\":\"OpenAlex:W7116840248\",\"title\":\"ADA1-Driven Metabolic Refueling Enhances CAR T Cell Therapy for Solid Tumors\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.3390/cancers18010034\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0581\",\"paper_id\":\"5e59b9ca9a72cc8a626d875743ecc0ce1315af76\",\"title\":\"Artemin and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) efficacy in metastatic colorectal cancer (mCRC): A correlative analysis of the Canadian Cancer Trials Group (CCTG) CO.26 trial.\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1200/jco.2024.42.16_suppl.3587\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:272644866\",\"title\":\"Inosine enhances the efficacy of immune‐checkpoint inhibitors in advanced solid tumors: A randomized, controlled, Phase 2 study\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1002/cam4.70143\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:220699268\",\"title\":\"Inosine is an alternative carbon source for CD8+ T cell function under glucose restriction\",\"year\":\"2020\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s42255-020-0219-4\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0589\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:219269178\",\"title\":\"Abstract LB-317: Use ofin vivomicrodialysis to evaluate biomarker levels in the tumor and tumor free flank of freely-moving PDX mice\",\"year\":\"2019\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1538-7445.am2019-lb-317\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0589\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"paper_id\":\"OpenAlex:W7116840248\",\"title\":\"ADA1-Driven Metabolic Refueling Enhances CAR T Cell Therapy for Solid Tumors\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.3390/cancers18010034\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:291235137\",\"title\":\"Non-nutritive sweeteners, the gut microbiome, and tumor immunity: evidence hierarchy and a sucralose-centered translational model\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fnut.2026.1868431\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0589\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"canonical_paper_id\":\"OpenAlex:W4296038319\",\"title\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0586\",\"paper_id\":\"04c11cfcf5a3539fa2c39d0839134cb7fc2116bd\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"04c11cfcf5a3539fa2c39d0839134cb7fc2116bd\",\"title\":\"Dual-function engineered bacteria remodel AML tumor microenvironment via IL-12 delivery and adenosine depletion to sustain NK cell immunity\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1182/blood-2025-5912\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"paper_id\":\"OpenAlex:W7116840248\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"OpenAlex:W7116840248\",\"title\":\"ADA1-Driven Metabolic Refueling Enhances CAR T Cell Therapy for Solid Tumors\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.3390/cancers18010034\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"title\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:272644866\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:272644866\",\"title\":\"Inosine enhances the efficacy of immune‐checkpoint inhibitors in advanced solid tumors: A randomized, controlled, Phase 2 study\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1002/cam4.70143\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0591\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:291487342\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:291487342\",\"title\":\"Peripheral blood biomarkers in PD-1/PD-L1 immunotherapy: distinguishing predictive from prognostic biomarkers\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1924506\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"title\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0592\",\"paper_id\":\"3720efcbdc55365f98b0da676548b3d1debd5944\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"3720efcbdc55365f98b0da676548b3d1debd5944\",\"title\":\"Abstract B046: Sensitizing the PDAC tumor microenvironment to immune checkpoint therapies: characterization of a PDAC 3D model to decipher immune infiltration\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1538-7445.pancreatic24-b046\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286644045\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286644045\",\"title\":\"Single-cell-based identification of drug synergy with immunotherapy via tumor microenvironment remodeling\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2025-014132\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"title\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286927958\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286927958\",\"title\":\"Targeting the gut microbiota-metabolite-immune axis in cancer immunotherapy: mechanistic interplay, therapeutic strategies, and translational applications-a narrative review\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.21037/tcr-2025-1992\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0594\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"paper_id\":\"c3ad940c5555f03c559b2198cb68aace35fa7dba\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"c3ad940c5555f03c559b2198cb68aace35fa7dba\",\"title\":\"Abstract 2033: Rigosertib promotes anti-tumor activity of cancer cells via CETSA revealed novel targets and activates NLRP3-dependent inflammatory responses\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1538-7445.am2024-2033\",\"identity_status\":\"unresolved_identity\"}],\"provenance\":{\"downloads\":0,\"model_calls\":1,\"source\":\"judge+focused_local_read\",\"whole_paper_rereads\":0},\"chapter_ids\":[\"Ch3\"],\"unit_key\":\"\"}},{\"tool_id\":\"tool::3226b0ef32058559fa3b1311ab735d320362e55a1cbe382a2f46fa8ea75d2c56\",\"value\":{\"need_id\":\"N76e5cbf6bca57e729afb-df9b777a93e759ce\",\"question\":\"人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷（inosine）的生理浓度及其与 ICI 疗效的具体相关性数据是什么？\",\"intended_use\":\"mechanism\",\"decision\":\"external_research\",\"usable_content\":\"现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告其与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效的具体统计关联。P0582 研究在人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者队列中仅检测了血浆中的肌苷水平，发现高基线血浆肌苷与尼莫鲁单抗治疗后的较长总生存期相关（中位 OS 33个月 vs. 22个月），但明确说明由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以 UBA6 表达作为通路活性的代理指标；该研究还指出肌苷在血浆中半衰期较长（约15小时），但未提供具体的血浆或组织浓度数值。P0588 研究主要关注体外 T 细胞代谢及小鼠模型，虽提及血液血浆中肌苷浓度为低微摩尔范围、坏死/缺氧微环境中可积累至数百微摩尔，但这些是引用外部文献的一般性陈述，并非本研究中对人类患者的实测数据，且明确指出缺乏人类临床相关性数据。P0587 综述同样未提取具体浓度值，仅引用其他研究关于粪便短链脂肪酸或精氨酸的数据示例。因此，当前材料无法回答人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷的具体浓度及其与 ICI 疗效的相关性问题。\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷（inosine）的绝对生理浓度数据，也未见其与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效（如ORR、PFS或OS）的具体统计关联结果。多项研究指出这是当前文献中的关键缺失环节：尽管有临床观察显示接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的肾细胞癌患者血浆中肌苷水平较高与总生存期延长相关（中位OS 33个月 vs 22个月），但研究者承认由于样本完整性问题，未能在其22人的临床队列中直接测量肌苷，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的替代指标；另有综述和机制研究引用外部文献提及坏死或缺氧微环境中肌苷可能积累至数百微摩尔（hundreds of micromolar），但这并非针对接受ICI治疗的人类患者的实测数据。此外，虽然有小鼠模型证实口服肌苷可增强ICB疗效，且体外实验显示T细胞可利用肌苷作为碳源，但这些前临床数据无法直接外推为人体内的具体浓度阈值或疗效相关性。目前缺乏将人源肿瘤组织或间质液中的肌苷定量值与ICI响应直接挂钩的证据。\\n\\n[\\\"这项研究在人体数据方面提供了两方面的关键证据：首先，通过分析 CheckMate 025 临床试验中肾细胞癌（RCC）患者的血浆代谢组数据（n=394 接受 nivolumab 治疗），发现血浆肌苷水平高低与总生存期（OS）显著相关（高肌苷组中位 OS 33 个月 vs 低肌苷组 22 个月），证实了循环肌苷水平与 ICI 疗效的临床关联。其次，在一个包含 22 名接受抗 PD-1 治疗的多癌种患者的小型队列中，作者检测了肿瘤组织内的 UBA6 蛋白表达（作为肌苷作用的下游靶点），发现低 UBA6 表达与更高的客观缓解率（ORR 50% vs 17%）及 CD8+ T 细胞浸润相关。然而，作者明确指出由于样本缺失，未能在该人体肿瘤队列中直接检测肌苷浓度。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"研究在小鼠模型（B16-F0, 4T1 等）中证实了外源性肌苷补充可增强 ICI 疗效，并揭示了分子机制：肌苷直接进入肿瘤细胞，抑制泛素激活酶 UBA6，从而解除 UBA6 对炎症信号和抗原呈递通路的抑制，提高肿瘤免疫原性。研究还指出肌苷在血浆中的半衰期较长（约 15 小时），而腺苷极短，这影响了体内测量的稳定性。此外，研究提到肌苷来源具有多源性（肠道微生物、饮食、癌细胞分泌），且在不同肿瘤类型中效果可能依赖基础 UBA6 表达水平（如在低 UBA6 的 MC38 模型中无效）。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告其与ICI疗效在组织层面的直接定量关联。P0582研究仅提供了人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者血浆中的肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）的相关性：在高肌苷组中，接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的患者中位OS为33个月，而低肌苷组为22个月。该研究明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的代理指标。P0588研究虽然指出文献报道肌苷在血浆中为低微摩尔范围，而在坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔，但这属于引用外部文献的理论背景，并非本研究对ICI响应患者的实测数据，且该研究主要关注T细胞代谢机制而非临床浓度-疗效关联。P0587综述同样未提取具体的肌苷浓度数值。因此，关于“人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷的生理浓度及其与ICI疗效的具体相关性数据”这一具体问题，当前材料缺失核心的绝对浓度测量值及对应的组织层面统计关联。\\nHuman RCC patients (CheckMate 025 trial, nivolumab-treated cohort) / Median Overall Survival: High inosine group 33 months vs. Low inosine group 22 months / Baseline plasma levels measured prior to or at start of treatment; survival follow-up：High plasma inosine: 33 months；Low plasma inosine: 22 months\\nMouse models (B16-F0, 4T1, etc.) and Human T cells (in vitro) / General concentration ranges cited from external literature (not measured in this study's human samples): Plasma low micromolar range; TME hundreds of micromolar range / Theoretical/External citation context for physiological relevance：Plasma (cited): low micromolar；TME (cited): hundreds of micromolar\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度及其与免疫检查点阻断（ICI）疗效的具体相关性数据。多项研究明确指出，目前文献中缺乏将肌苷等代谢物在粪便、血液、肿瘤组织及间质液中的配对定量测量与临床结局关联的证据。具体而言：P0582 报告了肾细胞癌患者血浆中肌苷水平与生存期的关联（高肌苷组中位总生存期33个月 vs 低肌苷组22个月），但明确说明未在人肿瘤样本中验证或测量肌苷浓度，仅以UBA6表达作为通路活性代理指标；P0588 指出虽然理论推测坏死/缺氧微环境中肌苷可达数百微摩尔，但该研究本身未在人类患者中测量TME内的肌苷浓度，且其引用的数值为外部文献的一般性陈述而非本研究数据；P0587 和 P0589 均强调，尽管有微生物产生肌苷增强小鼠ICI疗效的机制证据，但缺乏人体肿瘤组织或间质液中肌苷浓度的直接定量数据，且现有的SCFA数据多局限于粪便样本，未链接至TME浓度或ICI结果。因此，关于人体TME内肌苷的具体浓度阈值及其对ORR/PFS/OS的统计关联，当前材料显示为未满足的研究空白。\\n\\n[\\\"该研究确认了腺苷脱氨酶（ADA）将腺苷（Ado）转化为肌苷（Ino）的酶动力学参数（Km=0.05, Vmax=53µmol/min），并在体外实验中证实了腺苷暴露会抑制免疫细胞杀伤力，而转化为肌苷可恢复免疫功能。研究提及使用 LC-MS 评估 ADA 动力学和活性，表明肌苷及相关代谢物在实验体系中是可测量的。这为肌苷在肿瘤微环境中具有免疫刺激作用而非抑制作用提供了机制性证据，支持了微环境代谢重编程可能影响免疫治疗效果的假设。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"研究对象为工程化非致病性大肠杆菌（E. coli K12 DH5α），通过表面展示 IL-12 和 ADA 融合蛋白发挥作用。体内实验主要在免疫 competent 的 B16-F10 黑色素瘤小鼠模型和 WEHI-3 AML 小鼠模型中进行，观察到细菌在骨髓和肿瘤部位的聚集。免疫效应主要评估了 NK 细胞的活化标志物（CD25, NKp30）及细胞因子（IFNγ, TNFα），未直接报告 T 细胞检查点抑制剂（ICI）的使用或响应数据。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据，也未报告其与ICI疗效在组织层面的直接定量关联。P0582研究仅提供了人类肾细胞癌（RCC）患者血浆中的肌苷水平与总生存期（OS）的相关性：在高肌苷组中，接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的患者中位OS为33个月，而低肌苷组为22个月。该研究明确指出由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的代理指标。P0588研究虽然指出文献报道肌苷在血浆中为低微摩尔范围，而在坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔，但这属于引用外部文献的理论背景，并非本研究对ICI响应患者的实测数据，且该研究主要关注T细胞代谢机制而非临床浓度-疗效关联。P0587综述同样未提取具体的肌苷浓度数值。因此，关于“人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷的生理浓度及其与ICI疗效的具体相关性数据”这一具体问题，当前材料缺失核心的绝对浓度测量值及对应的组织层面统计关联。\\nHuman RCC patients (CheckMate 025 trial, nivolumab-treated cohort) / Median Overall Survival: High inosine group 33 months vs. Low inosine group 22 months / Baseline plasma levels measured prior to or at start of treatment; survival follow-up：High plasma inosine: 33 months；Low plasma inosine: 22 months\\nMouse models (B16-F0, 4T1, etc.) and Human T cells (in vitro) / General concentration ranges cited from external literature (not measured in this study's human samples): Plasma low micromolar range; TME hundreds of micromolar range / Theoretical/External citation context for physiological relevance：Plasma (cited): low micromolar；TME (cited): hundreds of micromolar\\n\\n现有材料未能提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数据。研究P0582仅报告了人体血浆（血清）中肌苷水平与免疫检查点阻断（ICB）疗效的关联：在肾细胞癌（RCC）患者中，基线血浆肌苷水平较高者接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的中位总生存期为33个月，显著高于低水平组的22个月。该研究明确指出，由于样本完整性问题，未在其临床队列中直接验证或测量肌苷浓度，而是以UBA6表达作为通路活性的替代指标。此外，P0582提到腺苷降解为肌苷的半衰期差异（约15小时），暗示了检测策略的挑战，但未给出具体的人体组织浓度数值。其他材料如P0588和P0596主要基于小鼠模型或体外实验，其中P0588引用文献指出肌苷在坏死/缺氧微环境中可达数百微摩尔，但这并非本研究在人体中的实测数据；P0596提供了体外培养中使用的短链脂肪酸浓度，而非人体内源性肌苷浓度。P0639虽然建立了尿液中肌苷的定量方法并报告了膀胱癌患者术前术后尿液浓度的变化（术后24小时升高约1.7倍），但尿液浓度不能直接等同于肿瘤微环境或血清中的浓度。因此，目前缺乏将人体肿瘤组织或间质液中肌苷的具体绝对浓度（μM或ng/mL）与ICI响应（ORR/PFS/OS）直接挂钩的实证数据。\\n人体血浆中的肌苷浓度与ICB疗效的相关性 / 接受纳武利尤单抗治疗的RCC患者的总生存期（OS） / CheckMate 025临床试验队列，基线血浆测量值：P0582_High_Inosine: 33 months (median OS)；P0582_Low_Inosine: 22 months (median OS)\\n\\n[[\\\"Mechanism description: ADA1 enzyme converts immunosuppressive adenosine to inosine, which can serve as an alternative carbon source for T cells.\\\", \\\"General TME metabolite context: Extracellular adenosine concentrations in tumors can reach 100–200 μM, significantly higher than in healthy tissue.\\\", \\\"Metabolic rationale: Inosine supplementation or generation supports T cell metabolism (glycolytic and pentose phosphate pathways) under glucose restriction.\\\", \\\"Preclinical evidence: ADA1-expressing CAR T cells show reduced exhaustion and improved persistence in mouse models, linked to inosine availability.\\\", \\\"Combination concept: The authors discuss potential integration of metabolic reprogramming (like ADA1) with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) as a future strategy.\\\"]]\\n\\n[[\\\"Description of the CD39/CD73 axis responsible for adenosine generation in the tumor microenvironment.\\\", \\\"Details on T cell metabolic states (naïve, effector, memory, exhausted) and their vulnerability to adenosine.\\\", \\\"Engineering strategies for localizing ADA1 on T cell surfaces (e.g., via CD26 or scFv).\\\", \\\"Safety considerations regarding metabolic engineering, including risks of fueling tumor cells with inosine.\\\", \\\"Statement that no clinical trials of ADA1/CAR T cells in humans have been conducted to date.\\\"]]\",\"conditions\":[\"人体血浆中的肌苷浓度与ICB疗效的相关性\",\"CheckMate 025临床试验队列，基线血浆测量值\"],\"limits\":[\"需要找到直接在人体肿瘤组织活检、间质液或微透析液中测量肌苷绝对浓度，并将其与ICI治疗响应（如ORR、PFS、OS）进行统计关联的研究。目前的证据仅限于血浆水平的间接关联或动物模型/体外实验。\"],\"still_missing\":\"人体肿瘤微环境内肌苷（inosine）的生理浓度及其与 ICI 疗效的具体相关性数据是什么？\",\"allowed_use\":[\"background_context\",\"explicit_objectives\",\"explicit_method_summaries\",\"explicit_reported_findings\",\"explicit_leads\"],\"sources\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"title\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"title\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:220699268\",\"title\":\"Inosine is an alternative carbon source for CD8+ T cell function under glucose restriction\",\"year\":\"2020\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s42255-020-0219-4\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:220699268\",\"title\":\"Inosine is an alternative carbon source for CD8+ T cell function under glucose restriction\",\"year\":\"2020\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s42255-020-0219-4\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0588\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:280543786\",\"title\":\"The gut microbiota in cancer immunity and immunotherapy\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41423-025-01326-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0582\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:252309032\",\"title\":\"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine augments tumour immunogenicity and responses\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41467-022-33116-z\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:291235137\",\"title\":\"Non-nutritive sweeteners, the gut microbiome, and tumor immunity: evidence hierarchy and a sucralose-centered translational model\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fnut.2026.1868431\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0589\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286562058\",\"title\":\"Immunomodulatory effects of short-chain fatty acids and immune-supporting nutrients on slice cultures of head and neck tumors\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fnut.2026.1731077\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0596\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"7f1c43ec9ba638ccffb6291e9f21c1e1b48f6fc6\",\"title\":\"Multifaceted role of inosine in complex diseases and human health.\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1093/nutrit/nuae029\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0599\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0580\",\"paper_id\":\"c5e74d5eebf19335caebc97bdb8300261fcb0ee5\",\"title\":\"Targeting ribosomes reprograms the tumour microenvironment and augments cancer immunotherapy\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41416-025-03109-y\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0579\",\"paper_id\":\"1e76d13192f1c1a75fec92c6e6a2de5934fc6a1f\",\"title\":\"Characterisation of an autochthonous mouse ccRCC model of immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy resistance\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41598-025-04917-1\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0581\",\"paper_id\":\"5e59b9ca9a72cc8a626d875743ecc0ce1315af76\",\"title\":\"Artemin and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) efficacy in metastatic colorectal cancer (mCRC): A correlative analysis of the Canadian Cancer Trials Group (CCTG) CO.26 trial.\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1200/jco.2024.42.16_suppl.3587\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0639\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:259947308\",\"title\":\"Targeted quantitative metabolomics with a linear mixed-effect model for analysis of urinary nucleosides and deoxynucleosides from bladder cancer patients before and after tumor resection\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/s00216-023-04826-0\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0634\",\"paper_id\":\"680707c522895f780f927da2a5894def6930a602\",\"title\":\"Abstract 5175: DX-002, a dual EP2 and EP4 antagonist, alters the tumor microenvironment to enhance tumor immunogenicity and responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1538-7445.am2023-5175\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:280543786\",\"title\":\"The gut microbiota in cancer immunity and immunotherapy\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41423-025-01326-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0587\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0634\",\"paper_id\":\"680707c522895f780f927da2a5894def6930a602\",\"title\":\"Abstract 5175: DX-002, a dual EP2 and EP4 antagonist, alters the tumor microenvironment to enhance tumor immunogenicity and responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1538-7445.am2023-5175\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0609\",\"paper_id\":\"d69f29862a6e18da7c70e3c9d22cd4b7cabc18a3\",\"title\":\"Abstract B028: Multimodal approach to characterization of metabolism and immune modulation with insights from spatial metabolomics and transcriptomics\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1557-3265.targetedtherap-b028\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286562058\",\"title\":\"Immunomodulatory effects of short-chain fatty acids and immune-supporting nutrients on slice cultures of head and neck tumors\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fnut.2026.1731077\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0596\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0581\",\"paper_id\":\"5e59b9ca9a72cc8a626d875743ecc0ce1315af76\",\"title\":\"Artemin and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) efficacy in metastatic colorectal cancer (mCRC): A correlative analysis of the Canadian Cancer Trials Group (CCTG) CO.26 trial.\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1200/jco.2024.42.16_suppl.3587\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0639\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:259947308\",\"title\":\"Targeted quantitative metabolomics with a linear mixed-effect model for analysis of urinary nucleosid